1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selbach_mac_Ferchair
2 CONT
2 CONT Coronation:	King of Argyll
2 CONT
2 CONT Selbach mac Ferchair was a son of Ferchar Fota. He ruled as king of the Cenél Loairn from around 698 until his abdication in 723, but it may be that he was undisputed ruler of Dál Riata only in the final years of his reign.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ainbcellach_mac_Ferchair
2 CONT
2 CONT Ainbcellach mac Ferchair was king of the Cenél Loairn of Dál Riata, and perhaps of all Dál Riata, from 697 until 698, when he was deposed and exiled to Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a son of Ferchar Fota. He is given the epithet the Good in the Duan Albanach, a praise poem from the 11th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is unclear how long he remained in exile. There are reports of fighting in Dál Riata in the early 8th century which might be a conflict between Ainbcellach and his brother, Selbach mac Ferchair, or between the Cenél Loairn and 
2 CONC the Cenél nGabráin for control of Dál Riata. Ainbcellach had certainly returned by September 719, when he was killed fighting against Selbach in "Finnglen" (perhaps near Loch Fyne).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ainbcellach's son Muiredach was later king of the Cenél Loairn. The later Mormaers of Moray traced their descent to Ainbcellach and the Cenél Loairn through Ainbcellach's son Ruadrí.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedigrees of the Scottish Clans -From Irish and Scottish Ms.-http://clanmaclochlainn.com/pedigree.htm
