2 CONT
2 CONT Fergus established the Irish kingdon of Dalraida in what is now Argyle, Scotland. He is thought
2 CONT
2 CONT to have ruled for about three years in succession to his brother Loarn.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT History knows little of the Scots earlier then about 500AD, but at this point, the name of Fergus MorMacErc,(Fergus, son of Erc) emerges from the mists of legend as the King of the Scots in Dalriada. Dalriada was one of the four s
2 CONC eparate kingdoms in Scotland. Strathclyde was inhabited by Britons, Northumbria by the Angles and The Kingdom of the Picts.He acceded to the Throne about 490AD and was killed in 501.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 300?? a.d., in Crinan, Scotland, took rock fortress of Dunadd near Crinan.
2 CONT
2 CONT established Irish kingdom of Dalriada in Argyle
