2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Excerpts from the ''Annals of the Four Masters''''' [https://celt.ucc.ie/published/T100005A/index.html] 
2 CONT Click CELT editions as a single file, then then enter year + decimal, the into browser search.
2 CONT '''735.7''' – Forbasach, son of Ailell, Lord of Osraighe Ossory, was slain.
2 CONT '''741.10''' – The battle of Rath Cuile, by Anmchadh, in which Uargus, son of Fachtna, was slain.
2 CONT '''742.16''' – A battle was fought by Anmchadh, in which Cairbre, Fearghus, and Caicher, sons of Cumascrach, were slain, and sixteen chieftains along with them.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Excerpts from the ''Annals of Tigernach''''' [https://celt.ucc.ie/published/T100002A/index.html] 
2 CONT ''Click CELT editions as a single file'', then enter year + decimal, the into browser search.
2 CONT '''735.3''' – The battle of Belach Éle between Munster and Leinster where many Leinstermen and an almost countless number of Munstermen perished, wherein Cellach son of Faelchar king of Ossory fell and two sons of Cormac Rossa kin
2 CONC g of the Déise. Cathal son of Findguine, king of Munster, escaped.
2 CONT '''742.2''' – The smiting of the Cenél Fiachach and the Delbna by Ossory.
2 CONT '''750.10''' – The combat of Inishnag, gained by Anmchadh son of Cú Cerca.
2 CONT '''754.6''' – Devastation of the Fothart Fea by the Ossorians.
2 CONT '''759.6''' – The Battle of Gowran gained by Anmchad over Leinster.
2 CONT '''761.2''' – Battle of Áth duma between the Ulaid and the Uí Echach, in which fell Ailill son of Fedlimid.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Excerpts from the ''''Annals of Ulster'''' AD 431–1201''' [https://celt.ucc.ie/published/T100001A.html] 
2 CONT Enter2 the number(s), or year + decimal, into browser search.
2 CONT '''735.3''' – “A battle between Mumu and Laigin, in which many of the Laigin and well-nigh countless Munstermen perished; Cellach son of Faelchar, king of Osraige, fell therein, but Cathal son of Finnguine, king of Mumu, escaped.”
2 CONT '''742.2''' – “The devastation of Cenél Fiachach and of Delbna by the Osraige.”
2 CONT '''761.3''' – “The battle of Belat Gabráin in which Donngal son of Laidcnén, king of Uí Ceinnselaig, and other kings fell.”
2 CONT '''754.6''' – “Destruction of the Fotharta Fea by the Osraige.”
2 CONT '''769.1''' – “An overthrow in a battle between the Osraige themselves, in which the sons of Cellach, son of Faelchar, were put to flight. Tóim Snáma emerged victorious.”
2 CONT '''770.2''' – “Tóim Snáma son of Flann king of Osraige was killed.”
2 CONT '''802.4''' – “Fergal son of Anmchad, king of Osraige, dies.”
2 CONT
