1 NOTE Columba of Donegal, b. 543, son of Fedhlim of Donegal, became the famous Irish Missonary known as 'Apostle of Caledonia'; held sway over Columban churches in Ireland and north of England and Scotland; largely independent of papal 
2 CONC supervision.
2 CONT
