2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiachnae_mac_Demm%C3%A1in
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT Fiachnae mac Demmáin (died 627) was King of Ulaid from 626 to 627. He sometimes was called Fiachnae Dubtuinne. He was a member of the Dal Fiatach and nephew of Baetan mac Cairill (died 581) of Ulaid. He was the son of Demmán mac C
2 CONC airell (died 572).[1] He succeeded his uncle as king of the Dal Fiatach in 581.
2 CONT
2 CONT His first mention in the Irish annals is the battle of Cúl Caíl (possibly Kilkeel, modern County Down) in 601 where he was defeated by Fiachnae mac Baetain of the Dal nAraide.[2] The annals mention Fiachnae mac Baetan went against
2 CONC  him so was probably the aggressor. This was part of the struggle of these two rival clans for the overlordship of Ulaid. In 626 was fought the Battle of Leithit Midind at Drung (Knocklayd, modern County Antrim) between these two 
2 CONC rivals at which Fiachnae mac Demmáin was the victor and Fiachnae mac Baetan was slain.[3] The annals say the battle was fought by him which implies he was the aggressor.
2 CONT
2 CONT He now becomes King of Ulaid but was himself defeated and slain by the King of Dalriada, Connad Cerr at the Battle of Ard Corainn in 627.[4] The Annals of Clonmacnoise claim that this was in revenge for the slaying of Fiachnae mac
2 CONC  Baetan.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wives were:[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Cumne Dub''', daughter of Furudrán mac Béicce of the Uí Tuirtri.She was the mother of Dúnchad mac Fiachnai (died circa 644),a king of Ulaid and of a daughter Dub Lacha who married Mongán mac Fiachnai (died 625), the son of his 
2 CONC rival Fiachnae mac Baetan.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Cumne(Cummíne) Find''', daughter of Báetán Cáech of DalnAraide and sister of Fiachnae mac Baetan. She was the mother of Máel Cobo mac Fiachnae (died 647), a king of Ulaid and a son named Suibne.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was ancestor of all later Dal Fiatach kings.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT  Byrne, Table 6; Charles-Edwards, appendix XXI; Mac Niocaill, p. 155
2 CONT  Annals of Ulster AU 601.3, 602.3; Annals of Tigernach AT 600.3; Mac Niocaill, pg.88
2 CONT  Annals of Ulster AU 626.1; Annals of Tigernach AT 627.1; Mac Niocaill, pg.88; Byrne,pg.111; Ó Cróinín pg.218
2 CONT  Annals of Ulster AU 627.1; Annals of Tigernach AT 628.1; Mac Niocaill, pg.88; Byrne, pg.111; Ó Cróinín, pg.218
2 CONT  Mac Niocaill, pg.88-89
2 CONT
