1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Conall Cremthainne (died 480), also called Conall Err Breg, was an Irish king. He was the son of Niall of the Nine Hostages, and one of the progenitors of the Uí Néill dynasty.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He is the first king of Uisnech in Mide from the Ui Neill mentioned in the Book of Leinster king list.[2] His by-name Cremthainne implies fosterage among the Uí Cremthainn of the Airgialla.[3] He was probably originally the same p
2 CONC erson as Conall Gulban, the distinction arising from 8th century politics.[4]According to a life of Saint Patrick by Tírechán, Patrick blessed Conall and rejected his brother Coirpre mac Néill, ancestor of the Cenél Coirpri, at a 
2 CONC meeting at Tailtiu.[5] Nothing is recorded of him in the annals other than his death date.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Through his son Fergus Cerrbél, he was the ancestor of the Clann Cholmáin and Síl nÁedo Sláine. Another son was Ardgal mac Conaill (died 520) was ancestor of the Cenél nArdgail in Co.Meath
