2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Ambcellach is listed among the early ancestral figures associated with the lineage of Clan MacLaren in Scotland. Genealogical records, such as those found on RootsWeb, place an Ambcellach in a list of early names (circa 800-950) a
2 CONC ssociated with the progenitors of the clan, often listed alongside names like Dougall and Finlaech. 
2 CONT Wikipedia
2 CONT Wikipedia
2 CONT  +1
2 CONT Context: He is part of the traditional, early, and sometimes legendary genealogy of the Clan MacLaren, rather than a well-documented historical figure of the modern era.
2 CONT Significance: While often listed in historical overviews of the clan's lineage, specific details of Ambcellach's life or "great" deeds are not detailed in general records, which focus more on the later, established chiefs.
2 CONT Clan Background: Clan MacLaren's ancient rallying point is Creag an Tuirc (the Boar's Rock) in Balquhidde
