2 CONT
2 CONT >>>(a)       [https://www.geni.com/people/Tuathal-mac-Augaire-King-of-Leinster/6000000003495402182 TUATHAL] (-958).  The Annals of the Four Masters record “a victory…over the people of Laighis and the Ui-Faircheallain by Tuathal s
2 CONC on of Ugaire” in 950[633].  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 958 of "Tuathal son of Augaire king of Laigin”[634].  m ---.  The name of Tuathal´s wife is not known.  Tuathal & his wife had three child
2 CONC ren: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Donnchadh/6000000079503993016?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529787471684&through=6000000079503993016 DONNCHAD] (-964).  The Annals of the Four Masters records the death in 964 of “Donnchadh 
2 CONC son of Tuathal royal heir of Leinster”[637]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>2.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Augaire-O-Muiredaig/6000000006290757923?through=6000000003495402182  UGAIRE] (-killed in battle Bithland [976/77]).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Ugaire, son o
2 CONC f Tuathal, king of Leinster” was captured in [974/75] by “the Foreigners of Dublin”[638].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Ugaire, son of Tuathal, king of Leinster” was killed in [976/77] at “the Battle of Bithland”[639].  m 
2 CONC ---.  The name of Ugaire´s wife is not known.  Ugaire & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>a)         TUATHAL (-killed in battle Clontarf 23 Apr 1014).  The Annals of the Four Masters record that “Tuathal son of Ugaire, royal heir of Leinster” was killed in 1013 in the battle [of Clontarf][640]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>3.         [https://www.geni.com/people/D%C3%BAnlang-II-mac-Tuathail-King-of-Leinster/6000000002043263901?through=6000000003495402182 DUNLANG] (-1013).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of the Four Masters record the death in 101
2 CONC 3 of “Dunlang son of Tuathal king of Leinster”[641].  m ---.  The name of Dunlang´s wife is not known.  Dunlang & his wife had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>a)         GILLA COEMGIN (-killed [1017/18]).  Crown Prince of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Gilla Coemgin son of Dunlang crownprince of Leinster” was killed in [1017/18] “by the Leinstermen”[642]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>b)         DONNCUAN “the Simpleton” (-killed 1015).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of the Four Masters record that “Donncuan i.e. the Simpleton son of Dunlaing lord of Leinster and Tadhg Ua Riain lord of Ui-Drona” were killed
2 CONC  in 1015 by “Donnchadh son of Gillaphadraig at Leithghlinn”[643]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>c)         UGAIRE (-killed Dubloch [1022/24]).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Ugaire son of Dunlang king of Leinster” defeated “Sitric son of Olaf with the Foreigners of Dublin at Dergnae mo Goróc (D
2 CONC elgany)” in 1021[644].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Augaire son of Dunlang king of Leinster” was killed “at Dubloch, by Donn slébe” in [1022/24][645]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>d)         DONNCHAD (-killed [1036/37]).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Donnchad, son of Dunlang, king of Leinster” was blinded by “Donnchad Mac Gilla Pátraic” in 1036 and died[646].  The Annals of I
2 CONC nisfallen record the death in 1037 of "Dúnlang´s king of Laigin by the Osraige”[647]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>i)          DOMNALL (-1039).  Crown Prince of Leinster.  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 1039 of "Domnall son of Donnchad royal heir of Laigin”[648].  The Annals of Tigernach record the death in 1039 of “Domnall
2 CONC  son of Donnchad king of the Húi Faeláin…slain by Domnall Húa Fergail king of the Forths”[649]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>e)         MURCHAD (-killed in battle Mag Muilchet 1042).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Murchad son of Dunlang king of Leinster” was killed by “Gilla Pátraic son of Donnchad king of Ossory and by Ma
2 CONC c Craith Húa Donnchada king of the Eoganacht ´load-of-plunder´ on Mag Muilchet in Leix” in 1042[650]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>f)          MAILCORCRE .  The 13th century History of Gruffydd ap Cynan records that the "grandmother...his mother´s mother" of King Gruffydd was "Mailcorcre daughter of Dunlang son of Tuathal King of Leinster"[651].  m OLAF 
2 CONC of Dublin, son of SIHTRIC King of Dublin & his wife --- ([after 1013]-murdered 1034). 
2 CONT
