1 OCCU 126th HIgh KIng of Ireland, Greatest High King of Ireland, aka Nial Mor NAOIGHIALLACH `of the Nine Hostages'; 1st King (but reckoned 126th MONARCH) of IRELAND; conquered nine countries (incl. part of France), King of Ireland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Niall Noígiallach mac Echdach (c. 361 – 452), universally known as Niall of the Nine Hostages, was a legendary and foundational King of Connacht and ancestral Overking of Tara. As the towering progenitor of the Uí 
2 CONC Néill dynasties, his reign marked a violent, transitional epoch where Gaelic tribal coalitions aggressively expanded across Ireland and launched devastating transmarine slaving raids against a collapsing Roman Britain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Eochaid Mugmedón, Overking of the Midlands and Tara.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Cairenn Chasdub, a captive Saxon princess forced into concubinage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wives: 
2 CONT
2 CONT #Inne ingen Lugaid 
2 CONT
2 CONT #Mongfind ingen Fidach (a powerful Munster princess who fiercely contested Niall's succession).
2 CONT
2 CONT Niall’s famous title Noígiallach (meaning "of the Nine Hostages") directly reflects the brutal extortion methods required to hold power in the 5th century. To secure absolute submission and tribute from rival kingdoms, Niall exact
2 CONC ed human collateral. According to early records, he bound nine high-ranking noble hostages in chains as legal guarantees of submission: one from each of the five provinces of Ireland (Munster, Leinster, Connacht, Ulster, and Meath
2 CONC ), and four from foreign maritime adversaries (the Britons, the Picts, the Saxons, and the Scots). In the metaphysical worldview of the Gaels, the physical holding of these noble captives solidified a king's cosmic righteousness a
2 CONC nd prevented rebellion.
2 CONT
2 CONT Transmarine Slaving Raids and Saint PatrickOperating during the final decay of Roman authority in Britain, Niall deployed his fleets across the Irish Sea to plunder vulnerable Romano-British coastal settlements. These expeditions 
2 CONC were aggressive economic ventures designed to extract silver, livestock, and human cattle. During one of these massive maritime incursions along the western coast of Britain, Niall's raiding parties captured a 16-year-old youth na
2 CONC med Succat—the son of a Romano-British merchant. This captive was brought back to Ireland in heavy chains and enslaved as a swineherd, later escaping to become Saint Patrick, the patron saint of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Assassination and Death Omens. Niall's aggressive expansion sparked a bitter, multigenerational blood feud with the Kingdom of Leinster. According to the historical saga Orcuin Néill Nóigíallaig (The Slaying of Niall), his exp
2 CONC ansive career was cut short during a naval expedition across the English Channel (Muir nIcht). Niall was ambushed and assassinated by Eochaid mac Énnai, an exiled Prince of Leinster who shot the Overking with a poisoned arrow from
2 CONC  a hidden vantage point. His unexpected death triggered immediate political fragmentation, and his body was carried back by his warriors to be buried at Ochann (Faughan Hill, County Meath), leaving behind a fractured, heavily arme
2 CONC d network of sons who conquered Ulster.
2 CONT
2 CONT Known Lineage and DescendantsNiall's highly prolific lineage reshaped the genetics and politics of northwestern Europe for over six centuries. His primary sons founded the Northern and Southern Uí Néill branches:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Eoghan mac Néill (d. 465) – Founder of the Cenél nÉogain dynasty and direct ancestor of the O'Neill lines.#
2 CONT #Conall Gulban (d. 464) – Founder of the Cenél Conaill dynasty.
2 CONT #Lóegaire mac Néill (d. 462) – Overking of Tara who confronted Saint Patrick.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Within the official traditions of Clan MacNeil, Niall represents the 1st Ancestral Chief and the supreme genealogical root of the entire clan. While his historical title was King of Connacht and ruler of Tara rather than a Scottis
2 CONC h clan chief, he serves as the foundation of the traditional patrilineal lineage connecting the modern clan to the royal, prehistoric dynasties of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT I believe you may be interested in the first fully illustrated children's book about Niall of the Nine Hostages. I welcome your input, feedback and support: https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1195848313/niall-and-the-stone-of-de
2 CONC stiny/updates
2 CONT
2 CONT Sincerely,
2 CONT
2 CONT Lance McNeill
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT There are arguments to be made for Niall as an historical figure, but the father assigned to him in the genealogies comes from a long line of legendary kings; his profile can be found here: https://www.geni.com/people/Eochaid-mac-
2 CONC Muiredach-Lebor-Gab%C3%A1la-%C3%89renn/6000000002135571499
2 CONT
2 CONT DNA news -- an estimate of about 3 million men that carry DNA descended from Niall (of his equivalent): http://www.irish-genealogy-toolkit.com/niall-of-the-nine-hostages.html
2 CONT
2 CONT DNA (M-L21)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT #http://www.friesian.com/perifran.htm#england 
2 CONT
2 CONT #http://fabpedigree.com/s048/f753876.htm
2 CONT
