1 NOTE {geni:about_me} As shown below, the article in BLGS2001 on 'Macnab of Macnab' identifies many of this line as ancestor of various Scots clans. We intend, in due course, to investigate each of these claims and see how they coincide
2 CONC  with other sources. Early indications suggest that they do not. For example: The continuation for Macbeth "perhaps identical with" Malcolm de Glendochart links to Macnab01. As mentioned at the top of that page, there is at least 
2 CONC one other contradictory claim for the ancestry of that family. The following section is included within this database only because it may yet prove useful for linkage to various of the other clans.
2 CONT Feradach or Ferlach or Feradaig
2 CONT m. Kentigerna (d 734, dau of Ceallach Cualann of Leinster, sister of Comgan)
2 CONT 1.	St. Fillan (d 09.01.703)
2 CONT 2.	Ferchar Fada, King of Dalriada ancestor of Clans Duff, Mackintoch & Cameron
2 CONT  	A.	Ferchar Abraruadh (the Red Abbot) or Og
2 CONT  	BP2003 (Macnab of Macnab), which starts with Malcolm de Glendochart (mentioned below), notes that the Macnabs "by tradition" descend from this Abraruadh (the name Macnab means son of the abbot) but reports that "the genealogy be
2 CONC tween him and Kenneth MacAlpin ... is confused and uncertain". We show Alpin, father of that Kenneth, in the section above.
2 CONT  	i.	Donald Donn (the Brown) ancestor of Clans Macnab, MacLaren, Macnaghten & Mackay
2 CONT  	a.	Erc
2 CONT (1)	Aibertach
2 CONT  	(A)	Cormac ancestor of Clans Macgregor, MacQuarry, Mackinnon, MacMillan & MacLennan
2 CONT  	(i)	Ferchard ancestor of Clan MacDuffy
2 CONT  	(a)	Lorn ancestor of Clans Andres (Ross), Mackenzie & Matheson
2 CONT
