2 CONT '''[https://www.geni.com/people/D%C3%BAnlang-II-mac-Tuathail-King-of-Leinster/6000000002043263901?through=6000000003495402182 DUNLANG] (-1013).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of the Four Masters record the death in 1013 of “Dunlan
2 CONC g son of Tuathal king of Leinster”[641].  m ---.  The name of Dunlang´s wife is not known.  Dunlang & his wife had six children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>a)         [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079504659896?through=6000000079504659896&from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529789693645 GILLA COEMGIN] (-killed [1017/18]).  Crown Prince of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach rec
2 CONC ord that “Gilla Coemgin son of Dunlang crownprince of Leinster” was killed in [1017/18] “by the Leinstermen”[642]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>b)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Donncuan-mac-D%C3%BAnlaing-King-of-Leinster/6000000003494770356?through=6000000002043263901 DONNCUAN] “the Simpleton” (-killed 1015).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of the Four Masters 
2 CONC record that “Donncuan i.e. the Simpleton son of Dunlaing lord of Leinster and Tadhg Ua Riain lord of Ui-Drona” were killed in 1015 by “Donnchadh son of Gillaphadraig at Leithghlinn”[643]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>c)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Augaire-O-Toole/6000000006290757931?through=6000000002043263901 UGAIRE] (-killed Dubloch [1022/24]).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Ugaire son of Dunlang king 
2 CONC of Leinster” defeated “Sitric son of Olaf with the Foreigners of Dublin at Dergnae mo Goróc (Delgany)” in 1021[644].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Augaire son of Dunlang king of Leinster” was killed “at Dubloch, by Donn sl
2 CONC ébe” in [1022/24][645]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>d)         [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079503781372?through=6000000079503781372&from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529789693645 DONNCHAD] (-killed [1036/37]).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Don
2 CONC nchad, son of Dunlang, king of Leinster” was blinded by “Donnchad Mac Gilla Pátraic” in 1036 and died[646].  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 1037 of "Dúnlang´s king of Laigin by the Osraige”[647]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>i)          [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079504053097?through=6000000079504053097&from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529789693645 DOMNALL] (-1039).  Crown Prince of Leinster.  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death i
2 CONC n 1039 of "Domnall son of Donnchad royal heir of Laigin”[648].  The Annals of Tigernach record the death in 1039 of “Domnall son of Donnchad king of the Húi Faeláin…slain by Domnall Húa Fergail king of the Forths”[649]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>e)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Murchad-O-Toole/6000000006290757939?through=6000000002043263901 MURCHAD] (-killed in battle Mag Muilchet 1042).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Murchad son of D
2 CONC unlang king of Leinster” was killed by “Gilla Pátraic son of Donnchad king of Ossory and by Mac Craith Húa Donnchada king of the Eoganacht ´load-of-plunder´ on Mag Muilchet in Leix” in 1042[650]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>f)          [https://www.geni.com/people/M%C3%A1elcorcre-%C3%93-Tuathail/6000000003051255891?through=6000000002043263901 MAILCORCRE] .  The 13th century History of Gruffydd ap Cynan records that the "grandmother...his mother´
2 CONC s mother" of King Gruffydd was "Mailcorcre daughter of Dunlang son of Tuathal King of Leinster"[651].  m OLAF of Dublin, son of SIHTRIC King of Dublin & his wife --- ([after 1013]-murdered 1034). 
