2 CONT
2 CONT Flann Sinna
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT His third wife, Máel Muire, who died in 913, was the daughter of the King of the Picts, Cináed mac Ailpín. She was the mother of Flann’s son, Domnall (King of Mide 919–921; killed by his half-brother Donnchad Donn in 921), and his
2 CONC  daughter, Lígach (died 923), wife of the Síl nÁedo Sláine king of Brega, Máel Mithig mac Flannacáin (died 919).[30]
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth MacAlpin
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth's daughter Máel Muire married two important Irish kings of the Uí Néill. Her first husband was Aed Finliath of the Cenél nEógain. Niall Glúndub, ancestor of the O'Neill, was the son of this marriage. Her second husband was
2 CONC  Flann Sinna of Clann Cholmáin. As the wife and mother of kings, when Máel Muire died in 913, her death was reported by the Annals of Ulster, an unusual thing for the misogynistic chronicles of the age.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Daughter of King Keneth McAlpin of Scotland and granddaughter of Alpin, also a King of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT [1]  Desmond O Neill, "The Ancient and Royal Family of O Neill," Omeath, Co. Louth, Ireland, 1995.
2 CONT
