1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Lulach mac Gille Coemgáin''' (Modern Gaelic: Lughlagh mac Gille Chomghain,[1] known in English simply as Lulach, and nicknamed Tairbith, "the Unfortunate"[2] and Fatuus, "the Simple-minded" or "the Foolish"[3]; 
2 CONC 1030 – 17 March 1058) was King of Scots between 15 August 1057 and 17 March 1058. 
