2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT King of Scotland
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Killed By Malcolm III King Of Scotland
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Name: King Lulach of Scotland Father: Gillacomgean, Mormaer of Moray Mother: Gruoch, daughter of Beoedh, son of Kenneth III House of: Dunkeld Born: c. 1029/32 Ascended to the throne: August 15, 1057 Crowned: August, 1057 at Scone 
2 CONC Abbey, Perthshire Married: Finnghuala, daughter of Sinhill, Mormaer of Angus Children: one son and one daughter Died: March 17, 1058, killed at Essie in Strathbogie by his cousin and successor Malcolm III Buried at: Isle of Iona S
2 CONC ucceeded by: his cousin Malcolm III
2 CONT
2 CONT Lulach (Lulach mac Gille Coemgáin), also know as Lulach ‘The Fool’, was the stepson of Macbeth and son of Macbeth’s wife Gruoch by her first husband Gillacomgean. Lulach was the first Scots king to be crowned at Scone, but was a w
2 CONC eak ineffectual king. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His reigned lasted barely 8 months before he was killed at Essie, Strathbogie, by his successor Malcolm III. 
