2 CONT The O'Briens, one of the few native Irish families with a peerage, descend in the male line from Brian Boroimhe, Prince of Thomond (NorthMunster or the north part of southwest Ireland, roughly commensurate with an area centered on
2 CONC  modern Co. Clare) and Chief of the Dalgais, whobecame High King of Ireland 1002 and was killed at the victory over the Danes of Clontarf 23 April 1014. [Burke's' Peerage, p. 1495]
