1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Jorund Ulfsson''' was the father-in-law and grandfather of Erik the Red and Leif the Lucky the famous Icelandic vikings, Erik who  led the Norse colonisation of Greenland and Leif who brought Christianity to Gre
2 CONC enland and is remembered for "discovering" North America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jorund Ulfsson''' was born in the late 9th century in Reykjanesskagi region of Iceland where his father had settled after leaving Norway. The sagas record that by the time of his daughter's marriage to Erik the Red Jorund's wif
2 CONC e was married to another man which indicates Jorund had died prior to this.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parents:
2 CONT Úlfur "skjálgi" Högnason (b. c. 855, Norway - d. Iceland) & Björg Eyvindsdóttir (b. c. 848 - d. Iceland).
2 CONT ===Married:
2 CONT in Iceland with Thorbjorg Gilsdottir daughter of Gils "Ship-nose" Herfinnsson.
2 CONT ===Children of Jorund and Thorbjorg:
2 CONT #Thjodhild Jörundsdóttir  (c. 940, Iceland - after 1000, Greenland).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Further Reading 
2 CONT *http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Landnamabogen_2 (94)
2 CONT *http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Landnamabogen_2 (77)
2 CONT *http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Sagaen_om_Thorfin_Karlsefne_og_Snorre_Thorbrands%C3%B6n (2)
2 CONT *https://is.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%9Alfur_skj%C3%A1lgi_H%C3%B6gnason
2 CONT *https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%9Alfur_skj%C3%A1lgi_H%C3%B6gnason
2 CONT
2 CONT == Geni notes
2 CONT Hermann Pálsson and Paul Edwards in their 1972 translation of Landnámabók (titled [https://uofmpress.ca/books/detail/the-book-of-settlements The Book of Settlements]) called this man [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=jj6cIwMCZ
2 CONC qIC&q=jorund+atlason#v=snippet&q=jorund%20atlason&f=false "Jorund Atlason"].
