1 NOTE Constantine II King of Scotland
2 CONT Reign: 863-877
1 NOTE Ancestral File Number:<AFN> 9G9M-JKBeheaded in 877. King of Alba. Killedin battle against the Danes at Inverdorat, the Black Cove, Angus. Accededto the thrown in 863.[FAVthomas.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Reign: 863-877. King of the Picts and Scots. King of Alba. Weir says hewas killed in a battle against the Danes at Inverdorat, the Black Cove,Angus. Constantine succeeded to the kingship upon his uncle Donald I'sdeath in 862. His 
2 CONC reign was marked by Viking raid and expansion intoStrathclyde. He was succeeded by his brother Aed.
1 NOTE !SOURCES:
2 CONT     1. Burke's Peerage 99th ed (GS #942 D22bup prefix pp. 285-86)
2 CONT     2. A Vindication of MacBeth (GS #929.2706 M288c p. 14)
2 CONT     3. Dict. of Nat'l Biog. (GS #920.042 D561v vol 12 pp. 46-47)
2 CONT     4. Also searched without possitive results: Encyclopedia Britannica, Scots Peerage, The Complete Peerage, Royal Dau of Engl, and Queens of Scotland and English Princes.
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: Slain in battle with the Norseman at Inverdovat, or the "Black Cave." 
1 NOTE !SOURCES:
2 CONT     1. Burke's Peerage 99th ed (GS #942 D22bup prefix pp. 285-86)
2 CONT     2. A Vindication of MacBeth (GS #929.2706 M288c p. 14)
2 CONT     3. Dict. of Nat'l Biog. (GS #920.042 D561v vol 12 pp. 46-47)
