2 CONT Another name for Aedh was Aed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aedh (c840-878), sometimes spelt Aed or Aodh, became king of Scotland in 877 when he succeeded his brother Constantine I. He was killed shortly after taking the throne by Giric, also known as Gregory the Great, who had conspired w
2 CONC ith Aed's nephew, Eochaid. Not much is known of Aedh, or even if he was actually the one named by Constantine to hold the throne. Both Giric and Eochaid ruled jointly following Aedh's death. Aedh did marry at some point in his lif
2 CONC e, but the details, including the date and place of the marriage, and the name of his wife are not known. One son, Constantine II of Scotland, ruled later, while another son, Donald, became King of Strathclyde in 908. Aedh died vi
2 CONC olently in 878 at Strathallan. He may have been buried at Maiden Stone in Aberdeenshire. He was succceeded under the Scottish tanistry system by his nephew, Eochaid.
2 CONT Acceded: King of Scotland, 877.
1 NOTE He ruled Scotland from 877 to 878.
1 NOTE He ruled Scotland from 877 to 878.
1 NOTE Aedh (også Aed eller Aodh) (født ca. 840, død 878 i Strathallan) var konge av Skottland fra 877 til sin død året etter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Han etterfulgte sin bror Konstantin. Kort tid etter at han kom til makten ble han drept av Giric, som hadde konspirert med Aedhs nevø Eochaid. De etterfulgte ham i et samkongedømme.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lite er kjent om ham. Det er usikkert om det var ham Konstantin utnevnte til tronfølger. Han var gift, men hans kones navn og når de giftet seg er ikke kjent. Hans sønn Konstantin ble senere konge av Skottland, og en yngre sønn, 
2 CONC Donald, ble konge av Strathclyde i 908.
2 CONT
2 CONT Etter at han ble drept er det mulig at han ble begravet i Maiden Stone i Aberdeenshire.
1 NOTE Died in action, buried in Maiden Stone, Aberdeenshire, Scotland. 
