2 CONT a) EOCHAID (-[889]). The 10th century Pictish Chronicle Cronica de Origine Antiquorum Pictorum records that "Eochodius…filius Run regis Britannorum, nepos Cinadei ex filia" succeeded King Aedh and ruled for 11 years before being e
2 CONC xpelled[59]. The 12th century Cronica Regum Scottorum does not name Eochlaid in its king-list[60]. He succeeded his uncle as EOCHAID King of Scotland. His succession appears to have been challenged by Greg (see above). Deposed [88
2 CONC 9]. 
