2 CONC ographer of Gruffydd ap Cynan says Auloed was the King of Dublin and a fifth of Ireland and of Man and many other islands. He was a descendant of Harald Haarfagr. Auloed's wife was the daughter of King Brian, so Gruffydd sprang fr
2 CONC om the noblest royal lines of Wales, Norway and Ireland.   Simpson calls him Anlaf (Olaf) MacSihtric and says also known as Sihtricsson. She also gives vital stats.
2 CONT    Young: Olaf, King of Dublin.   K: Anlaf (Olaf) MacSihtric (Sihtricsson), King of Dublin. Died 1034 on a pilgrimage to Rome.
