2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott's The Consorts and Children of Gruffudd ap Llwelyn , http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id210.html, in which he charts this woman as the wife of Cynan ap Idwal, and NOT Cynan ap Iago. (Steven Ferry, July
2 CONC  22, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Eidio Wyllt - What Was His Birthname?; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id156.html. (Steven Ferry, September 9, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Other names for Ragnaillt were Ragnhildir, Radnaillt of Dublin and Ranult of Dublin ingen Olaf. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Section VJ: Descendants of King Olaf Kvaaran David Thaler 18043 NE 132nd St, Redmond WA 98052 Send questions and corrections to: dthaler@microsoft.com
2 CONT
2 CONT HTML generated by Issue v1.3.6 on 8 Dec. 2008 http://www.armidalesoftware.com/issue/ From Thaler_export.ged Generation One
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. KING OLAF1 KVAARAN of Dublin, Ireland has an unknown birthdate. He married (WN-2) GORMFLIATH OF NAAS, daughter of (WN-1) King Murchad, who died in 1030[1]. Child: +	2	i.	KING SIHTRIC2 OF DUBLIN of Dublin; m. (V-5) SLANI. Genera
2 CONC tion Two
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. KING SIHTRIC2 OF DUBLIN (Olaf KVAARAN1) of Dublin, son of (1) King Olaf1 and (WN-2) Gormfliath (of NAAS) (BORU), was born between 934 and 1031, and died between 948 and 1140. He married (V-5) SLANI, daughter of (V-3) King Brian
2 CONC . [1] Sihtric of the Silken Beard, King of Dublin AR: (239-2) Child: +	3	i.	KING OLAF3 of Dublin; m. (WM-2) MAELCORCRE. Generation Three
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. KING OLAF3 OF DUBLIN (Sihtric2, Olaf KVAARAN1) of Dublin, son of (2) King Sihtric2 and (V-5) Slani, has an unknown birthdate. He married (WM-2) MAELCORCRE, daughter of (WM-1) King Dunlang. [2] Child: +	4	i.	RAGNAILLT4; m. (TO-1
2 CONC ) PRINCE CYNAN AP IAGO. Generation Four
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. RAGNAILLT4 (Olaf of DUBLIN3, Sihtric2, Olaf KVAARAN1), daughter of (3) King Olaf3 and (WM-2) Maelcorcre, was born between 1000 and 1041, and died between 1055 and 1151. She married (TO-1) PRINCE CYNAN AP IAGO of North Wales, Wa
2 CONC les, United Kingdom. [3] Child: See (TO-1) Prince Cynan ap IAGO
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Frederick Lewis Weis, "Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists", 7th ed., Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc., 1999. 2. Ibid., (239-3). 3. Ibid., (239-4).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cynan ap Iago b abt 1030. He md Radnaillt of Dublin abt 1053, daughter of Amlaib mac Sitric and Maelcorcre ingen Dunlaing. She was b abt 1038, of Dublin, Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Cynan ap Iago and Radnaillt of Dublin was:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gruffydd ap Cynan, King of Gwynedd, b abt 1070, d 1137.
2 CONT
2 CONT Radnaillt of Dublin1,2
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 1031
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Amlaíb mac Sitric, rí Gall3,4 b. circa 1010, d. 1034
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Máelcorcre Ó Toole3,4,2 b. before 1014
2 CONT
2 CONT      Also called Ragnhilda Ólafsdóttir.5,6 Radnaillt of Dublin was born in 1025.6 She was born circa 1031 at Dublin, Ireland.7 She was the daughter of Amlaíb mac Sitric, rí Gall and Máelcorcre Ó Toole.3,4,2 Radnaillt of Dublin mar
2 CONC ried Cynan ab Iago, Prince of Gwynedd, son of Brenin Gwynedd Iago ab Idwal o Gwynedd and Afandreg verch Gwair of Wales, before 1055.5,6,1
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Cynan ab Iago, Prince of Gwynedd b. circa 1014, d. 5 August 1063
2 CONT
