1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ivarr Gamal Haraldsson of Dublin was also called Iomhar mac Arailt, rí Gall. He was King of Dublin in Ireland between 999 and 1054. According to the Annals of the Loch Cé 1054: "Imhar, son of Aralt, king of the For
2 CONC eigners, died. / Iomhar mac Arailt, rí Gall, do ég." Got that?
