1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dúnlaith ingen Muirchertach (c. 925 – 999), recorded historically as Dúnflaith ingen Muirchertaig, was an exceptionally prominent 10th-century Irish queen and political dynastic link who connected the northern Uí N
2 CONC éill, the southern Uí Néill, and the Norse-Viking Kingdom of Dublin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Muirchertach mac Néill (Muirchertach of the Leather Cloaks), King of Ailech (d. 943).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Flann ingen Donnchaid, a princess of Mide.
2 CONT
2 CONT Husbands: 
2 CONT
2 CONT #Domnall Donn mac Donnchada, King of Mide.
2 CONT #Olaf Sithricsson (Amlaíb Cuarán), the powerful Norse-Viking King of Dublin and York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dúnlaith lived during an era where strategic marriages were vital to navigating the brutal conflicts between Irish provincial kings and Viking expansion. As the daughter of the most successful anti-Viking general of the age, her m
2 CONC arriages served as massive geopolitical treaties.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first union with the King of Mide bridged the northern and southern branches of the Uí Néill dynasty. Her second marriage to Olaf Cuarán represented a profound political shift, weaving her directly into the elite ruling family
2 CONC  of the Dublin Vikings. Through these strategic marriages, Dúnlaith achieved a rare historical distinction: she became the mother of both a legendary Irish High King and a Viking King of Dublin.
2 CONT
2 CONT She survived the violent political downfalls of her husbands and lived to see her sons rule their respective realms before passing away in 999.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is historically recorded as the mother of:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Máel Sechnaill II (by Domnall Donn) – The celebrated High King of Ireland who spent decades reigning over Tara and locked in a famous rivalry with Brian Boru.
2 CONT #Glúniairn (by Olaf Sithricsson) – The prominent Norse-Gaelic King of Dublin who later allied closely with his half-brother Máel Sechnaill.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
