2 CONT 1.         [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000212119218825 EOCHAID].  m ---.  The primary source which names the wife of Eochaid has not yet been identified.  Eochaid & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)        [https://www.geni.com/people/Alp%C3%ADn-R%C3%AD-na-D%C3%A1l-Riata/6000000001041459819 ALPIN] (-killed in battle against the Picts in Galloway [20 Jul/Aug] 834).  The Chronicle of John of Fordun records the accession of 
2 CONC "Alpin the son of Achay" in 831, that he ruled for three years, was defeated by the Picts "20 July" and beheaded[12].  The 12th century Cronica Regum Scottorum lists "Alpin filius Eochal venenosi iii, Kynedus filius Alpini primus 
2 CONC rex Scottorum xvi…" as kings, dated to the 9th century[13].  m ---.  The name of Alpin's wife is not known.  Alpin & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>i)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Kenneth-I-Mac-Alpine-king-of-the-Picts/6000000001041559796 KENNETH] [Cinaed] MacAlpin (-Forteviot, Perthshire 13 Feb [858], bur [Isle of Iona]).  His parentage is confirmed by the Annals o
2 CONC f Ulster which record the death in 858 of "Cinaed son of Ailpín king of the Picts"[14].  He succeeded as KENNETH I King of Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>ii)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Domnall-mac-Alp%C3%ADn-R%C3%AD-na-D%C3%A1l-Riata/6000000123896637852 DONALD] [Domnall] (-Kinn Belachoir palace or killed in battle Scone 13 Apr [863], bur [Isle of Iona]). The 10th centur
2 CONC y Pictish Chronicle Cronica de Origine Antiquorum Pictorum records that "Kinadius…filius Alpini, primus Scottorum…Dunevaldus frater eius" ruled for four years[15].  The 12th century Cronica Regum Scottorum lists "Alpin filius Eoch
2 CONC al venenosi iii, Kynedus filius Alpini primus rex Scottorum xvi, Dolfnal filius Alpini iiii…" as kings, dated to the 9th century[16].  The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that "Donald also a son of Alpin" succeeded his brother
2 CONC  in 854, reigned for four years, died "at Scone" and was buried "in Iona beside his brother"[17].  He succeeded his brother as DONALD I King of Scotland.  The 11th century Synchronisms of Flann Mainistreach name (in order) "Cinaet
2 CONC  mac Ailpin…Domnall mac Ailpin, Custantin mac Cinaeta, (Aedh mac Cinaedha), Girg mac Dungaile, Domnall Dasachtach (mac Custantin)" as Scottish kings, dated to the 9th and 10th centuries[18].  The Annals of Ulster record the death 
2 CONC in 862 of "Domnall son of Ailpín king of the Picts"[19].  The Chronicle of the Scots and Picts dated 1177 records that "Douenald mac Alpin" reigned for 4 years, died "in Rathinueramon" and was buried "in Iona insula"[20].  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The precise relationship between the following family group and the main family of Scottish kings has not been determined, but the names suggest a close relationship. 
2 CONT 1.         ALPIN .  m ---.  The name of Alpin’s wife is not known.  Alpin & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT >a)         EOCHAID (-[937/40]).  The 10th century Pictish Chronicle Cronica de Origine Antiquorum Pictorum records the death of "Dubucan filius Indrechtaig mormair Oengusa, Adalstan filius Advar rig Saxan, et Eochaid filius Alpin
2 CONC i"[32], dated to [937/40] if the second person named can be identified as Æthelstan King of Wessex. 
