2 CONT Conaire slew Nuadha Neacht to become the ninety-seventh monarch of Ireland and was known as the "Peace King".
2 CONT
2 CONT Tha Annals of the Four Masters says: "It was in the reign of Conaire that the sea annually cast its produce ashore, at Inbhear Colptha. Great abundance of nuts were annually found upon the Boinn Boyne and the Buais during his time
2 CONC . The cattle were without keepers in Ireland in his reign, on account of the greatness of the peace and concord. His reign was not thunder producing or stormy, for the wind did not take a hair off the cattle from the middle of Aut
2 CONC umn to the middle of Spring. Little but the trees bent from the greatness of their fruit during his time."
