1 NOTE King of the Picts, inhabitants of the land north of the Firth of Forth. The Picts were locked in a civil war in the early 700s with many kinsmen challenging one another for kingship. Nechtan mac Derile became king in 711, but was 
2 CONC driven from the throne in 726 by Drest, the head of a rival lineage. Drest was himself defeated later that year by Alpín. Alpín was defeated in 728 by Unuist mac Uurguist.
1 NOTE King of the Picts, inhabitants of the land north of the Firth of Forth. The Picts were locked in a civil war in the early 700s with many kinsmen challenging one another for kingship. Nechtan mac Derile became king in 711, but was 
2 CONC driven from the throne in 726 by Drest, the head of a rival lineage. Drest was himself defeated later that year by Alpín. Alpín was defeated in 728 by Unuist mac Uurguist.
