1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''Aoife (Macduibhn) Campbell (abt. 1050)'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT Aoife (Eva) Campbell formerly Macduibhn
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Born:''' about 1050 in Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ANCESTORS:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of '''Paul (MacDuibhn) O'Dwibhne MacDuibhn''' and '''Marion (Godfrey) O'Dwibhne MacDuibhn'''
2 CONT * Sibling(s) unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SPOUSE:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of '''Archibald Campbell''' — married [date and location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''DESCENDANTS:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Mother of '''Duncan MacDurine Campbell'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Died:''' Date and location unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BIOGRAPHY:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Aoife, known to the English as Eva, was born in the mid 11th C., the daughter of Paul MacDuibhn (1015-1066)  and Marion Godfrey (1030-?). Her father Paul was treasurer to the Kings Duncan Ist and his son, Malcolm of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following her father's death, her uncle Arthur Cruachan became her guardian.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married her cousin Gillespie (Archibald Campbell), whose father, Malcolm MacDuibhn had married the heiress of Cambus-bellus in Normandy. In memory of their Norman origins, descendants of Aoife and Gillespie took the name "Camp
2 CONC bell" [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Gillespie and Aoife O’Duibhne - [2] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Duncan Campbell d. in 1097; m. Diorbahil - Dorvail (Dorothy) MacFiachir, dau. of Dugald Cruachan Thane of Over Lochow; issue (surname Campbell): Cailen (bald good) “Maol Math” Chief of Clan MacDuine (–1110 in Dunstaffnage, Oban, K
2 CONC ilmore, Argyll).
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Electric Scotland : The House of Argyle and the Collateral Branches of the Clan Campbell from the year 420 to the present time - pub: John Tweed, Glasgow 1871 - [http://www.electricscotland.com/webclans/atoc/houseofargyllcampbel
2 CONC l.pdf]
2 CONT # Not to be confused with Gilleasbaig of Menstrie ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilleasbaig_of_Menstrie]) who first appeared in royal charters dating to the 1260s
2 CONT # Clan Cleary.com ([http://www.clancleary.com]) has her proper Irish naming of Aoife, but is one of the sources that confuses her husband with the Gillespic Campbell of several generations later who was father of Sir Colin Mohr Ca
2 CONC mpbell of Lochow.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Macduibhn-1]
