1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diarmait_mac_M%C3%A1el_na_mB%C3%B3
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IRELAND.htm#_Toc389126196
2 CONT
2 CONT Darbforgaill married Diarmait MacMáil nam Bó, King of Ireland & Leinster. Diarmait was King of Leinster from 1042 to 1052, at which time he became High King of Ireland, a post which he held from 1052 until his death on February 7,
2 CONC  1072. When Dairmait became High King of Ireland in 1052, it appears that he resigned as King of Leinster and his son Murchad took over that post.
2 CONT
2 CONT Darbforgaill and Diarmait had the following son:
2 CONT
2 CONT Murchad macDiarmata macMáil
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Name: Diarmait MacMail na MBO , King Of Ireland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: M 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: BET 1000 AND 1025 in Leinster, Ireland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 1090
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT I came across information that says Diarmait's name was "Diarmait MacMail" and his son's name was Murchad MacDiarmata MacMail.  (Terry O'Hare 9/12/08)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''[https://www.geni.com/people/Dairmait-King-of-Leinster-High-King-of-Ireland/6000000008630666266?through=6000000006831823543  DIARMAIT], son of MAEL na mBó & his wife --- (-killed in battle Odba 7 Feb 1072).  The Annals of Tige
2 CONC rnach record that “Ruaidri son of Tadg son of Lorcan” was blinded in 1036 by “Mael na mbó” (which must indicate the latter´s son assuming that the death date of Mail na mBó is correctly recorded above)[665].  The Annals of Tigerna
2 CONC ch record that “Diarmait son of Mael na mbó king of the Húi Cennselaig” plundered “Colomb cille´s Maein (Moone), Dísert Diarmata and my Senóc´s Mugna and Clonmore” in 1040[666].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Echmarcach son
2 CONC  of Ragnall king of the Foreigners went oversea” in 1052 and “the son of Mael na mbó assumed the kingship after him”, adding in a later passage that “the son of Mael na mbó took the kingship of Dublin by force” in 1053[667].  King
2 CONC  of Leinster.  High King of Ireland.  The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle records that Harold Godwinsson and his brother Leofwine, sons of Godwin Earl of Wessex, sought refuge with him in 1051 following the family's disgrace[668].  Orderic 
2 CONC Vitalis records that “duo filii Heraldi regis Angliæ” had fled “ad Dyrmetum regem Hiberniæ” after their father was killed and, with his support, landed at Exeter with 66 ships, ravaged the interior of the country, but were defeate
2 CONC d by “Briennius Eudonis comitis Britanniæ minoris filius et Guillelmus Gualdi” and fled back to Ireland[669].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Diarmait son of Mail na mbó, king of Britons and the Hebrides and Dublin and Mug N
2 CONC uadat´s Half [southern Ireland]” was killed in 1072 by “Conchobar Húa Mael-Sechlainn in the battle of Odba”[670].  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1072 of "Diarmait son of Mael na mBó king of Laigin and the foreigners…7 F
2 CONC eb” killed in battle by “Conchobar ua Mael Sechlainn king of Temair”[671]. m [https://www.geni.com/people/Dearbforgail-%C3%93-Briain/6000000005599447055?through=6000000006831823543  DERBORGAILL], daughter of ---, granddaughter of 
2 CONC BRIAN Boru King of Ireland (-Imlech 1080).  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1080 of "Derbhforgaill daughter of Brian´s son, wife of Diarmait son of Mael na mBó…in Imlech”[672]. Diarmait & his wife had three children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Murchad-Mac-Diarmata-O-Cheinnselaig/6000000006831823543  MURCHAD] (-Dublin 1070, bur Dublin).  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Murchad son of Diarmait son of Mael na mbó” invaded “Man
2 CONC n…and defeated Ragnall´s son” in 1061[673].  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1070 of "Murchad son of Diarmait king of Laigin and the foreigners…buried in Áth Cliath”[674].  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 107
2 CONC 0 of "Murchad son of Diarmiat son of Mael na mBó king of foreigners and Gaedil…in Áth Cliath”[675].  m ---.  The name of Murchad´s wife is not known.  Murchad & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>a)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Donal-Mac-Morough-Dublin/6000000008177419512 DOMNALL] (-1075).  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "the son of Murchad, grandson of Mael na mBó took the kingship of Áth Cliath” in 1075 
2 CONC and died “in the same year”[676].  King of Dublin.  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1075 of "Domnall son of Murchad, king of Áth Cliath…of a three nights' sickness"[677]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>b)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Donnchad-mac-Murchada-King-of-Leinster-and-Dublin/6000000002043258537  DONCHAD] (-1115).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “the son of Murchad, son of
2 CONC  Diarmait, son of Máel na mbó” won a battle in 1114[678]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>c)         ENDA .  His parentage is confirmed by the Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) which names “Diarmait son of Enda, son of Murchad, king of the Foreigners and Leinstermen”[679].  m ---.  The name of Enda´s wife is not kn
2 CONC own.  Enda & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>i)          DIARMUIT (-[1117]).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Diarmait son of Enda, son of Murchad, king of the Foreigners and Leinstermen, rested in Dublin” in 1117[680]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>d)         GORMLAITH (-1112).  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "Gormlaith, daughter of Murchad coarb of Brigit, rested” in 1112[681].  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1112 of "Gormlaith daughter of Murchad son of 
2 CONC Diarmait, successor of Brigit”[682]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>2.         ENNA (-killed 1092).  His parentage is confirmed by the Annals of Ulster which name "Diarmait son of Enna son of Diarmait king of Laigin”[683].  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "Enna son of Diarmait and the noble
2 CONC s of Desmumu” successfully held the fortress of “Port Láirge” in 1088 against “the Laigin and the son of Domnall Remar”[684].  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "Muirchertach Ui Briain” imprisoned “Énna son of Diarmait” in 1089
2 CONC [685].  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 1092 of "Enna son of Diarmait…slain by the Uí Cheinnselaig”[686].  m ---.  The name of Enna´s wife is not known.  Enna & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>a)         DIARMUIT (-killed Cell Dara 1098).  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1098 of "Diarmait son of Enna son of Diarmait king of Laigin, killed by the sons of Murchad son of Diarmait…in the middle of Cell Dara”[687
2 CONC ]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>3.         --- “Glún Iairn” (-killed in battle 1070).  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 1070 of "Glún Iairn son of Diarmiat son of Mael na mBó…slain by Cartach´s son and the Gailenga and by the north of Ireland”[688]
2 CONC . 
