2 CONC as Jarl of Orkney and Caithness.  He defeated Findlaech Mormaer of Moray before 995 at the second battle of Skidmoor in Caithness, consolidating his power on the Scottish mainland.  Orkneyinga Saga records Sigurd´s battle against 
2 CONC “a Scottish earl called Finnleik”[858].  Orkneyinga Saga records that “[http://www.geni.com/people/Olav-Tryggvason/6000000003867333182 Olaf Tryggvason]” pressured Sigurd to accept baptism and returned to Norway with Sigurd´s son a
2 CONC s a hostage[859].  Orkneyinga Saga records that Sigurd went to Ireland “five years after the Battle of Svoldur” to support “King [http://www.geni.com/people/Sitric-I-King-of-Dublin/6000000002043182790?through=6000000003645985234 S
2 CONC igtrygg Silk-Beard]” against “[http://www.geni.com/people/Brian-B%C3%B3ruma-mac-Cenn%C3%A9tig/6000000002043263223  King Brian] of Ireland”, and left “his elder sons in charge of the earldom”, but was killed in the battle in which 
2 CONC King Brian was killed[860].  Snorre records that "Sigurd the Thick" went to Ireland and fell "in Brian's battle"[861].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
