2 CONT A Goði and the owner of the Ljosavatn estate in Þineyjar County.  President of the Alþing from 985-1000.  He was appointed by the Alþing, in 999 or 1000 to make the decision as to whether or not Iceland should legally adopt Christ
2 CONC ianity.  His decision to make it law that all should be baptized is said to have saved the country from a lot of Parliamentary wrangling and possibly civil war.  When Þorgeirr returned home after closing the Alþing (which had unan
2 CONC imously agreed to abide by his decision) he took all his pagan images and threw them into a large waterfall near his home.  It has since been known as Goðafoss (god’s falls).
