1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Muirchertach Ua Néill (c. 950 – 977), known historically as Muirchertach Midech, was a prominent 10th-century Irish prince and royal heir of the Northern Uí Néill dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Domnall ua Néill, the 173rd High King of Ireland (d. 980).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Mór, a princess of Connacht.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Cres Cumal of the Uí Maine.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Note: In unverified genealogies, his biography is frequently confused and blended with his famous grandfather, Muirchertach "of the Leather Cloaks" who died in 943).
2 CONT
2 CONT Muirchertach grew up during a highly volatile era marked by shifting alliances and intense conflict with the Norse-Vikings of Dublin. As the son of the High King, he was recognized as a Rígdamna (an eligible royal prince and heir 
2 CONC to the throne).
2 CONT
2 CONT His promising political and military career was cut tragically short in 977. Muirchertach was slain in a fierce battle fought against the Dublin Vikings, who were led at the time by his own uncle, Olaf Sithricsson. Because of his 
2 CONC early death, he never succeeded his father to the High Kingship of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is historically recorded as the father of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Flaithbertach Ua Néill (c. 975 – 1036) – The powerful King of Ailech who later abdicated to go on a pilgrimage to Rome.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Within the official traditions of Clan MacNeil, Muirchertach is recognized as the 17th Ancestral Chief. While his historical title was a prince of Ailech rather than a Scottish clan chief, he represents a crucial link in the tradi
2 CONC tional lineage connecting the clan to the royal Uí Néill dynasty of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hugo O'Neill, heir apparent (in 1970 anyway) to the Chieftainry of
