1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Donald mac William1,2 M, #49311, d. 31 July 1187
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	William Fitz Duncan Earl of Moray, Lord of Skipton1,3 b. bt 1092 - 1094, d. bt 1153 - 1154 Mother	Gruaidh (?)1,3,4
2 CONT
2 CONT Donald mac William died on 31 July 1187 at Margania Moor, Speyside, Scotland; killed in uprising to regain the throne.1,3,2 Family 	 Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT Gothred/Godfrey mac Donald1,2 d. 1213 <br/>
2 CONT Donald mac Donald1,2 d. 1215
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Citations====
2 CONT
2 CONT [S1361] Mike Ashley, The Mammoth Book of British Kings & Queens (New York: Carroll & Graf Publishers, Inc., 1998), p. 396. ''Hereinafter cited as Ashley: British Kings.''
2 CONT
2 CONT [S1438]  [http://genealogy.euweb.cz/index.html Miroslav Marek, online], unknown author (e-mail address), downloaded updated 15 May 2003, [http://genealogy.euweb.cz/brit/dunkeld.html Dunkeld page (The House of Dunkeld)]
2 CONT
2 CONT [S1426] Jiri Louda (Tables) and Michael Maclagan (text), Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe (NY: Barnes & Noble Books, 2002), Table 12: Scotland: Kings until the accession of Robert Bruce. Hereinafter ci
2 CONC ted as Louda & Maclagan "Lines of Succession."
2 CONT
2 CONT [S1490] Leo van de Pas Web Site [http://www.genealogics.org/index.php "Leo's Genealogics Website"], (online), [http://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00076166&tree=LEO William FitzDuncan]. ''Hereinafter cited as Leo's 
2 CONC Genealogics Website.''
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.acvancestors.com/g1/p1644.htm#i49311  Ancestors of Alexandra Catlin Vaut] 
2 CONT
2 CONT William had several marriages. His first marriage was over, presumably through death, by the year 1137, when he married Alice de Rumilly, daughter of William Meschin. By the latter, he had a son, also called William (William of Eg
2 CONC remont or William the Atheling), who died in 1160, and a daughter Cicely, Lady of Skipton, who married William le Gros, 1st Earl of Albemarle. He also had a large number of bastards, probably including Wimund of the Isles. 
2 CONT
2 CONT " ''It is now presumed that Domnall mac Uilleim, and the Meic Uilleim clan that repeatedly rebelled against later Scottish kings in their quest to gain the Scottish throne, were legitimate descendants of a marriage to a daughter o
2 CONC f Óengus of Moray.'' "
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1147, whereupon Moray fell back into the hands of David [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_fitz_Duncan William fitz Duncan (Wikipedia)] 
