1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The name Campbell comes from the Gaelic "Cam beul", meaning curved mouth (as in cam shaft).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT FamilySearch []https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L5Y8-P7N?1=1&spouse=L5Y4-GTD
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ='''Archibald Gillespic "Gillocallum" Campbell aka Campbell of Menstrie (1041-1091)'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Born:''' about 1041 in Menstrie, Clackmannanshire
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ANCESTORS:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of '''Malcolm MacDwine MacDuibhn''' and '''Cambus Bellus Beauchamp'''
2 CONT * Brother of '''Duncan Dionysius Campbell''' and '''Dwine (Campbell) O'Dwibhne'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SPOUSE:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Husband of '''Aoife (Macduibhn) Campbell''' — married [date and location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''DESCENDANTS:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father of '''Duncan MacDurine Campbell'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Died:''' 1091 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BIOGRAPHY:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT This person was created on 21 March 2011 through the import of Rose Family Tree.ged. --- Archibald (Gillespic) Campbell of Menstrie, Clackmannanshire. Died in 1091.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Aoife O’Duibhne, dau. of Paul “the Sporran” MacDuibhn (O’Duin) Lord of Lochow, Kings Treasurer (son of Arthur Armderg (red armour)) and Marion _____ of Man (dau. of Godfred I _____ King of the Isle of Man). AKA: Eva Na (Ma
2 CONC cduibhn)
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue of Archibald (Gillespic) Campbell of Menstrie, Clackmannanshire and Aoife O’Duibhne: i. son Duncan Campbell d. in 1097; m. Diorbahil - Dorvail (Dorothy) MacFiachir, dau. of Dugald Cruachan Thane of Over Lochow; issue (surnam
2 CONC e Campbell): Cailen (bald good) “Maol Math” Chief of Clan MacDuine (–1110 in Dunstaffnage, Oban, Kilmore, Argyll).
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes on Archibald (Gillespic) Campbell of Menstrie, Clackmannanshire: (http://www.baronage.co.uk/2003b/tavish.html)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes on Aoife O’Duibhne: http://www.clancleary.com has her proper Irish naming of Aoife, but is one of the sources that confuses her husband with the Gillespic Campbell of several generations later who was father of Sir Colin Moh
2 CONC r Campbell of Lochow.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT '''FURTHER INFORMATION:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Archibald was born in 1041 in Normandy, Gaul (France), and died about 1076 in Scotland. He married Eva (Aoife) na MacDubhn about 1067 in Scotland. His parents were Campbell Malcolm MacDubhn and Cambus Bellus Beauchamp.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Campbell-1399]
