1 NOTE rí Laigin = Roi de Leinster <li> RBS : Annals of Ulster 1115: "A defeat was inflicted by Domnall ua Briain and the foreigners of Áth Cliath on the Laigin, and in it fell Donnchad grandson of Mael na mBó king of Uí Cheinnselaigh, a
2 CONC nd Conchobor ua Conchobuir, king of Uí Fhailgi, with their sons and many others besides. / Maidm ria n-Domnall H. m-Briain & ria Gallaibh Atha Cliath for Laighnibh i torchair Donnchadh H. Mail na m-Bo ri H. Ceinnselaigh ..."2 He d
2 CONC ied in 1115 in Lough Carmen, Wexford, Leinster, Ireland. Killed in battle against Domnal Ua Briainn and the foreigners of Áth Cliath.
1 NOTE Source: "The Rufus Parks Pedigree" by Brian J.L. Berry.
