1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/6516/TABLES%20-%20EARLY%20SERIES_47.png?sequence=8&isAllowed=y (May 31, 2018; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT It is Darrell Wolcott who suggests that Ithel was the son of Coel ap Gweirydd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ithel also served at the courts of Llewelyn ap Seisyll and Cynfyn ap Gwerystan.  He married Nest verch Cynfyn, sister of Efa verch Cynfyn, who married Ithel's beother Llewelyn.  When Gruffudd ap Llewelyn became king, he made Ithel
2 CONC  "pencynydd," the chief huntsman in charge of the hounds.  For his service, he was granted lands on Pennant Melangell.
2 CONT
