1 OCCU Foreldrar: Ósvaldur helgi Englakonungur og Úlfrún Játmundardóttir.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''from [http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Landnamabogen_1#cite_ref-20 '''Landnamabok] <br/>
2 CONT Rap var gift med Thorun Grønninge-rype. Sammen havde de sønnen Thord Skægge, som var gift med Vilborg, en datter af kong Osvald og Ulfrun den Ufødte, der var en datter af kong Edmund af England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Viborg Osvaldsdatter (Vilborg Ósvaldsdóttir)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Viborg bodde på Island''' 
2 CONT * f, ca 860 sannsynligvis i East Anglia, England, datter av Osvald og Ulfrun 
2 CONT * Viborg var gift  med Tord Skægge, de hadde barna Helga og Thurid 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ósvaldr enn helgi  Tilnavn / fordanskning: Osvald  Lokalitet: Norge Relationer: Havde datteren Vilborg, som var gift med Thord Skægge. Kilder: Landnamabogen: 11, 268. Noter: Kaldes konge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilder Olav Tryggvasons saga Bind 1 ss  218 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Navneindex:_A._Personnavne#V
2 CONT
2 CONT http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Oldnordiske_Sagaer,_Bind_1-12
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Vilborg, the daughter of king Oswald and of Ulfrun the Unborn, daughter of Edmund, king of the English. .. Cf Olaf Tryggvi's son's Saga, c. n8.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Landnamabogen_1#cite_ref-15 (11)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oswald_of_East_Anglia Oswald was king of East Anglia in the 870s after the death of Edmund the Martyr. No textual evidence of his reign is known, but some of his coins are known from the same period
2 CONT
2 CONT Evidence suggests that during the period between the death of Edmund the Martyr and the return of Guthrum to East Anglia in 880, Oswald and Æthelred ruled the East Angles as client kings. It is possible that the East Anglian arist
2 CONC ocracy had been almost, but not entirely, extinguished by the Viking attacks that resulted in Edmund's death, and that in the years when Oswald, Æthelred and Guthrum successively ruled the kingdom, there was a period of opposition
2 CONC  or defiance against the Danish leadership.[1] The Vikings ruled the East Angles from the accession of Oswald, until 920, when East Anglia was incorporated into the kingdom of England after the defeat of the Danes by Edward the El
2 CONC der.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The existence of Oswald is known solely because of his coins.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Coins and silver bullion was used throughout the period of the Viking attacks in East Anglia and the Vikings continued the Anglo-Saxon tradition of producing silver pennies, although at a reduced rate. Eight coins are known from t
2 CONC he reigns of Æthelred and Oswald, whereas over two hundred are known to have been made by the moneyers of Oswald's predecessor, Edmund.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT A few coins bearing Oswald's name were found in the Cuerdale Hoard. The coins can be dated from the 870s to the 900s, following the death of Edmund the Martyr. One of the coins, produced by a moneyer whose name started Beor..., is
2 CONC  of the temple type: another has an alpha, a common East Anglian design.[5][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Foreldrar: Ósvaldur helgi Englakonungur og Úlfrún Játmundardóttir. Átti 3 börn með Þórði „skeggi“ Hrappssyni
2 CONT
2 CONT http://baekur.is/en/bok/000233823/0/450/Landnamabok  ...Vilborg Ósvaldsdóttir the king... Landnáma
2 CONT
2 CONT Vilborg Ósvaldsdóttir born. Fædd (860) Parents: Foreldrar: Ósvaldur helgi Englakonungur og Úlfrún Játmundardóttir. Sources: Heimildir: Landnáma, Sturl., Njáls saga, Austurland.II
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Parent: Ósvaldur helgi Englakonungur og Úlfrún Játmundardóttir. 
