2 CONC th Sigurd´s son “Hvelp or Hundi…baptised…[as] Hlodvir” as a hostage, adding that “Hlodvir didn´t live long” and that his father refused to pay homage to King Olaf after his son died[884].  He was taken to Norway as a hostage by Ol
2 CONC af Tryggvesson [995], baptised as Hlodve, but died there soon after[885].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
