1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Freydís Eiríksdóttir was a daughter of Erik the Red, associated with the Norse exploration of North America. The only medieval sources which mention Freydís are the two Vinland sagas, believed to be composed in the
2 CONC  13th century but purporting to describe events around 1000. They offer widely different accounts, though in both Freydís appears as a strong-willed woman. Eiríks saga rauða describes her as a half-sister of Leif Eiríksson but acc
2 CONC ording to Grœnlendinga saga she was a full sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Read more: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freyd%C3%ADs_Eir%C3%ADksd%C3%B3ttir 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2021: This year it is 1000 years since Freydís Eiríksdóttir lived in Vinland.
2 CONT
2 CONT BBC: [https://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-58996186 Vikings settled in North America in 1021AD, study says.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Frøydis Eiriksdatter (norrønt Freydís Eiríksdóttir) var ei beryktet norrøn kvinne som seilte til Vinland i Nord-Amerika tidlig på 1000-tallet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fra Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fr%C3%B8ydis_Eiriksdatter
