1 NAME Roderic O'Connor /of Connaught/
2 GIVN Roderic O'Connor
2 _MARNM of Connaught
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1198
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children and descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT The last of Ruaidrí's descendants to hold the kingship of Connacht, Aedh mac Ruaidri Ua Conchobair, died in 1233. The Annals of Connacht give the following reason for this:
2 CONT
2 CONT Aed mac Ruaidri had been five years King of Connacht, as the poet said: 'Aed mac Ruaidri of the swift onslaught, five years his rule over the province, till he fell— a loss on every frontier— by the hand of Fedlimid.' Here ends th
2 CONC e rule of the children of Ruaidri O Conchobair, King of Ireland. For the Pope offered him the title to [the kingship of] Ireland for himself and his seed for ever, and likewise six wives, if he would renounce the sin of adultery h
2 CONC enceforth; and since he would not accept these terms God took the rule and sovranty from his seed for ever, in punishment for his sin.
2 CONT
2 CONT The annals and genealogies list thirteen children fathered by Ruaidrí. There may have been more.
2 CONT
2 CONT – Conchobar Ua Conchobair
2 CONT
2 CONT – Muirchertach Ua Conchobair
2 CONT
2 CONT – Aedh Muimhnech Ua Conchobair. Had a son, Conchobar, alive in 1236.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Domnall Mór Ua Conchobair. Had a son, Niall, killed 1242.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Aed mac Ruaidrí Ua Conchobair, died 1159.
2 CONT
2 CONT - The daughter of Ruaidhri Ua Conchobair, wife of [F]laithbertach Ua Maeldoraidh, was killed by the sons of Ua Cairella[i]n in 1176.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Rose Ní Conchobair, married Hugh de Lacy, Lord of Meath about 1180, and had descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT – Conchobar Máenmaige Ua Conchobhair, died 1189.
2 CONT
2 CONT – Diarmait mac Ruaidrí Ó Conchobair, died 1221. Had sons Diarmait (fl. 1237), Donnchad (fl. 1237), Muirchertach (k. 1237) and Cormac.
2 CONT
2 CONT – Muirghis Cananach Ua Conchobhair, died 1224.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Nuala Ní Conchobair, died 1226.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Aedh mac Ruaidri Ó Conchobair, died 1233.
2 CONT
2 CONT – Toirdelbach mac Ruaidhi Ó Conchobair, died 1239. Had sons Conchobar Buide and Brian.
2 CONT
2 CONT - M1211.8. Raghnailt and Caillech De, two daughters of Roderic O'Conor, died.
2 CONT
2 CONT All of Ruaidrí's large male progeny faded into obscurity in the first half of the 13th century. The last to be mentioned in the Gaelic-Irish annals was his grandson, Niall son of Domnall Mór, who was killed in 1242.
2 CONT
2 CONT The result is that there are no demonstratable male-line descendants of Ireland's last high-king recorded after the 1240s. All kings of Connacht from 1233 descended from Ruaidrí's much younger brother, Cathal Crobhdearg Ua Conchob
2 CONC air. The Ó Conchubhair Donn, the senior member of the entire Síol Muireadaigh dynasty, likewise descends from Cathal Crobhdearg.
