1 NOTE {geni:about_me} King Dub Dubh Duff of the Scots ruled Scotland from 962 to 967 He followed Indulphus as King of Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Malcolm I & his wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         DUBH [Duff] (-killed in battle Forres [19/20 Jul 966], bur Isle of Iona).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The 10th century Pictish Chronicle Cronica de Origine Antiquorum Pictorum records that "Niger filius Maelcolaim" was king after King Indulf and reigned for five years[126].  The 11th century Synchronisms of Flann Mainistreach name
2 CONC  (in order) "…Domnall Dasachtach (mac Custantin), Custantin mac Aeda, Maelcolaim mac Domnall, Illolb mac Custantin, Dub mac Maelcolaim, Cuillen mac Illiulb…" as Scottish kings, dated to the 10th century[127].  It is assumed that "
2 CONC Niger" and "Dub" in these two sources refer to the same person, although this is not beyond all doubt.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The 12th century Cronica Regum Scottorum lists "…Duf filius Malcolin iv annis et vi mensibus…" as king[128].  The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that "Duff the son of King Malcolm" succeeded in 961 after Indulf was killed and
2 CONC  reigned for four years and six months[129].  He succeeded in 962 as DUFF King of Scotland.  The 10th century Pictish Chronicle Cronica de Origine Antiquorum Pictorum records that "Niger filius Maelcolaim" defeated "Caniculum supe
2 CONC r Dorsum Crup", in which battle "Duchad abbas Duncalden et Dubdon satrapas Athochlach" were killed, after which Niger was expelled and "Caniculus" reigned for a short time[130].  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 967 of "Du
2 CONC b son of Mael Coluim king of Scotland…killed by the Scots themselves"[131].  The Chronicle of the Scots and Picts dated 1177 records that "Duf mac Malcolm" reigned for 4 years and 6 months, was killed "in Fores…absconditus…sub pon
2 CONC te de Kynloss", when the sun did not shine, and was buried "in Iona insula"[132].  The Chronicle of the Picts and Scots dated 1251 includes the same information[133].  The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that Duff was killed b
2 CONC y robbers who hid his body, that "no ray of sunlight gleamed within the whole kingdom" until it was found, and that he was buried at Iona[134].  According to Duncan, this eclipse of the sun has been dated to 20 Jul 966[135].  Dunc
2 CONC an says that, according to other sources, he was killed "by the men of Moray", in 967[136].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Dubh's wife is not known.  Dubh & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Kenneth-III-Mac-Duibh-king-of-Scots/4659985?through=6000000003219779698 KENNETH], son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Dubh-mac-M%C3%A1el-Coluim-King-of-Scots/6000000000202034309?through=4659985 '''DUFF
2 CONC '''] King of Scotland & his wife --- (-killed in battle Monzievaird [25 Mar 1005]).  The 11th century Synchronisms of Flann Mainistreach name (in order) "…Cuillen mac Illiulb, Cinaet mac Maelcolaim, Custantin mac Cuilen, Cinaet ma
2 CONC c Duib, Maelcolaim mac Cinaeta" as Scottish kings, dated to the 10th and 11th centuries[208].  The 12th century Cronica Regum Scottorum lists "…Chinet filius Duf i anno et dimidium…" as king[209].  He succeeded in 997 as KENNETH I
2 CONC II King of Scotland.  The Annals of Ulster record that "the king of the Albu Cinaed son of Dub" was killed in battle "between the men of Albu themselves" in 1005[210]. m ---.  The name of Kenneth's wife is not known. Kenneth III &
2 CONC  his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Giric-II-mac-Cin%C3%A1eda-King-of-Scots/6000000003615429242?through=4659985 GREG] [Giric] (-killed in battle Monzievaird [25 Mar 1005], bur Isle of Iona).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >2.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Gille-Coemg%C3%A1in-mac-Cin%C3%A1eda/6000000002278167864?through=4659985 GILLACOMGAIN] (-killed in battle 999).  
2 CONT
