2 CONC planned to change the laws of succession. See ESSH, pp. 512–515.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10.^ ESSH, p. 516.
2 CONT
2 CONT 11.^ Annals of the Four Masters, s.a. 998: "Dúngal Cináed's son, was killed by Gille Coemgáin, Cináed's son." It is not clear if the Cináeds (Kenneths) referred to are Cináed mac Maíl Coluim (Kenneth II) or his nephew and namesake
2 CONC  Cináed mac Duib (Kenneth III). Smyth, pp. 221–222, makes Dúngal following ESSH p. 580.
2 CONT
2 CONT 12.^ Compare Duncan, p.345 and Lynch (ed), Genealogies, at about p. 680. See also ESSH, p. 580.
