2 CONT Kenneth II, King of Scots 971-95, was murdered in 994/95
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Kenneth became King of Scots in 971, when his predecessor Cuilen was killed by the Strathclyde Britons. There are some indications that Kenneth had a joint kingship with Cuilen's brother Olaf until 977, when Olaf was killed. Kenne
2 CONC th led successful raids against Strathclyde in both 971 and 972.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 973, Kenneth attended a conference of kings at Chester, in England, which was probably organized by Edgar, King of England. Kenneth appears to have had a quiet but successful reign and was killed 'by treachery' in 995, and succ
2 CONC eeded by Constantine son of Cuilen, a distant cousin.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is possible that Kenneth married an Irish woman from Leinster, as a twelfth-century Scottish poem calls his son Malcolm 'son of a woman of the Leinstermen'.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He was murdered by his own men. He came to his end by "female treachery". He had to put to death the only son of Fenella, wife of the maor mor or viceroy of Kincardineshire. Fenella, though the execution had been a deserved one, d
2 CONC id not the less readily determine to revenge her son's death. She invited Kenneth to lodge in her house near Ferrercairn in the Mearns. here he was assassinated. The inhospitable murderess escaped from her castle, down the valley 
2 CONC to a place in the parish of Fordun where she was seized and put to death.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Kenneth II, King of Alba 
