2 CONT
2 CONT Cammán mac Amlaíb was a Norse-Gaelic viking who is recorded in the Irish annals as being defeated in 960. He has been identified as being a son of Amlaíb mac Gofraid (d.941), as well as possibly being Sitriuc Cam, who was defeated
2 CONC  in battle by Amlaíb Cuarán two years later.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IRELAND.htm#_Toc389126206
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf [& his wife] had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          SIHTRIC "Caman" (-after 960).  The Annals of Ulster record that "Camán son of Amlaíb son of Gothfrith was defeated at Dub” in 960[1229].  The Annals of the Four Masters record in 960 “a prey by Sitric Cam from the sea 
2 CONC to Ui-Colgain, but he was overtaken by Amhlaeibh, with the foreigners of Ath-cliath and the Leinstermen”[1230]. 
