1 OCCU Queen of Northumbria and Abbess of Wimborne Minster
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Saint Cuthburga of Wimborne'''
2 CONT Birth  665  England
2 CONT Death  31 Aug 725 (aged 59–60), Wimborne Minster, East Dorset District, Dorset, England
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT St. Cuthburga Churchyard
2 CONT Wimborne Minster, East Dorset District, Dorset, England
2 CONT Plot  Buried under the wall of the chancel
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/258181930/cuthburga-of_wimborne
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth date approx. Saint Cuthburga (also Cuthburh or Cuthburg) was the first Abbess of Wimborne Minster. She was also Queen Consort of Northumbria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cuthburga was the sister of Ine, King of Wessex and was married to the Northumbrian King Aldfrith. She was the daughter of Cenred of Wessex. In addition to her brother Ine, she also had a brother Ingild and a sister Cwenburh. Her 
2 CONC marriage to Aldfrith allied him with Ine, one of the most powerful Kings in Anglo-Saxon England. Cuthburh was Aldfrith's only known wife. Aldfrith had at least two sons, Osred and Offa, it is believed Cuthburh was the mother of Os
2 CONC red. Offa is unconfirmed. It is also believed they were the parents of a daughter Osana, who would later be known as Saint Osana.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cuthburh entered Abbess Hildelith's nunnery at Barking Abbey. After Aldfrith's death, around 705, Cuthburh and Cwenburh established a double-monastery in her brother's kingdom of Wessex, at Wimborne, Dorset. She is described as au
2 CONC stere, and she communicated with prelates through a little hatch in the nunnery at Wimborne.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1558, Wimborne Minster being in need of repair, the guardians of the church wrote to Thomas Cromwell for permission to melt down the silver reliquary containing Cuthburh's head. A few years later, the tower collapsed, so it is 
2 CONC surmised that the reliquary was confiscated to the King's use.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her feast day is 31 August.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuthburga
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Cuthburga or Cuthburg (died c. 718) was the first abbess of Wimborne Minster. She was the sister of Ine, King of Wessex and was married to the Northumbrian king Aldfrith.
2 CONT
