1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ='''Devrail 'Dorothy' Cruachan (MacFiachir) Campbell (1072-1140)'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Born:''' 1072 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ANCESTORS:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of '''Dugald Cruachan''' and [mother unknown]
2 CONT * Sibling(s) unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SPOUSE:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Wife of '''Duncan MacDurine Campbell''' — married [date and location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''DESCENDANTS:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Mother of '''Cailen Campbell'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Died:''' 1140 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BIOGRAPHY:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter to Dugald Cruachan, Thane Over Luchow; mother to Cailen
2 CONT
2 CONT Diorbahil - Dorvail (Dorothy) MacFiachir, dau. of Dugald Cruachan Thane of Over Lochow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Duncan Campbell, son of Archibald (Gillespic) Campbell of Menstrie, Clackmannanshire and Aoife O’Duibhne (dau. of Paul “the Sporran” MacDuibhn (O’Duin) Lord of Lochow, Kings Treasurer and Marion _____ of Man). Duncan Campb
2 CONC ell d. in 1097.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue of Diorbahil - Dorvail (Dorothy) MacFiachir and Duncan Campbell:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. son Cailen (bald good) “Maol Math” Campbell Chief of Clan MacDuine d. in 1110 in Dunstaffnage, Oban, Kilmore, Argyll; m. (1) Eaill _____ neice of King Alexander I, dau. of Edmund _____ Prince of Cumbria (son of Malcolm III ’Can
2 CONC more’ _____ King of Scotland and Margaret ’the Saint’ Atheling); issue (surname Campbell): Gillespic (Archibald) of Lochow (1090–1163); m. (2) dau. of Suibhne Ruadh Swyfyns (or Swaynes) between 1105 and 1107.
2 CONT
2 CONT OTHER NAMES AND INFO: Diorbahil - Dorvail (Dorothy) MacFiachir, dau. of Dugald Cruachan Thane of Over Lochow.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The following information comes from a merged duplicate profile. It is unsourced and may be inaccurate:
2 CONT
2 CONT * MacDurine Duncan Campbell was born in 1070 in Scotland, and died in 1097, also in Scotland. He married Dorothy Dervail Crauchan about 1090 in Scotland. He was the son of Archibald Gillespic Campbell.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter to the Laird of Carrick in Argyllshire, by whom he had three sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Gilmoky of Corearica''', who never married, but had a natural son, ancestor of the MacNaughts, M'Naughtans, or Naughtans, of Lochaber, and other
2 CONT # '''Corcarwa''', ancestor of the MacUilins or rather MacAillins, in Ireland.
2 CONT # '''Duncan Drummanich''', so-called, because he resided beyond Drum-albin, said to be ancestor of the Drummonds in Perthshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/MacFiachir-1]
