2 CONT ='''Cailen Campbell (1090-1120)'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Cailen "Maol Maith (Naith)" Campbell aka 3rd Campbell''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Born:''' 1090 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ANCESTORS:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of '''Duncan MacDurine Campbell''' and '''Devrail Dorothy Cruachan (MacFiachir) Campbell'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [sibling(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SPOUSE (2):'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # Husband of '''Eiall Alexander''' — married [date and location unknown]
2 CONT # Husband of '''Marjory (Rus) Swyfyns''' (1090-1150) — married [date and location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''DESCENDANTS:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Faus Coir Campbell, Iver Croumb Campbell and Archibald Campbell
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Died:''' 1120 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BIOGRAPHY:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Cailen was the child of Gillespic Archibald Campbell and Finvol Fraser. Cailen passed away in 1110.
2 CONT
2 CONT XIX. Cailen Maol Maith, i.e., Bald Good Colin, the 3rd Campbell. He married a niece of Alexander the First, the 90th King of Scotland, by whom he had Gillespie, his heir. By the owner of Castle Sween, in Knapdale's daughter, he ha
2 CONC d two natural sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st. Faus Coir, powerful and warlike, he took most part of Cowall from the Lamonts. Of him the Clan Tavish, such as the famihes of Scanish, Rudale, Dun- arclary, &;c., are descended.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd. IvER Ckoumb, of whom the Maclver Camp- bells of Asknish and theb branches are descended.*
2 CONT
2 CONT Then' mother was taken from Cailen Maol by her father Sweene Kus, and afterwards married to MacLachlan of Dunad, &c. Cailen Maol Maith was appointed Justice -General, also Master of the King's Household and Lord of the Isles, the 
2 CONC rebels from the Western Isles having attacked the King, Alexander the First, in the Castle of Dunstaffnage, where he was slenderly attended. By the brave conduct of the Campbells he escaped. Cailen, who led the attack on them, was
2 CONC  killed with all his retinue while saving his sovereign's life. He died, anno 1110. His son and successor was Sir GiLLESPic, or Sir Archibald Campbell/
2 CONT
2 CONT peeigree given by http://www.clanmactavish.org/documents/campbell_connection.pdf (Gillespig/Archibald4 , Malcolm/Gillecollum3 Oduibhne, Dhuine2 deudgheal, Dhiarmid1 odhuibhne)1
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Campbell-6099
