2 CONC named Fróði in many accounts, noted mainly as the father to the two kings who succeeded him in the rule of Denmark, kings named Hroðgar and Halga in the Old English poem Beowulf and named Hróar and Helgi in Old Norse accounts.
2 CONT
2 CONT His name would in his own language, Proto-Norse, have been *Halbadaniz (Danish on only one side of the family).
