1 NOTE *Aud Ivarsdotter <http://www.mathematical.com/ivarsdotteraud633.html> born Abt 0633 Of Am, Denmark married Abt 0669 Of Denmark
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: Audr Ivarsdottir of_Am (633-) [Pedigree] 
2 CONT Daughter of Ivar Halfdansson King of Lethra (612-) 
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY:        REF Halldor Arnason (harnason@u.washington.edu).
2 CONT        Son means son and is never used for daughters. Daughters have
2 CONT        -dottir instead of -son (or -sdottir instead of -sson, the s          is the genitive ending of the father's name). It is however           quite common to see people not familiar with the patronymic           system, mix t
2 CONC his up.
2 CONT        The name Audr (the r is a nominative case ending that I like          to keep but most people don't) could both be used as a woman's        and a man's name and maybe there is some confusion because of        that.
2 CONT        In later time it became exclusively female.
2 CONT        There is a male Audr in the Norse mythology, but a female one
2 CONT        was one of the settlers of Iceland around 900. She came from
2 CONT        Ireland, so maybe she had an Irish name that sounded somewhat
2 CONT        similar to Audr, so Audr was used for her even though it was
2 CONT        male. I don't know about that, just wondering.
2 CONT        There is a Audr Ivarsdottir mentioned in the poem Hyndluljod          as mother of Haraldr hilditonn Hraereksson and Randver
2 CONT        Radbardsson. That poem is written in Iceland in the twelfth
2 CONT        century, so the poet might not have any better idea of who            Audr was than we do. He even uses the nickname "djupudga"
2 CONT        (deepminded) for her, but that was the nickname of the
2 CONT        Icelandic settler. I don't know who got it from whom.
2 CONT        E-Mail
2 CONT     b. ABT 633
2 CONT     r. Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Married Radbard of Russia King of Garderidge (Russia) (638-) 
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Children: [listed under entry for Radbard of Russia]
2 CONT
