2 CONT He became one of Harald Fairhair's men the summer before the battle at Solskel circa August 866.   He was set as chief over the two districts, North More and Raumsdal, by Harald Fairhair, who strengthened him both with men of migh
2 CONC t and bondes, and gave him the help of ships to defend the coast against enemies in 867.   He was given South Möre to govern as well, following the defeat of King Arnvid by Harald Hairfair, but the Firdafylke still remained in the
2 CONC  possession of King Ardbjorns brother Vemund in 868 [Circa 1225 A.D. Snorri Sturluson, Heimskringla, or The Chronicle of the Kings of Norway (London: Norroena Society, 1907)].
