2 TITL President of the American College for Genealogical Registry and Heraldry statement.pdf
1 NOTE The old vikings had long beards and hair. There came a time whenways began to change and that fashion changed as well. KingHarold Fairhair, first king of Norway was given his name by ourancestor, Earl Rognvald. It happened in this
2 CONC  way: King Haroldwas at a feast at Rognvald's holding at More and prepared for itby having a bath and having his long hair washed. Earl Rognvaldcut his hair which had been uncut and uncombed for 10 years andhad caused his name "Lu
2 CONC fa" or "Rough Matted Hair". Suchbeautiful, abundant, fair hair was revealed after the washingthat Rognvald gave him the name "Harold Harfager" (HaroldFairhair). All present agreed. This was described in theHiemskringla by Snorri S
2 CONC turleson. The great story of the kingsof Norway.
1 NOTE Ble norsk høvding i år 900 over Mørefylkene.
1 NOTE Rollo, also called ROLF, or ROU, French ROLLON (b. c. 860--d. c. 932),Scandinavian rover who founded the duchy of Normandie.
2 CONT Making himself independent of King Harald I of Norway, Rollo sailed offto raid Scotland, England, Flanders, and France on pirating expeditionsand, about 911, established himself in an area along the Seine River.Charles III the Sim
2 CONC ple of France held off his siege of Paris, battled himnear Chartres, and negotiated the treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte, givinghim the part of Neustria that came to be called Normandie; Rollo inreturn agreed to end his brigandage. 
2 CONC He gave his son, William ILongsword, governance of the dukedom (927) before his death. Rollo wasbaptized in 912 but is said to have died a pagan. [EncyclopaediaBritannica CD, 1997, ROLLO]Ancestral File Number:<AFN> FLGS-2R
