1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Brusi Sigurdsson, Earl of Orkney==
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.friesian.com/germania.htm#orkney
2 CONT
2 CONT Jarl på Orknøy, sønn av Sigurd II Digre. Earl of Orkney Islands. På norrønt Brusi Sigurdsson, fornavnet i moderne tid fornorsket til Bruse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earl_of_Orkney#Norse_Earls_of_Orkney
2 CONT
2 CONT Brusi Sigurdsson (died 1030-1035) was one of Sigurd Hlodvirsson's four sons (together with Thorfinn, Einar and Sumarlidi). He was jointly Earl of Orkney from 1014. His life is recorded in the Orkneyinga Saga.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Earl Sigurd was killed at the Battle of Clontarf, he left four sons: Brusi, Sumarlidi, Einar and Thorfinn. Thorfinn was only a child, whereas his three brothers were grown men, so the Earldom was divided between the three old
2 CONC er brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sumarlidi died soon after, and Einar, called Wry-Mouth (Rangmunn), took his share, ruling two-thirds of the Earldom and leaving a third for Brusi. Einar soon became unpopular, demanding heavy taxes and frequent military service fr
2 CONC om the farmers, and gaining little booty on his raids. He was, the saga says, "a great bully", whereas Brusi was "gentle, restrained, unassuming and a fine speaker" and "well-liked by everyone".
2 CONT
2 CONT Brusi had to make peace between Einar and Thorfinn when the youngest brother grew to manhood, not once but twice. In the end, Einar plotted Thorfinn's death but was found out and killed by Thorfinn. The agreement made with Einar m
2 CONC eant that Brusi inherited another third of the earldom on Einar's death, leaving Thorfinn with one part of the earldom, Brusi with two. Thorfinn was not pleased with this arrangement, and asked Brusi for a half share. This Brusi r
2 CONC efused. However, while Thorfinn could count on the aid of his maternal grandfather, Máel Coluim mac Cináeda, Brusi could rely only on his own resources.
2 CONT
2 CONT To find support Brusi went to Norway, to the court of King Olaf Haraldsson, to have the sharing out of the Earldom settled, and Thorfinn followed him there. Olaf kept Einar's share for himself, appointing Brusi to administer it, a
2 CONC nd kept Brusi's son Rognvald at his court. Brusi later gave Thorfinn the disputed third of the islands in return for Thorfinn seeing to the defence of Orkney and Shetland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brusi died before 1035 as the saga says he had died before his son Rognvald accompanied Magnus the Good back to Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#SigurdDigridied1014A
