2 CONC h”, adding that he left them “in charge of the earldom” when he left for Ireland and that they divided the earldom between them after he was killed[866].  Snorre names "Sumarlide, Bruse and Einar Rangmund" as "older sons" of "Sigu
2 CONC rd the Thick", recording that they succeeded on the death of their father when the country was divided into three parts[867].  He succeeded his father 1014 as Jarl of 1/3 Orkney.  Orkneyinga Saga records that Somerled “had the sho
