1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==concerns==
2 CONT '''This Thorfinn is the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Thorfnn-The-Black-Sigurdsson-Orkenoyene/6000000059316432961.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography==
2 CONT Thorfinn (1009?–-c1064?), called Thorfinn the Mighty, was Earl of Orkney. Son of Earl Sigurd Hlodvirsson by his marriage to the daughter of Malcolm II of Scotland. He married Ingibiorg Finnsdottir, daughter of Finn Arnesson, Jarl 
2 CONC of Halland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Heimskringla of Icelandic historian Snorri Sturluson, and the anonymous compiler of the Orkneyinga Saga, write that Thorfinn was the most powerful of all the earls of Orkney. He is said to have been earl for seventy-five years
2 CONC  and ruler of nine earldoms in Scotland, of the Hebrides, and of part of Ireland. A sizable part of the account in the Orkneyinga Saga concerns his wars with a "King of Scots" named Karl Hundason whose identity is very uncertain.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thorfinn_Sigurdsson
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/KFPX-KY8
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT Thorfinn was certainly out of the picture by 1066, perhaps even before 1057. When and under what circumstances he died is unknown, suggesting illness rather than anything more dramatic.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#SigurdDigridied1014A
2 CONT
2 CONT SIGURD "Digri/the Stout", son of [HLODVIR Torfinnsson Jarl of Orkney & his wife Eithne of Ireland] ([965/70]-killed in battle Clontarf 23 Apr 1014). 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([1005 or after]) --- of Scotland, daughter of MALCOLM II King of Scotland & his wife ---. Orkneyinga Saga records that “Earl Sigurd” married “the daughter of Malcolm King of Scots” (whose succession is recorded in 1005)[240]. S
2 CONC norre records the marriage of "Sigurd the Thick" and "a daughter of the Scottish king Malcolm"[241]. It appears unlikely that Sigurd´s wife could have been King Malcolm´s daughter Donada (as shown in many secondary sources, includ
2 CONC ing the Complete Peerage[242]) if it is correct that Donada´s recorded husband Findlaech was killed in 1020 and that their son was born in [1005][243].
2 CONT
2 CONT ===On the question of whether Sigurd married a 3rd daughter of Malcolm II, or whether he married Donalda before the death of her first husband, Findlaech in 1020 [http://www.geni.com/discussions/115687  See Discussion]
2 CONT [Med Lands' above explanation for the 'daughter of Malcolm not likely to have been taken from her first husband, Findlaech before his death in 1020 is not a strong argument in my opinion, given that Findlaech and Sigurd were old a
2 CONC dversaries - (Sigurd beating Findlaech at Skidamoor c 995).  Malcolm's kingship in 1005, perhaps made his daughter a greater prize than the beaten enemy of Sigurd warranted. It is possible to conjecture that Sigurd's neutrality or
2 CONC  assistance might have been crucial for Malcolm to beat off the Vikings at Nairn and Mortlach in 1009/10 - something Findlaech had failed to do on his own, and Donalda was 'transferred' in that exchange. Thorfinn's birth (the saga
2 CONC s tell us he was 5yrs old when Sigurd dies in 1014) coincides perfectly with this timing. Although, this doesn't prove there wasn't another daughter;  secondary sources do put Thorfinn's parents as Donada & Sigurd. But, as Anne Be
2 CONC rge has pointed out - it is more typical for sources to 'forget' a person than a conflate two people.  - Sharon]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigurd & his second wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. THORFINN "the Black" ([1009]-[1060/65], bur Birsay, Christchurch). Orkneyinga Saga names “Earl Thorfinn” as the son of Sigurd and his wife “the daughter of Malcolm King of Scots”, adding that his father sent him to Scotland “to
2 CONC  be fostered by the King, the boy´s maternal grandfather” when he left for Ireland, and that he was five years old when his father was killed[264]. Snorre names Thorfin as son of "Sigurd the Thick" & his wife, recording that he wa
2 CONC s five years old when his father was killed[265]. He succeeded [1030] as sole Jarl of Orkney. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "After Torf-Einar, his sons Arnkel, Erlend, and Thorfin Hausakljufer (Skull-Splinter) ruled over these lands. In their days came Eirik Blood-axe from Norway, and subdued these earls. Arnkel and Erlend fell in a war expedition; but
2 CONC  Thorfin ruled the country long, and became an old man. His sons were Arnfin, Havard, Hlodver, Liot, and Skule. Their mother was Grelad, a daughter of Earl Dungad of Caithness. Her mother was Groa, a daughter of Thorstein Raud. In
2 CONC  the latter days of Earl Thorfin came Eirik Blood-axe's sons, who had fled from Earl Hakon out of Norway, and committed great excesses in Orkney. Earl Thorfin died on a bed of sickness, and his sons after him ruled over the countr
2 CONC y, and there are many stories concerning them. Hlodver lived the longest of them, and ruled alone over this country. His son was Sigurd the Thick, who took the earldom after him, and became a powerful man and a great warrior. In h
2 CONC is days came Olaf Trygvason from his viking expedition in the western ocean, with his troops, landed in Orkney and took Earl Sigurd prisoner in South Ronaldsha, where he lay with one ship. King Olaf allowed the earl to ransom his 
2 CONC life by letting himself be baptized, adopting the true faith, becoming his man, and introducing Christianity into all the Orkney Islands. As a hostage, King Olaf took his son, who was called Hunde or Whelp. Then Olaf went to Norwa
2 CONC y, and became king; and Hunde was several years with King Olaf in Norway, and died there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death Earl Sigurd showed no obedience or fealty to King Olaf. He married a daughter of the Scottish king Malcolm, and their son was called Thorfin. Earl Sigurd had, besides, older sons; namely, Sumarlide, Bruse, and Eina
2 CONC r Rangmund. Four or five years after Olaf Tryggvason's fall Earl Sigurd went to Ireland, leaving his eldest sons to rule the country, and sending Thorfin to his mother's father, the Scottish king. On this expedition Earl Sigurd fe
2 CONC ll in Brian's battle (l). When the news was received in Orkney, the brothers Sumarlide, Bruse, and Einar were chosen earls, and the country was divided into three parts among them. Thorfin Sigurdson was five years old when Earl Si
2 CONC gurd fell. When the Scottish king heard of the earl's death he gave his relation Thorfin Caithness and Sutherland, with the title of earl, and appointed good men to rule the land for him. Earl Thorfin was ripe in all ways as soon 
2 CONC as he was grown up: he was stout and strong, but ugly; and as soon as he was a grown man it was easy to see that he was a severe and cruel but a very clever man."
2 CONT
2 CONT from Heimskringla, "The Saga of St Olav" by Snorri Sturlusson
2 CONT
2 CONT http://lind.no/nor/index.asp?lang=gb&emne=asatru&vis=s_e_olav_haraldsson
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Torfinn Sigurdsson Rike
2 CONT
2 CONT Fra Wikipedia, den frie encyklopedi
2 CONT
2 CONT Torfinn Sigurdsson Rike (ca 1000 - ca 1065) var jarl på Orknøyene, og regnes som en av de mest energiske jarlene i øygruppas historie. Torfinn bodde trolig flere steder, men til sist på Birsay på nordvestre Mainland, hvor han også
2 CONC  lot bygge en kirke og fikk anlagt et bispesete.
2 CONT
2 CONT Torfinn var sønn av jarl Sigurd Lodvesson Digre og Bethoc av Skottland, datter av den skotske kongen Malcolm II. Han var gift med Ingebjørg Finnsdatter, datter av Finn Arnesson. Sammen med Ingebjørg hadde han sønnene Pål og Erlend
2 CONC , og han var farfar til den hellige Magnus Orknøyjarl og Håkon Pålsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT I følge sagaen fikk Torfinn Caithness (Katanes) som jarledømme etter sin morfar. Da faren Sigurd døde i 1014 ble jarledrømmet på Orknøyene delt mellom Torfinns (halv)brødre Sumarlide, Einar Vrangmunn og Bruse. Denne delingen ble b
2 CONC egrunnet med at Torfinn allerede hadde Caithness. Torfinns krig med sine brødre pågikk fra 1018 (da Sumarlide døde, og Torfinn tok kontroll over hans tredjedel), til 1046, da Torfinn ble enejarl. Einar Vrangmunn ble ryddet av veie
2 CONC n i 1020, og Bruse døde i 1034. Torfinns brorsønn Ragnvald Bruseson var samjarl med Torfinn fra sist i 30-åra til Torfinn drepte ham i 1046.
2 CONT
2 CONT Som enejarl rådde Torfinn over et område «fra Tussaskjær (på Shetland) til Dublin», med Arnor Jarleskalds ord. Torfinn arbeidet aktivt for å holde dette riket samlet. Siden kong Olav II i 1021 skapte (midlertidig) fred mellom Torf
2 CONC inn og Bruse, hadde den norske kongen styrket sitt grep om jarldømmet på Orknøyene og de andre vesterhavsøyene. Torfinn hadde for sin del en dobbel lojalitet, i og med at han som jarl av Caithness også sto under den skotske kongen
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Torfinn besøkte Norge i 1047 da Harald Hardråde hadde blitt enekonge. Senere, ca 1049/1950, reiste Torfinn i følge sagaen gjennom Europa fra Danmark til Roma, hvor han besøkte paven, trolig Leo IX, og fikk syndsforlatelse. Det må 
2 CONC ha vært etter dette at han lot bygge en kirke på Birsay.
2 CONT
2 CONT I følge sagaen ble Torfinn mindre av en hærkonge, og mer av en lovbygger etter Roma-ferden.
2 CONT
2 CONT [rediger] Litteratur
2 CONT
2 CONT Narve Bjørgo. «Torfinn Sigurdsson Rike». I: Norsk biografisk leksikon, 2. utg., bd 9. 2005 
2 CONT
2 CONT Orknøyingenes saga: - nettutgave 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hentet fra «http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torfinn_Sigurdsson_Rike»
2 CONT
2 CONT http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torfinn_Sigurdsson_Rike
