2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson, King Olaf Trygvason's Saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "60. OF THE HORDALAND PEOPLE.
2 CONT ... In Hordaland, however, were many bold and great men of Hordakare's race. He, namely, had left four sons, -- the first Thorleif Spake; the second, Ogmund, father of Thorolf Skialg, who was father of Erling of Sole; the third wa
2 CONC s Thord father of the Herse Klyp who killed King Sigurd Slefa, Gunhild's son; and lastly, Olmod, father of Askel, whose son was Aslak Fitjaskalle; and that family branch was the greatest and most considered in Hordaland. ..."
