2 CONC ga names “Paul and…Erlend” as the two sons of Jarl [http://www.geni.com/people/Thorfinn-Sigurdsson/6000000001052002306 THORFINN II]  and his wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Ingibj%C3%B6rg-Finnsd%C3%B3ttir/6000000001052011900 Ingi
2 CONC björg] who survived childhood[902].  He succeeded his father in [1065] as Joint Jarl of Orkney, jointly with his brother.  Morkinskinna records that Harald III King of Norway sailed to Orkney en route for his invasion of England i
2 CONC n 1066 and “recruited the aid of Jarl Thorfinn´s sons Páll and Erlendr”[903].  Orkneyinga Saga records that Magnus "Barelegs" King of Norway “seized the Earls, Paul and Erlend” on his arrival in Orkney, “sent them east to Norway, 
2 CONC and made his own son Sigurd overlord of the islands with regents to govern the earldom”, adding in a later passage that Erlend “had died and been buried at Trondheim”[904].  He was deposed and imprisoned in 1098 by [http://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/people/Magnus-III-Olavsson-%C2%ABBarefoot%C2%BB-Berrf%C3%B8tt/5381202464070053447  Magnus "Barelegs]" King of Norway, and "died of sickness at Nidaros and is buried there" according to Snorre[905].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/M
