1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.geni.com/people/Domnall-mac-Gilla-P%C3%A1traic-king-of-Osraige/6000000079398749024?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529326625341&through=6000000079398749024  DOMNALL] (-1087).  King of Ossory.  The Annals of 
2 CONC Inisfallen record that "Domnall Ua Gilla Pátraic submitted to Tiadelbach Ua Briain and received a very large stipend of valuables and riches from the king of Mumu” in 1070[739].  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "the son of Co
2 CONC nchobair Ua Mail Sechnaill (king of Temuir), Gofraid grandson of Ragnall king of Áth Cliath, and Domnall son of Gilla Pátraic king of Osraige…submitted to Tairdelbach Ua Briain king of Mum” in 1072 and “gave acknowledgement and hi
2 CONC gh-kingship to him”[740].  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1087 of "Domnall mac Gilla Pátraic king of Osraige”[741].  m ---.  The name of Domnall´s wife is not known.  Domnall & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>(a)       [https://www.geni.com/people/Donnchad-mac-Domnall/6000000079398731078?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529326625341&through=6000000079398731078  DONNCHAD] (-killed 1090).  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 109
2 CONC 0 of "Donnchadh son of Domnall Ua Gilla Pátraic…slain”[742]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>(b)       MUIRCHERTACH (-1095).  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 1095 of "Muirchertach son of Domnall son of Gilla Pátraic, royal heir of Osraige”[743]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>(c)      ''' [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079398950962?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529326625341&through=6000000079398950962  GILLA PATRAIC] “Ruad/Red” (-killed in battle Mag Coba, Ulster 1103).  The primary sour
2 CONC ce which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   King of Ossory.  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "Gilla Pátraic Ruad king of Osraige” was killed in 1103 at “the battle of Mag Coba”[744].]  m ---.  The name of G
2 CONC illa Patraic´s wife is not known.  Gilla Patraic & his wife had one child:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>(1)       DONNCHAD (-killed 1123).  King of Ossory.  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "Tadc son of Mac Carthaig accompanied by the Desmumu went to Osraige” and “Ua Gilla Pátraic king of Osraige submitted to him”, addin
2 CONC g that “the nobles of Osraige including their king were imprisoned by the Dál Cais”[745].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Donncadh Húa Gilla Padraic king of Ossory” was killed in 1123[746].  The Annals of Inis
2 CONC fallen record the death in 1123 of "the son of Gilla Pátraic, king of Osraige…slain by his own people”[747]. 
2 CONT
