1 OCCU King of Munster
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DIARMAIT (-Corcach Mór Muman 1118).  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "Diarmait Ua Briain brought a fleet to Wales and took great spoil therefrom” in 1080[939].  The Annals of Inisfallen record that, on the dea
2 CONC th of Tordelbach in 1086, Munster "was divided in three between [his] three sons…Tadc, Muirchertach and Diarmait”, but adding that Diarmait “was banished from Mumu” in 1086 after the death of his brother Tadhg, when his brother Mu
2 CONC irchertach “took the kingship”[940].  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "Diarmait Ua Briain was banished to Ulaid” in 1092[941].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Diarmait Húa Bríáin” seized the kingdom of Mu
2 CONC nster in 1114 when “Muirchertach Húa Bríáin” fell ill[942].  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "Diarmait Ua Briain took the kingship of Mumu and banished Muirchertach from Luimnech to Cell Da Lua” in 1114, but in a later passag
2 CONC e records that “Muirchertach came to Luimnech and Diarmait was imprisoned by him” in 1115[943].  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "Diarmait Ua Briain turned against Muirchertach Ua Briain” in 1116 and that “Muirchertach Ua Bri
2 CONC ain went to Les Mór and assumed the pilgrim´s staff”[944].  King of Munster 1116.  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Diarmuit Húa Bríáin king of the southern half of Ireland [Lethe Mogha]” died in 1118[945].  The
2 CONC  Annals of Inisfallen record that "Diarmait Ua Briain died in Corcach Mór Muman” in 1118[946].  m ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Diarmait´s wife is not known.  Diarmait & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)             CONCHOBAR (-1142).  King of Munster.  
2 CONT
2 CONT b)             TORDELBACH (-1167).  King of Munster. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)             TADHG (-1167).  King of Thomond 1122. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT King of Munster
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diarmait_Ua_Briain Diarmait Ua Briain (Wikipedia)]
