2 CONT Lafracoth Princess of Ireland ingen Muiredaig de Montgomery (born Ó Briain), 1076-1135 Lafracoth Princess of Ireland ingen Muiredaig de Montgomery (born Ó Briain) was born in 1076, at birth place, to Muirchertach mac Toirdelbach M
2 CONC or Ua Briain High King of Ireland and Ua Briain (born Murrough). Muirchertach was born circa 1050, in Munster, Ireland. Lafracoth had 8 siblings: Donnhadh King Of Leinster, Moy O'Brien and 6 other siblings. Lafracoth married Arnou
2 CONC ld Cimbricus de Montgomery circa 1103, at age 27. Arnould was born circa 1066, in Montgomery, Normandie, France. His occupation was Earl of Pembroke. They had 6 children: Philip Montgomery Sir, Unknown de Montgomery and 4 other ch
2 CONC ildren. Lafracoth passed away in 1135, at age 59 at death place. She was buried at burial place.www.wikitree.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Lafracoth de Montgomery formerly O'Brien Born 1076 in Tipperary, Clare, Irelandmap
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Muichertach macToirdelbach Mor O'Brien and [mother unknown] Sister of Domnall OBrian Dublin [half], Blathmin (O'Brien) Ireland [half] and Mathgamain (Corcobaskin) O'Brien [half] Wife of Arnoulf (Montgomery) de Montgome
2 CONC ry — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Philip (Montgomerie) Montgomery and Alice (Montgomerie) de Montgomery Died 1119 in Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile manager: Harry Boswell Profile last modified 12 Apr 2019  Created 20 May 2011 .
2 CONT Biography Lafracoth ingen Muiredaig Ó Briain was the daughter of the king of Munster. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lafracoth O'Brien is the daughter of Murrough O'Brien, King of Munster. She married Arnolph de Montgomery; their child Alice de Montgomery married Maurice fitz Gerald (son of Gerald fitz Walter and Nesta, Princess of Deheubarth) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source Cork Past and Present The Peerage #335172 : Lafracoth O'Brien
