1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Cináed mac Duib''' (Modern Gaelic: Coinneach mac Dhuibh)[1] anglicised as Kenneth III, and nicknamed '''An Donn''', "the Chief" or "the Brown",[2] (before 967–25 March 1005) was King of Scots from 997 to 1005. H
2 CONC e was the son of Dub (Dub mac Maíl Coluim). Many of the Scots sources refer to him as Giric son of Kenneth son of Dub, which is taken to be an error.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Three children, mother's name unknown:
2 CONT * Giric
2 CONT * Gillacomgain
2 CONT * Boite
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources and Resoures==
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/MacAlpin-19
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenneth_III_of_Scotland
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Medieval Lands==
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Kenneth-III-Mac-Duibh-king-of-Scots/4659985?through=6000000003219779698 '''KENNETH'''], son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Dubh-mac-M%C3%A1el-Coluim-King-of-Scots/6000000000202034309?through=4659985 D
2 CONC UFF] King of Scotland & his wife --- (-killed in battle Monzievaird [25 Mar 1005]).  The 11th century Synchronisms of Flann Mainistreach name (in order) "…Cuillen mac Illiulb, Cinaet mac Maelcolaim, Custantin mac Cuilen, Cinaet ma
2 CONC c Duib, Maelcolaim mac Cinaeta" as Scottish kings, dated to the 10th and 11th centuries[208].  The 12th century Cronica Regum Scottorum lists "…Chinet filius Duf i anno et dimidium…" as king[209].  He succeeded in 997 as KENNETH I
2 CONC II King of Scotland.  The Annals of Ulster record that "the king of the Albu Cinaed son of Dub" was killed in battle "between the men of Albu themselves" in 1005[210]. m ---.  The name of Kenneth's wife is not known. Kenneth III &
2 CONC  his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Giric-II-mac-Cin%C3%A1eda-King-of-Scots/6000000003615429242?through=4659985 GREG] [Giric] (-killed in battle Monzievaird [25 Mar 1005], bur Isle of Iona).  The Chronicle of the Picts and Sc
2 CONC ots dated 1251 records that "Girus mac Kinath mac Duff" reigned for 8 years, was killed "a filio Kinet in Moeghauard" and was buried at Iona[211].  The Chronicle of the Picts and Scots dated 1317 includes the same information[212]
2 CONC .  His existence is not recorded in any of the earlier chronicles and should be treated with caution.  The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that King Kenneth II decreed a change to the Scottish royal succession to enable "the n
2 CONC earest survivor in blood to the deceased king to succeed", in opposition to "Constantine the Bald, son of King Culen, and Gryme son of Kenneth son of King Duff"[213].  The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that "Gryme the son of
2 CONC  Kenneth son of Duff" succeeded in 996 after King Constantine III was killed and reigned for eight years and three months[214].  The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that Grime was killed by Malcolm, son of King Kenneth II, add
2 CONC ing that the latter arranged his burial at Iona[215].] 
2 CONT
2 CONT >2.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Gille-Coemg%C3%A1in-mac-Cin%C3%A1eda/6000000002278167864?through=4659985 GILLACOMGAIN] (-killed in battle 999).  His parentage is confirmed by the Annals of Ulster which record that "Cathal
2 CONC  son of Amalgaid, king of Western Laigin, and his wife, the daughter of the son of Gilla Caemgein son of Cinaed, and his hound were killed at the same time by the son of Cellach son of Dúnchad"[216].  m ---.  The name of Gillacomg
2 CONC ain's wife is not known.  Gillacomgain & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>a)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Son-of-Gille-Coemg%C3%A1in/6000000038367237855?through=6000000002278167864 son] . 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>i)          [https://www.geni.com/people/Granddaughter-of-Gille-Coemg%C3%A1in/6000000038367026259?through=6000000038367237855 daughter] (-murdered 1035).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >3.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Boedhe-mac-Cin%C3%A1eda/6000000003219779698 BOITE] [Bodhe] (-before 1033).  His parentage is confirmed by the Annals of Ulster which record that "the grandson of Baete son of Cinead was kil
2 CONC led by Mael Coluim son of Cinaed" in 1033[219].  m ---.  The name of Boite's wife is not known.  Boite & his wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT >>a)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Gille-Mac-Boede/6000000038365613707?through=6000000003219779698  GILLE] .  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>i)         [https://www.geni.com/people/NN/6000000038367150065?through=6000000038365613707 son] (-murdered in infancy 1033).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>b)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Gruoch-Lady-MacBeth/6000000004533031237?through=6000000003219779698 GRUOCH] ([1015]-).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>i)          [https://www.geni.com/people/Lulach-mac-Gille-Coemg%C3%A1in-King-of-Scots/6000000000307274746?through=6000000004533031237 LULACH] ([1032]-killed in battle Essie, Strathbogie 17 Mar 1058, bur Isle of Iona).  
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#_Toc209085741
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The only event reported in Kenneth's reign is the killing of Dúngal mac Cináeda by Gille Coemgáin mac Cináeda, by the Annals of the Four Masters s.a. 999. It is not certain that this refers to events in Scotland, and whether one o
2 CONC r both were sons of this Kenneth, or of Kenneth II of Scotland, or some other person or persons, is not known.[4] Kenneth was killed in battle at Monzievaird in Strathearn by Malcolm II (Máel Coluim mac Cináeda) in 1005.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Whether Boite mac Cináeda was a son of this Kenneth, or of Kenneth II, is uncertain, although most propose this Kenneth. A son, or grandson of Boite, was reported to be killed by Malcolm II in 1032 in the Annals of Ulster.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth's granddaughter, Gruoch daughter of Boite (Gruoch ingen Boite meic Cináeda) — Shakespeare's Lady Macbeth — was wife firstly of Gille Coemgáin, Mormaer of Moray, and secondly of King Macbeth; her son by Gille Coemgáin, Lula
2 CONC ch (Lulach mac Gille Coemgáin), would briefly succeed Macbeth as King of Scotland. The meic Uilleim, descendants of William fitz Duncan by his first marriage, were probably descended from Kenneth; and the Clann Mac Aoidh or Clan M
2 CONC ackay claim descent from Kenneth III through Lulach's daughter.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. ^ Cináed mac Duib is the Mediaeval Gaelic form.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. ^ The former is probable because later English-speaking sources called him "Grim"; Old Irish donn has similar meaning to Old English greimm, which means "power" or "authority"; see Skene, Chronicles, p. 98; Hudson, Celtic Ki
2 CONC ngs, p. 105.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. ^ Duncan, p. 22; Smyth, pp. 220–221 and 225, prefers to assume that Kenneth had a son, Giric, who ruled jointly with his father; also ESSH, p.522, note 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. ^ ESSH, p.520, note 5; Smyth, pp. 221–222, makes Gille Coemgáin the son of this Kenneth following ESSH, p. 580.
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. ^ Annals of Ulster and Chronicon Scotorum, s.a. 1005; the various versions of the Chronicle of the Kings of Alba and the Prophecy of Berchán agree on the site of the battle; ESSH, pp 522–524. Duncan, p. 22, suggests that the
2 CONC  killer's name should be read as Giric mac Cináeda, "Giric son of Kenneth", a brother of Malcolm. If not, this Giric was presumably also killed at about this time.
2 CONT
2 CONT    6. ^ This Cináed and Boite's son, Smyth, pp. 220–221; Duncan, p. 32. See also ESSH, p. 571, note 7.
2 CONT
2 CONT    7. ^ Duncan, pp. 102–103.
2 CONT
