1 NOTE "ALPIN"; KING OF SCOTLAND 997-1005; KILLED AT MONZIEVAIRD BY MALCOLM II
1 NOTE Murdered by Malcolm II, King of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth III of Scotland
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth III (Cináed mac Duib) was King of Scots from 997 to 1005. He wasthe son of King Dubh, fourth cousin of the previous king Constantine III,and first cousin of his successor Malcolm II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth was the last king of Scotland to succeed to the throne throughthe system of tanistry, whereby the succession was shared between twofamily lines and the dying king named the person from the other familyline who was to succe
2 CONC ed him. The system was much discredited as itensured that the two royal families of the Kingdom of Scotland were in aconstant state of war with each other.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth and his son Giric were both killed in the Battle of Monzievaird,Tayside on March 25, 1005. It was his first cousin Malcolm, succeedinghim at the battle, who abolished the tanistry system by killing all ofKenneth's male des
2 CONC cendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, Kenneth had a granddaughter, Gruoch, via his son Bodhe. Gruoch'sfirst husband was Gillacomgain, Mormaer of Moray. They had a son calledLulach. She then married King Macbeth of Scotland (becoming LadyMacbeth). On the death
2 CONC  of Macbeth, her son via her first marriage(Kenneth III's great-grandson), succeeded to the throne, becoming KingLulach of Scotland.
1 NOTE He ruled from 997 to 1005.
1 NOTE He ruled from 997 to 1005.
