1 NOTE From THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry,  chart pg 45.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 44:
2 CONT
2 CONT 19.     Malcolm II MacKenneth, murdered 25 Nov. 1034; King of Scots from 25 March 1005.  In 1008 at Carham, Northumbria, with the help of Uchtred, Earl of Northumbria, won the rich wheatlands of Bernicia from King Canute, uniting 
2 CONC the four Kingdoms into the geographical Scotland of today; overcame the Danes 1017; published a code of laws 1018; succeeded in having his grandson Duncan appointed King of Strathclyde and Cumbria.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amie, Adam and FAL
