1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gregor Garbh, or the Stout, designated of Glenurchay, a man of martial spirit and great renown in Malcolm’s time. He also fought under King Duncan I. against the Normans and Danes, inter 1035 and 1040, and promoted
2 CONC  the restoration of his son, Malcolm III. He married a daughter5 of the ancient house of Lochow,6 by whom he had two sons—
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.   Sir John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.   Gregorious, or Gregor, bred to the church, ‘obiit electus episcopus St Andria.’
