2 CONT Diarmuid Mac Murchadha (later known as Diarmaid na nGall or "Dermot of the Foreigners"), anglicized as Dermot MacMurrough, was a King of Leinster in Ireland. Ousted as King of Leinster in 1166, he sought military assistance from K
2 CONC ing Henry II of England to retake his kingdom. In return, Diarmuid pledged an oath of allegiance to Henry, who sent troops in support. As a further thanks for his reinstatement, Diarmuid's daughter Aoife was married to Richard de 
