2 CONT Owain Gwynedd , d. 1170, prince of North Wales (1137-70). During the troubled reign of King Stephen of England, Owain and other Welsh princes were able to reoccupy much territory earlier wrested from them by the Anglo-Normans. Hen
2 CONC ry II of England invaded North Wales in 1157 and, though his expedition was a military failure, compelled Owain to do homage. In 1165, however, Owain inspired a general Welsh revolt, and the English army that attempted to quell it
2 CONC  was forced to turn back because of bad weather and short supplies. Owain continued to expand his possessions and enjoyed independence until his death.
2 CONT
