1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Frodi "the Valiant" Fridleifsson, legendary king of Denmark. Fourth of that name according to the layout in "Hversum Noreg Byggdist".
2 CONT
2 CONT == Basics ==
2 CONT * Father: Fridleif III
2 CONT * Mother: Unknown
2 CONT * Wife: Unknown, many suggestions in Geni
2 CONT ** Son: Ingjald Starkadsfostre (according to "Hversum Noreg Byggdist" first list)
2 CONT ** Son: Halfdan Frodasson (according to "Hversum Noreg Byggdist" second list)
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT See [http://wiki.geni.com/index.php?title=Skjoldungene the Wiki] for details of sourcing of the above.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other notes ==
2 CONT This rather coherent piece is given without a source:
2 CONT
2 CONT Som søn af en voldtaget kvinde mentes Åle ikke egnet til tronarving; derfor overtog Frode magten efter sin fader. Men Åle blev viking; på grund af sit held i den håndtering fik han (til)navnet Åle hinn fræckne. Frode begyndte også
2 CONC  at blive berømt for sine mange bedrifter og blev kald den Store eller Berømte. Han havde sit kongesæde i Lejre og Ringsted. Ligesom sin fader oprettede han en hird, hvor han underholdt adskillige krigere med kæmpekræfter, og i sp
2 CONC idsen for dem satte han Starkad. Han havde også tolv jarler under sig.
2 CONT
2 CONT Åle, der var Frodes halvbroder, erobrede nu ved en modig krigerisk indsats kongemagten i Sverige 
2 CONT
2 CONT Efter å ha sørget for drapet på sin halvbror Åle, besejrede kong Frode svenskekongen Jørund og gjorde ham skatskyldig; på samme måde gik det en svensk jarl ved navn Sverting. Frode bortførte også svenskekongens datter, med hvem ha
2 CONC n fik sønnen Halfdan. Hun var hans elskerinde. Senere giftede han sig og fik med denne kvinde en ægtefødt arving, sønnen Ingjald. Frodes søn Ingjald giftede sig med en datter af den førnævnte Sverting Jarl, efter alles mening for 
2 CONC at gøre ham mere samarbejdsvillig.
2 CONT
2 CONT fikk sønnene:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hálfdán Fródason ~503
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Frodi Frodasson ~505
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Ingjald Fródason ~501
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Frode IV Fridleifsson, King of the Danes
2 CONT
2 CONT Frode IV Fridleifsson, King of the Danes||p111.htm#i13320|Fridleif III Fordisson, King of the Danes||p111.htm#i13321||||Frode III "the Pacific" Dansson, King of the Danes|b. c 433\nd. 310|p285.htm#i13322||||||||||
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Fridleif III Fordisson, King of the Danes1,2
2 CONT
2 CONT      Frode IV Fridleifsson, King of the Danes was the son of Fridleif III Fordisson, King of the Danes.1,2 King of the Danes at Denmark before 407.3 Frode IV Fridleifsson, King of the Danes died in 407.4 He was the predecessor of 
2 CONC Ingild, King of the Danes; King of the Danes.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hálfdan II Frodasson, King of the Danes+ d. 5805
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Ingild, King of the Danes d. 4364
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. [S278] DfAdam, online unknown url, The Line of Skjöld, King of Danes, 66.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, RfC, 324-51.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. [S261] Regnal Chronologies, online http://www.hostkingdom.net/regindex.html, Scandanavia, Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. [S277] Gene Gurney, Kingdoms of Europe, pg. 430, Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. [S278] DfAdam, online unknown url, The Line of Skjöld, King of Danes, 67.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Frode - ruled Denmark at an uncertain date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another legendary descendant of Odin in Denmark was Frode, who is said to have made vassals of 225 other kings, thus extending his dominions from Russia to the Rhine. Frode, too, was beset with relatives who wished to take away hi
2 CONC s kingdom. One of these was Ubbe, who had married Frode's sister Ulfhild. While Frode was fighting wars in Russia and Ruthenia, Ubbe usurped the throne. Frode was forced to return to Denmark to reclaim his crown. He captured his b
2 CONC rother-in-law Ubbe, took Ulfhild away from him, and wedded her to another man. [Royal Families of Medieval Scandinavia, Flanders, and Kiev]
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: Royal Families of Medieval Scandinavia, Flanders, and Kiev, by Rupert Alen & Anna Dahlquist, 1997, King's River Publ. Page: 75
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Early legendary kings of Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Note: Frode - ruled Denmark at an uncertain date.
2 CONT
