2 CONT == Synopsis ==
2 CONT Ráðbarðr, Raðbarðr or Rathbarth (late 7th century) was a legendary king of Garðaríki (Russia), Swedish name Gårdarike (land of the farms) , who appears in ''Sögubrot'' and the ''Lay of Hyndla''. He appears to be a literary inventi
2 CONC on.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Sögubrot'' tells that he married the fugitive princess Auðr the Deep-Minded without the consent of her father king Ivar Vidfamne, who soon departed to punish his daughter. He died, however, on route, and so Ráðbarðr helped Auð's
2 CONC  son Harald Wartooth claim his maternal grandfather's possessions in Sweden and Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ráðbarðr and Auðr had a son together named Randver.
2 CONT
