2 CONT  Ivarr Vídfadmi Hálfdanarson, King of the Danes and Swedes was the son of Hálfdan Snälle Haraldsson, King of Roeskilde and Maolda (?). Ivarr Vídfadmi Hálfdanarson, King of the Danes and Swedes went to Scania after the death of his
2 CONC  uncle Gudrod, and collected an army in all haste, and moved with it into Sweden where he hoped to avenge the death's of his uncle and father at the hands of Ingjalds daughter Aasa.4 He subdued the whole of Sweden, he brought in s
2 CONC ubjection to himself all the Danish dominions, a great deal of Saxland, all the East Country, and a fifth part of England, for this he became known as the "Wide Reacher" for so expanding his kingdom.4 Ivarr Vídfadmi Hálfdanarson, 
2 CONC King of the Danes and Swedes also went by the name of Ivar "the Wide-Reacher". King of the Danes at Roskilde, Denmark, between 588 and 647.5 He was the successor of King of the Swedes Óláfr Trételgju Ingjaldsson; King of the Swede
2 CONC s.6 Ivarr Vídfadmi Hálfdanarson, King of the Danes and Swedes was began to bring his army against the wicked king of Skåne, Ingjald Illråd and surrounded Ingjald's great hall on Lake Mälen in which Ingjald perished when he burned 
2 CONC down his own palace around him and his daughter circa 623 at Lake Mälaren, Uppsala, Sweden.4 King of the Swedes at Uppsala, Sweden, between 630 and 647.6 He married Gyrita of Jutland.7 Ivarr Vídfadmi Hálfdanarson, King of the Dane
2 CONC s and Swedes witnessed the death of Prince of Lejre Rörik Skjölding before 647; He was killed by Oda's father, Ivar, in revenge for Rurik's killing of Oda's lover, Helge. Ivarr Vídfadmi Hálfdanarson, King of the Danes and Swedes d
2 CONC ied in 647. He died while sailing for Russia, where he set out to punish his daughter's new husband for marrying Oda without permission, and to do some plundering as well. His boat sank and he drowned in the frigid waters of the G
2 CONC ulf of Finland.8,9 He was the predecessor of King of the Danes and Swedes Harold Hildetand Röriksson; King of the Swedes.6 Ivarr Vídfadmi Hálfdanarson, King of the Danes and Swedes was the predecessor of King of the Danes and Swed
2 CONC es Harold Hildetand Röriksson; King of the Danes.5
2 CONT
