2 CONT Cross 1964, p. 74: "For the total evidence stresses that OE. earendel has an area of meaning which allows it to represent Latin words describing varying concepts of 'light'; and on occasions, (aurora, lucifer, dægrima) this area i
2 CONC s limited to permit equation with words meaning: 'coming or rising light, beginning of light, bringer of light'. It would appear from discussions of the etymology of earendel that the more limited meaning is the original one, and 
2 CONC the meanings attested in equations with OE. leoma and Latin jubar are later extensions."
