2 CONC thelwulf sent his son Alfred to Rome. Then at that time, the lord Leo was pope of Rome [Leo IV 847–55]; and he hallowed him king, and took him for his episcopal son [i.e. as his godson in confirmation].”  Æthelweard and Asser also
2 CONC  say the same thing, though Asser adds (§8) that Alfred, who was four years-old in 853, was accompanied by: “an honourable escort both of nobles and commoners.”  Unlikely as it seems, it appears that Alfred did, indeed, make this 
2 CONC journey to Rome. In a letter to Æthelwulf (generally accepted as being authentic) Pope Leo says: “We have now graciously received your son Alfred, whom you were anxious to send at this time to the thresholds of the Holy Apostles, 
