2 CONT
2 CONT It is from the Normans that Normandy gets its name. The word "Norman" derives from "North Man," that is, People of the North.
2 CONT
2 CONT - - - - - - - - - -  --  - - - - - --  -  --  - -  - - - -  -  --  - - - - - - - --  -
2 CONT
2 CONT Rollo (c. 860 – c. 932), baptised Robert, was the founder and first ruler of the Viking principality in what soon became known as Normandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Rollo is a Frankish-Latin name probably taken from the Old Norse name Hrólfr (cf. the latinization of Hrólfr into the similar 
2 CONT
2 CONT Falaise castle was the home of Rollo.
2 CONT
