2 CONT
2 CONT According to Stuart--Royalty for Commoners 1-3 & Weis Ancestral Roots 4-10
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rollo/Rolf  was son of Rognvald, Earl of More, presumably of Norwegianancestry. He had a Viking career, raiding in Scotland, Ireland andFrance. He was defeated outside Chartres in 911 but his right to lands inthe  Seine valley was
2 CONC  later confirmed by the emperor and he was baptisedby the Archbishop of
2 CONT Rouen.
2 CONT Info from David C Douglas 'William the Conqueror [Methuen, 1969, p16].
2 CONT
2 CONT    Sources: A. Roots 121E, 243A; Kraentzler 1160, 1443, 1453; RC 162,166; Coe;
2 CONT Guizot; The Normans and Their Myth (chart) by R.H.C. Davis; Pfafman; WEDStokes;
2 CONT A History of the Vikings by Gwyn Jones; Ashley; Norr, p59.
2 CONT    He established the Northmen in France and was the first Duke ofNormandy.
2 CONT Count of Rouen. Conquered Normandy. Also known as Hrolf (Gongu-Hrolfr),
2 CONT Rollon, Ganger and Granger Rolf.
2 CONT    WED says the area near "Mora, Norway, was the domain of the jarl ofMore,
2 CONT whose son Hrolf, with his followers...in 911 settled in the districtlater
2 CONT known as Normandy."
2 CONT    Roots: Ganger Rolf, "the Viking (or Rollo), banished from Norway tothe
2 CONT Hebrides ca. 876; 890 participated in Viking attack on Bayeux, whereCount
2 CONT Berenger of Bayeux was killed, and his daughter Poppa taken, 886, byRollo (now
2 CONT called Count of Rouen) as his "Danish" wife. Under Treaty of St. Clair,911,
2 CONT received the Duchy of Normandy from Charles III, "the Simple."
2 CONT    Davis: Rollo, ruler of Normandy from 911-931. The dukes of Normandyfree
2 CONT married with non-Scandinavians. "Rollo is said to have married thedaughter of
2 CONT the Frankish king and to have had his son by the daughter of a Frankishcount.
2 CONT That son, William, married the daughter of a Frankish count and had hisson,
2 CONT Richard, by a Breton. None of the dukes' wives came from Scandinavia or
2 CONT England, and by the first half of the 11th century their familyconnections
2 CONT were typically French." An early historian, Dudo, said Rollo was Danish.
2 CONT    Ashley: Count Rolllo or Rolf the Viking., died 993?
2 CONT    Norr: Rollo or Rolf, 1st duke of Normandy 912-917-(927), born about856. He
2 CONT was of the same Danish origin as the ancestors of the English which his
2 CONT descendants conquered in 1066.
2 CONT
2 CONT The vast majority of the information presented is obtained from online sources.  While I believe it to be accurate, caution must be taken to always be careful of its validity.
2 CONT Please do contact me if you find errors or have questions.
