1 NOTE Earl of Hedemarken.
2 CONT Født: den høyrøstede.
2 CONT 887237938. Øystein Jarl Sjøfarer (21906). Han var jarl på Oplandene (Hedmarken) og i viken. Han gikk i Harald Hårfagres theneste og blev hans jarl først på Oplandene og senere, da Haralds morbror Guttorm døde, også i Viken. Øy
2 CONC stein var som flere menne på Oplandene en stor viking, hvas også hans tilnavn "sjøfarer" forteller. He was married.
1 NOTE Alias/AKA Øystein Glumra
1 NOTE Earl of More
1 NOTE 35th great grandfather
1 NOTE Øysten must have lived ca. 830.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father would have been Ivar Opplendingajarl, son of Håkon Gamle and grandson of Gor.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Saga of Olaf Haraldson:
2 CONT
2 CONT "99. HISTORY OF THE EARLS OF ORKNEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is related that in the days of Harald Harfager, the king of Norway, the islands of Orkney, which before had been only a resort for vikings, were settled . The first earl in the Orkney Islands was called Sigurd, who was a son of
2 CONC  Eystein Glumra, and brother of Ragnvald earl of More. ..."
1 NOTE OR "EYSTEIN BJORN""RATTLE"; JARL OF THE UPPERLANDERS
1 NOTE !BIRTH: "Royal Ancestors" by Michel Call - Based on Call Family Pedigrees FHL
2 CONT film 844805 & 844806, Family History Library, Salt Lake City, UT. Copy of
2 CONT "Royal Ancestors" owned by Lynn Bernhard, Orem, UT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Data From Lynn Jeffrey Bernhard, 2445 W 450 South #4, Springville UT  84663-4950 
2 CONT email - bernhardengineer@netscape.net
