2 CONT PAM, http://home.sol.no/~nermo/slekt/d0007/g0000055.html#I7061
2 CONT http://www.stirnet.com/HTML/genie/ancient/tz/viking03.htm
2 CONT http://worldroots.com/ged/pomer/dat82.html#8
1 NOTE Alias:<ALIA> Noisy Jarl of the /Uplands/
2 CONT Sources: A. Roots 121E, 143A; RC 44, 166; Kraentzler 1453, 1593, 1609, 
2 CONT 1645;
2 CONT AF; The Dukes of Normandy and Their Origins; Pfafman; History of the 
2 CONT Vikings;
2 CONT Russell.
2 CONT RC:Eistein Ivarsson, Jarl of Hedemarken (of the Uplands), ca 830.
2 CONT Roots: Eystein Glumra, Jarl of the Upplands, ca. 830, said to have 
2 CONT fathered
2 CONT two known children: Swanhild and Ragnvald I.
2 CONT K. calls him Eystein Ivarsson, aka Euslin "Ghimrice/Ghemvice" of 
2 CONT Schleswig.
2 CONT K: Eystein "Glumra" Ivarsson, Count of Maere (More). Jarl of the Uplanders
2 CONT in Norway.
2 CONT Russell: Eisten Glumru of Vors, A.D. 870. Names Rogvald as ason, but not
2 CONT son Malahue and daughter Swanhild. Names instead Sigurd, Jarl ofthe 
2 CONT Orkneys,
2 CONT andd Huldrich, ancestor of Raoul de Toeny.
2 CONT Eystein Glumra wasthe Earl of Moera (various spellings for this) in 
2 CONT Norway
2 CONT and Jarl of Orkneyand Shetland.
2 CONT According to both the Heimskringla Saga and the Orkneyinga Saga, Eystein
2 CONT Glumra was the father of Rognvald. The Orkneyinga Saga says Eystein 
2 CONT Glumra's
2 CONT earliest forebear was Fornjot, King of Finland and Kvenland. Fornjot's
2 CONT great-great-grandson was Thorri, or Fhorri, who had two sons, Norr and 
2 CONT Gorr,
2 CONT who emigrated westward. Norr took the mainland called Norway and Gorr 
2 CONT took the
2 CONT islands. Gorr's son Heiti was the father of Sveithi (Sveide), the Sea 
2 CONT King,
2 CONT who died about 760. Sveithi's son, Halfdan the Old, who died in 800, was 
2 CONT the
2 CONT father of Ivar, Earl of the Uplands. And Ivar, in turn, was the father of
2 CONT Eystein Glumra.
2 CONT RC 44 calls this man Eistein Ivarsson, son of Ivar, who was son of Halfdan
2 CONT the Old. So it follows the Sagas for three generations.
2 CONT There was no written language during this period, and the Norse sagas
2 CONT provided oral histories, much like those Alex Haley,
1 NOTE Eystein Ivarsson was married to Ascrida (Aseda) Roganvaldsdatter, the Countess of Oppland. He was described as a petty King. They had at least 4 children all born in Maer, Norway
