1 NOTE He was the King who was first to rule all of Norway. He ruled from 860 to 940.
1 NOTE He was the King who was first to rule all of Norway. He ruled from 860 to 940.
1 NOTE Harald I, King of Norway also went by the nick-name of Harald 'Schoenharr' (?) (or in English, Harald 'the Fairhaired'). He gained the title of King Harald I of Norway in 858. He abdicated as King of Norway in 928.
1 NOTE "HAARFAGRE"; KING OF NORWAY
1 NOTE Harald the Fairhaired (aka Harald Finehair or Haarfarge), was at the sea battle of Hafrsfjord in 872 hwn Harald, King of Vestfold on the Oslo fjord, defeated a coalition of other minor kings and united Norway under his rule, accor
2 CONC ding the  Henrikson, the Chronicler.  Many of Harald's followers left the country at this time, rather be under his rule, and went to the Swedish Province of Jamtland and to Iceland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald Haarfarge, or the Fair Haired, was the ancestor of most of the Royal Houses of Modern-day Europe.  Most of today's royal houses descend from this man.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald the Fairhaired died age 85, one of the few Viking kings to die in old age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald Haarfargre, he of the thick hair, first over-all King of Norway, died in 934, ancestor of the Kings of Norway, overlords of Man the Isles until 1266 (Scotland); and ancestor of all the Royal Houses of Europe.
1 NOTE 	1  NAME Fairhair //
2 CONT 	2  GIVN Fairhair
2 CONT 	2  SURN
2 CONT 	2  NICK Fairhair
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Vestfold, King of Norway, had many wives and concubines, undertook conquest of Norway to win Gytha, and until successful refused for ten years to cut or comb hair (called Lufa, "the Slovenly"), became 1st King of all Norwa
2 CONC y abt. 883/890, cut hair after conquest (then called "Fairhair"), won Gytha, d. abt. 936.
2 CONT MISC: Harald inherited three small domains from his father in eastern, central, and western Norway, and set out to conquer the rest of Norway. According to the medieval saga, he was motivated by the refusal of Gyda (another petty 
2 CONC king's daughter) to marry him until he had conquered all of Norway. According to the story, King Harald declared that he would not cut or comb his hair until he had conquered all of Norway. When he finally had victory about ten ye
2 CONC ars later, he then had his hair done and was called "Fairhair." The chieftains of western Norway were the hardest to defeat, but Harald attained his victory in the Battle of Hafrsfjord about 885. Harald was a strong ruler, and man
2 CONC aged to unite Norway. At Harald's death, his sons divided Norway with the favorite son, Eric Bloodaxe, as the overking, but dissensions and wars disrupted the unity of the country.
2 CONT Alternatively, there are references that spell his first name "Harold," and list his death date as being 933 or 945.
2 CONT He succeeded to the throne of his father's kingdom as a child in 860.
2 CONT
2 CONT Age at death: Over 72.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the first king of United Norway.
