1 NOTE Princess of Scotland
2 CONT Heiress of Scone
1 NOTE This person is listed as the father of Maldred AFN 8XJJ-WP taken from the Family Search Ancestral File and  Uchtret is taken from "The House Of Adam" records on file from the Genealogical Library.
1 NOTE 30th great grandmother
1 NOTE Elder daughter of Malcolm II, King of Scots [ROWLEYHR.GED]
1 NOTE For father's ancestry, see N.N. Malcolmsdatter (RN=1631).
1 NOTE For father's ancestry, see N.N. Malcolmsdatter (RN=1631).
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 84-11
1 NOTE [large-G675.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Srce:  Broderbund World Family Tree Vol. II, pedigree # 1822
1 NOTE Alias:<ALIA> /BEATRIX/
2 CONT Ancestral File Number:<AFN> 8XJK-HR
2 CONT REFN: 1316
2 CONT [Mary Stewart.FTW]
2 CONT BETHOC (or BEATRIX)21 (Malcolm II20, Kenneth II19, Malcolm18, Don ald
2 CONT II17, Constantine I16, Kenneth15, Alpin14, Eochy-Annuine (Eugenius
2 CONT III) 13, Ed-fin12, Eochaid III of11, Eochy II (Eugenius II)10, Domangart
2 CONT (Dongardu s)9, Donald I8, Eochy I (Eugenius I)7, Aidan (Aidanus)6, Gavran
2 CONT (Goranus)5, D omangart (Dongardus)4, Fergus the Great3, Erc2, Eochy
2 CONT (Eugenius)1), daughter of (20) Malcolm II20, (King), was born after 938,
2 CONT and died after 1000. She ma rried in 1000, (M-1) CRINAN THE THANE, who was
2 CONT born in 978, and died in 1045. [25]
2 CONT Apparently the only child of Malcolm MacKenneth
2 CONT AR: (170-19), (172-19) [25]
2 CONT Children: See (M-1) Crinan the ThaneHeiress of Scone
1 NOTE Bethoc av Skottland, eller Bethóc ingen Maíl Coluim meic Cináeda, var den eldste datteren til kong Máel Coluim mac Cináeda (Malcolm II av Skottland) som ikke hadde noen sønner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Det sterkeste arvelige krav til å etterfølge som skottenes konge gikk derfor via Bethóc. Omtrent rundt år 1000 giftet prinsesse Bethóc seg med Crínán av Dunkeld, lekmannsabbed og muligens mormaer. Den første sønnen av dette 
2 CONC ekteskapet ble Donnchad mac Crínáin (Duncan I av Skottland) som overtok den skotske tronen i 1034. Tidlige skribenter har også forfektet at Máel Coluim mac Cináeda (Malcolm II av Skottland) selv hadde utsett Donnchad som sin 
2 CONC etterfølger under reglene om tanisteri ettersom det var andre mulige krav til tronen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Det er mulig at Bethóc tidligere hadde vært gift med jarl Sigurd Lodvesson (kalt den digre eller staute) av Orknøyene, og med Findláech, mormaer av Moireabh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethóc må ikke forveksles med Bethóc ingen Domnaill Bain meic Donnchada, en datter av Donald III av Skottland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Litteratur
2 CONT Anderson, Marjorie Ogilvy: Kings and Kingship in Early Scotland, 1973 
1 NOTE The strongest hereditary claim of succession to the Scottish throne therefore passed through Bethóc. Approximately 1000, Princess Bethóc married Crínán, Abbot of Dunkeld. The first son of this marriage was Donnchad I, who ascended
2 CONC  to the throne of Scotland in 1034. Early writers have asserted that Máel Coluim also designated Donnchad as his successor under the rules of tanistry because there were other possible claimants to the throne. It is possible that 
2 CONC Bethóc had previously been married to Jarl Sigurd the Stout of Orkney, and to Findláech, the Mormaer of Moireabh.
1 NOTE Bethoc (Beatrix, Beatrice) MacKenneth, Princess of Scotland, born 984 at Atholl, Perth, Scotland; date of death is uncertain. Bethoc was the eldest daughter of King Malcolm II of Alba (Scotland), who had no sons. The strongest her
2 CONC editary claim of succession to the Scottish throne therefore passed through Bethoc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Approximately 1000 CE, Princess Bethoc married Crinan the Thane de Mormaer (Earl) of Dunkeld. The first son of this marriage was Duncan Cæn-Mohr MacCrinan, who ascended to the throne of Scotland in 1034.
2 CONT
2 CONT Early writers have asserted that Malcolm II also designated Duncan as his successor under the rules of tanistry because there were other possible claimants to the throne.
2 CONT Bethoc married Crinan of Atholl before 1008. (Crinan of Atholl was born in 978 in Atholl, Perth, Scotland and died in 1045 in Dunkeld, Tayside, Scotland.) The cause of her death was killed in battle.
1 NOTE This person is listed as the father of Maldred AFN 8XJJ-WP taken from the Family Search Ancestral File and  Uchtret is taken from "The House Of Adam" records on file from the Genealogical Library.
1 NOTE Bethoc
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=2ef648a0-788e-455c-bf9d-b760a4f979d5&tid=9692367&pid=-523359621
1 NOTE Source: THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry.  Chart: page 45.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 44:
2 CONT
2 CONT 20.    Bethoc (Beatrix), eldest dau.; m. 1000 Crinan, Thane of Dull 978-1045, Lay Abbot of Dunkeld, the ecclestiasical center of Scotland, and Governor of the Scots Islands.  He fell in battle between the Scots themselves.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amie, Adam and FAL
