1 NOTE Daughter or Widow of Thorfinn, Earl of Orkney. {Burke's Peerage} [GADD.GED]
1 NOTE Widow of the Earl of Orkney.
2 CONT Malcolm III Canmore (1058-93) came to the throne by disposing of his rivals and thereafter sought, in five unsuccessful raids, to extend his kingdom into northern England. Whereas his first wife, Ingibjorg, was the daughter of a N
2 CONC orse earl of Orkney, his second, Margaret, came from the Saxon royal house of England.
2 CONT Ingibjorg married Thorfinn the Black Sigurdsson, son of Sigurd "the Stout" Hlodvirsson and Daughter Of Scotland, before 1038. (Thorfinn the Black Sigurdsson was born in 1009 and died in 1064.)
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT http://www.geocities.com/marthajanehick/b67.htm#P6300
1 NOTE 1  NAME Inebiorg /Finnsdatter/ 1  DEAT 2  DATE ABT. 1066
1 NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Ingebjorg Finnsdotter (Finn's-Daughter) was the first wife of King Malcolm III (Canmore) of Scotland. Her first husband was Earl Thorfinn of Orkney, by whom she had two sons Paul and Erlend. Uponthe death of Thorfinn she marri
2 CONC ed Malcolm and had further children including the future King Duncan II of Scotland.
2 CONT
