1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Paul Thorfinnsson, Earl of Orkney and Caithness=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Possibly a twin, as he and his brother were joint rulers and always mentioned together.
2 CONT * Jarl of Orkney and Caithness
2 CONT
2 CONT =Thorfinn & his wife  Ragnhildr Hákonardóttir  had [three or more] children=
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.         [http://www.geni.com/people/P%C3%A5l-Thorfinnsson/6000000000424848932?through=6000000001052011900  PAUL Thorfinnsson, son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Thorfinn-Sigurdsson/6000000001052002306 THORFINN II] "the Black" 
2 CONC Jarl of Orkney & his wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Ingibj%C3%B6rg-Finnsd%C3%B3ttir/6000000001052011900 Ingibjörg] Finnsdatter (-in prison Bergen 1098, bur Bergen).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Paul and…Erlend” as the two sons of Jar
2 CONC l Thorfinn and his wife who survived childhood[932].  He succeeded his father [1065] as Joint Jarl of Orkney, jointly with his brother.  Morkinskinna records that Harald III King of Norway sailed to Orkney en route for his invasio
2 CONC n of England in 1066 and “recruited the aid of Jarl Thorfinn´s sons Páll and Erlendr”[933]. Orkneyinga Saga records that [http://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-III-Olavsson-%C2%ABBarefoot%C2%BB-Berrf%C3%B8tt/5381202464070053447  Magnu
2 CONC s "Barelegs]" King of Norway “seized the Earls, Paul and Erlend” on his arrival in Orkney, “sent them east to Norway, and made his own son Sigurd overlord of the islands with regents to govern the earldom”, adding in a later passa
2 CONC ge that Paul “was buried at Bergen”[935].  He was deposed and imprisoned in 1098 by Magnus "Barelegs" King of Norway, and died in Bergen according to Snorre[936].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc26845
2 CONC 0047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >m --- [http://www.geni.com/people/Ragnhild-Haakonsdatter/6000000003645825356?through=6000000000424848932 Haakonsdatter], daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Haakon-Ivarsson-Earl/6000000003645772914?through=6000000003645825356
2 CONC   HAAKON] Ivarsson & his wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Ragnhild-Princess-of-Norway/6000000003645772920?through=6000000003645825356  Ragnhild] Magnusdatter of Norway.  Orkneyinga Saga records that “Earl Paul Thorfinnson” married
2 CONC  “a daughter of Earl Hakon Ivarsson”[937]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >Paul & his wife had children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>1.         [http://www.geni.com/people/H%C3%A5kon-P%C3%A5lson/6000000003645825338?through=6000000000424848932  HAKON] Paulsson (before [1070]-Orkney [1126]).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Hakon” as son of “Earl Paul Thorfinnson” and h
2 CONC is wife[938].  It is extremely unlikely that Hakon was born before [1070], given the estimated birth date of his granddaughter Margaret (see below).  Snorre names "Hakon, a son of Earl Paul" when recording that "a year or two afte
2 CONC r King Magnus's fall…[he] came from Orkney" and was given the earldom of Orkney by Kings Eystein, Sigurd and Olav, before sailing back to Orkney[939].  Orkneyinga Saga records that Hakon left Orkney for Norway where he visited “Ki
2 CONC ng Olaf the Peaceful…towards the end of Olaf´s reign” (King Olaf´s death is dated to 1093) before sailing east to Sweden and “King Ingi Steinkelsson”[940].  He was appointed Joint Lieutenant for Sigurd Magnusson King of Orkney and
2 CONC  the Isles, when the latter returned to Norway in 1103 on his accession as king.  He was installed in [Spring 1105] as Jarl of Orkney by King Sigurd.  He ruled as Joint Jarl from Spring 1108, when his cousin Magnus Erlendsson was 
2 CONC installed as Jarl of ½ Orkney.  He later quarrelled with his cousin, took him prisoner on Egilsay and had him killed.  Orkneyinga Saga records that “Earl Hakon Paulsson died in his bed in Orkney”[941].  
2 CONT >>m ---.  The name of Hakon´s wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Hakon & his wife had one child: [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>a)         [http://www.geni.com/people/H%C3%A5kon-P%C3%A5lson/6000000003645825338  PAUL (II)] Hakonsson "the Silent" (-after 1137).  Orkneyinga Saga records that earl Hakon “had another son Paul…the Silent”[943].  He succeeded 
2 CONC his father in [1126] as Joint Jarl of Orkney and Caithness, jointly with his half-brother, sole Jarl after the latter's death in [1131].  His second cousin, Kali-Ragnvald, rebelled in 1135 and demanded a half share of Orkney.  In 
2 CONC revenge for being refused, the latter seized Shetland in 1136, but Paul [II] defeated him in Yell Sound 27 Jun 1136.  The following year he again seized the Shetlands, and captured and deposed Paul [II] in 1137.[http://fmg.ac/Proj
2 CONC ects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Mistress (1): [http://www.geni.com/people/Helga-Moddansd%C3%B3ttir/6000000003645825345#/tab/discussion HELGA], daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Moddan-Moddansson/6000000000424817611?through=6000000003645825345 MODDAN] of 
2 CONC Dalr in Caithness & his wife ---.  Orkneyinga Saga names “Helga” daughter of “a farmer…Moddan…living in the Dales of Caithness” as “Earl Hakon´s mistress”[942].  Her stepson banished her and her sister [http://www.geni.com/people/
2 CONC Frakok-Moddansdatter/6000000003086848152 Frakok] to the latter's estates in Helmsdale, Sutherland after the death of her son [1131]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Hakon had three illegitimate children by Mistress (1):
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>b)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Harald-Hakonsson/6000000002134793657 HARALD] [I] "Slettmali/Smooth-spoken" (before [1090]-[1131]).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Harald…Smooth-Tongue and two daughters…Ingibjorg…Margaret” as the
2 CONC  children of Earl Hakon and his mistress Helga[944].  It is unlikely that Harald was born later than [1090] if the estimated birth date of his daughter Margaret is correct.  He succeeded his father in [1126] as Joint Jarl of Orkne
2 CONC y and Caithness, jointly with his half-brother.  Orkneyinga Saga records that he died after trying on a poisoned garment prepared by his mother and intended for his half-brother Paul[945]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH
2 CONC %20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>m ---.  The name of Harald´s wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>Harald & his wife had one child:  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>i)          [http://www.geni.com/people/Erland-Haraldsson/6000000008248157063?through=6000000002134793657 ERLEND] Haraldsson (-murdered Damsay Dec 1156).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Erlend” as son of “Harald Smooth-Tongue” when re
2 CONC cording that he was reared by [http://www.geni.com/people/Frakok-Moddansdatter/6000000003086848152 Frakok], sister of his paternal grandmother[946].  Eystein II King of Norway gave him permission in Autumn 1151 to administer ½ Ork
2 CONC ney during the absence of Jarl Kali-Ragnvald, but he was unable to impose his claim.  He was recognised as Earl of ½ Caithness by Malcolm IV King of Scotland 24 May 1153, in opposition to his first cousin Harald Maddadsson, during
2 CONC  the absence of Jarl Kali-Ragnvald.  He was invested as Jarl of Orkney in 1153 by King Eystein II, invaded Orkney and defeated Jarl Harald [II] at Kiarrek-Stadir 28/29 Sep 1154, forcing him to surrender his share of Orkney.  He wa
2 CONC s dispossessed of Orkney by Jarl Kali-Ragnvald in Sep 1156 after the latter's return.  After a brief revival as Jarl following his defeat of Jarl Harald [III] 24 Oct 1156, he was once more defeated by Kali-Ragnvald and killed.  [h
2 CONC ttp://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>c)          [http://www.geni.com/people/Ingebj%C3%B6rg-H%C3%A1konard%C3%B3ttir/6000000009706835506?through=6000000002134793657 INGIBJÖRG] .  Orkneyinga Saga names “Harald…Smooth-Tongue and two daughters…Ingibjorg…Margaret” as t
2 CONC he children of Earl Hakon and his mistress Helga, adding that Ingibjörg married “[http://www.geni.com/people/Olof-Bitling-of-Isle-of-Man/6000000001744995580?through=6000000009706835506 Olaf Tit-Bit] King of the Hebrides”[947].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>m [as his second wife], [http://www.geni.com/people/Olof-Bitling-of-Isle-of-Man/6000000001744995580?through=6000000009706835506  OLAV] Bitling King of Sodor and Man 1097-1098 and 1103-1153, son of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>Olav & his wife had one child:  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>i)          [http://www.geni.com/people/Godrod-%C3%93l%C3%A1fsson/6000000017405011036  GODROD].  His parentage is deduced from the Orkneyinga Saga which records that the mother of “Rognvald Godrodarson, King of the Hebrides” w
2 CONC as “Ingibjorg, Earl Hakon Paulsson´s daughter”[948].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>m ---.  The name of Godrod´s wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>Godrod & his wife had one child:  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>(a)        [http://www.geni.com/people/Ragnvald-Godradorson/6000000017404478781 RAGNVALD] Godradarson .  King of Man and the Isles. Orkneyinga Saga records that the mother of “Rognvald Godrodarson, King of the Hebrides” was “
2 CONC Ingibjorg, Earl Hakon Paulsson´s daughter”[949].  William "the Lion" King of Scotland sold Caithness to him after the battle of Wick in 1198.  He lost Caithness to Harald [II] Maddadsson Jarl of Orkney in 1200.  [http://fmg.ac/Pro
2 CONC jects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>d)        [http://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-of-Orkney/6000000012888440533?through=6000000002134793657 MARGARET] (before [1115]-).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Harald…Smooth-Tongue and two daughters…Ingibjorg…Margaret” as the chil
2 CONC dren of Earl Hakon and his mistress Helga[950].  It is unlikely that Margaret was born after [1115] if it is correct that her son was born in 1134.  Orkneyinga Saga records that “Margaret Hakon´s-Daughter” married “[http://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/people/Madach-1st-Earl-of-Athol/6000000012888499687?through=6000000012888440533  Earl Maddad] of Atholl”[951].  Orkneyinga Saga records that “[http://www.geni.com/people/Erland/6000000017404525840?through=6000000012888440533
2 CONC  Erlend the Young]” abducted Margaret from Orkney and took her to Shetland, and that her son eventually granted permission for their marriage[952].  
2 CONT >>>m firstly ([1133]) as his second wife, [http://www.geni.com/people/Madach-1st-Earl-of-Athol/6000000012888499687?through=6000000012888440533 MADDAD] [Madach] Earl of Atholl, son of --- (-[1142/52]).  
2 CONT >>>m secondly [http://www.geni.com/people/Erland/6000000017404525840?through=6000000012888440533 ERLAND] "Ungi/the Young" (-killed 1156).  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>2.         [http://www.geni.com/people/Thora-of-Orkney/6000000002553673810?through=6000000000424848932 THORA] Paulsdatter .  Orkneyinga Saga names (in order) “Thora…Ingirid…Herbjorg…Ragnhild” as the daughters of “Earl Paul Thorf
2 CONC innson” and his wife, adding that Thora married “in Norway…[http://www.geni.com/people/Halldor/6000000000571789205  Halldor], the son of Brynjolf Camel” and that their son was “[http://www.geni.com/people/Brynjolf/6000000017405255
2 CONC 404 Brynjolf], the father of [http://www.geni.com/people/Halldor-Ulvalde/6000000002553594992 Halldor] who married [http://www.geni.com/people/Sigrid-Austraat/6000000006197675244 Gudrid Dag´s-Daughter”][953].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>m [http://www.geni.com/people/Brynjulv-III-Ulvalde/6000000000571789205?through=6000000002553673810 HALLDOR], son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Brynjulf-Ulvalde-II/6000000008688269823?through=6000000000571789205 BRYNIOLF] Camel 
2 CONC & his wife –[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>3.         [http://www.geni.com/people/Ingrid-Paalsdatter/6000000002134793568?through=6000000000424848932 INGRID] Paulsdatter .  Orkneyinga Saga names (in order) “Thora…Ingirid…Herbjorg…Ragnhild” as the daughters of “Earl Paul T
