2 CONT From "The Ynglinga Saga":
2 CONT
2 CONT "51. OF KING EYSTEIN'S DEATH.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eystein, Halfdan Hvitbein's son, became king after in Raumarike and Westfold. He was married to Hild, a daughter of Eric Agnarsson, who was king in Westfold. Agnar, Eric's father, was a son of Sigtryg, king in the Vend district. K
2 CONC ing Eric had no son, and died while King Halfdan Hvitbein was still in life. The father and son, Halfdan and Eystein, then took possession of the whole of Westfold, which Eystein ruled over as long as he lived. ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Hild married Öystein Halfdansson, son of Halvdan "Hvitbeinn" Olofsson and Åsa Eysteinsdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT og gift med Hild, dotter hans Eirik Agnarsson i Vestfold. Han arva Vestfold av verfaren. Snorre fortel at Eirik var soneson av ein konge i Vendsyssel.
