2 CONT Halvdan Øysteinsson den gavmilde
2 CONT
2 CONT Halvdan Øysteinsson den gavmilde og matille (født ca. 750 død ca. 800) var ifølge sagaene konge over Vestfold og Romerike. Av ynglingeætten.
2 CONT
2 CONT Foreldre: Øystein Halvdansson og Hild Eriksdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift med: Liv Dagsdotter, Helga Dagsdotter, datter av Dag Frode
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn: Gudrød Halvdansson Veidekonge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Halvdan var kjent som en stor kriger og han vant store rikdommer på sine ferder. Han lønnet mennene sine bra, og var kjent for sin gavmildhet. Døde sottedød, ble hauglagt i Borre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorre skriver;
2 CONT
2 CONT Så sier Tjodolv:
2 CONT
2 CONT Og til møte Lokes møy tredje konge fra livet kalte,
2 CONT
2 CONT da Halvdan, Holtanbonden,
2 CONT
2 CONT hadde nytt det norner bød.
2 CONT
2 CONT Og seierens menn siden gjemte budlungen der i Borre..
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hálfdanar saga Eysteinssonar
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Hálfdanar saga Eysteinssonar is a legendary saga from early 14th century Iceland about Halfdan Eysteinsson. The main events appear to take place in the 9th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan's grandfather was Þrándr the eponymous king of Trondheim, who in turn was the son of Sæmingr the king of Halogaland and the son of Odin. Sæmingr had married Naumu who had given her name to Namdalen. Þrándr had married Dagm
2 CONC ær, the sister of Svanhvít, the heroine of Hrómundar saga Gripssonar, and they had had the sons Eysteinn and Eirikr inn víðförli who is the hero of Eireks saga víðförla and discovered Ódáinsakr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eysteinn married Ása, the daughter of Sigurd Hart and Áslaug, the daughter of Sigurd Snake-in-the-Eye. They had several sons among them Halfdan.
2 CONT
2 CONT It deals with Eysteinn's adventures in Staraja Ladoga (Aldeigjuborg), his conquest of Alaborg and about the adventures of his son Halfdan.
2 CONT
