2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan the Mild (Old Norse: Hálfdan hinn mildi) was the son of king Eystein Halfdansson, of the House of Yngling and he succeeded his father as king, according to Heimskringla. He was king of Romerike and Vestfold.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was said to be generous in gold but to starve his men with food. He was a great warrior who often pillaged and gathered great booty.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was Liv, the daughter of king Dag of Vestmar. Halfdan the Mild died of illness in his bed.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his son, Gudrød the Hunter.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Frå Wikipedia – det frie oppslagsverket
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigering, søk
2 CONT
2 CONT Halvdan den Milde og Mat-ille var ein konge av Ynglingeætta, far til Gudrød Veidekonge og farfar til Halvdan Svarte. Han var son av kong Øystein av ynglingeætta.
2 CONT
2 CONT Han sat som konge i Holtar, no Holtan i Borre, og er gravlagd der. Han var gift med Liv, dotter til kong Dag på Vestmar, i dag eigna kring Langesund. Namnet og gravstaden hans tyder på ei lekk til Danmark (Borrestil).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
