2 NOTE Note: This Coat of Arms is very similar to that of Royal Arms of King Richard the Lionheart (circa 1198). His Coat of arms has THREE lions.
2 NOTE To Margaret Faye Ashworth (Handwerk), in response to your ridiculous comment.
3 CONT
3 CONT On Sep 27, 2008, at 2:01 PM, Margaret Ashworth wrote:
3 CONT “But when you put your Ashworth Photos title on the pictures, does it make it look like you took them?  Just wondered.  Didn't want to insult some photographer (amateur or professional) somewhere”.
3 CONT
3 CONT • Before you start claiming I have designed family coat of arms.
3 CONT • Let me clear up your confusion.
3 CONT • It’s apparent you do not comprehend my credits. It is plain and simple. 
3 CONT • I do not nor have I ever designed a Family Coat of Arm. (Though an Interesting
3 CONT   idea)
3 CONT • No where does it say designed or created by Ashworth Photos.
3 CONT • This Coat of Arms is hundreds of years old. I do not have a time machine yet.
3 CONT • It is from the album of Walter G. Ashworth, not designed or photographed by
3 CONT   Ashworth Photos, or Walter G. Ashworth. 
3 CONT • I hope this has been made perfectly clear to you now.
3 CONT Thank you. You can stop wondering.
