2 CONT Philip Montgomery formerly Montgomerie Born 1102 in Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales ANCESTORS  Son of Arnoulf (Montgomery) de Montgomery and Lafracoth (O'Brien) de Montgomery Brother of Alice (Montgomerie) de Montgomery Husband of 
2 CONC Margaret Dunbar — married 1118 in Dunbar, East Lothian, Scotlandmap DESCENDANTS  Father of Hugh (Montgomerie) de Montgomery and Robert Montgomery Died 1177 in Thornton, Fife, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile manager: Pat Credit  Profile last modified 26 Apr 2020  Created 11 Jun 2017 Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip (Montgomerie) Montgomery is a member of Clan Montgomery. Philip was the son of Arnoulf Montgomery and Lafracoth O'Brien. He was born about 1101 at Pembroke. His father was banished from the Kingdom while he was still an inf
2 CONC ant. He eventually returned to Scotland with a group of Normans. There he was called the Welshman or Cymbricus since he was born in Wales. He obtained a fair inheritance and married Lady Margaret Dunbar. She was the daughter of Go
2 CONC spatric II Dunbar, second Earl of Dunbar and March. Based upon the ages of his grandchildren, the marriage must have been before the year 1120. Philip by Lady Margaret left two sons, Robert and Hugh. Robert succeeded him after his
2 CONC  death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes Data from Unsourced GEDCOM subject to record confirmation
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 1102 in Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales. Confirmed  Death: 1177 in Thornton, Fife, Scotland Confirmation pending. Fuller-5853 17:23, 10 June 2017 (EDT) Marriage: 1118 Dunbar, East Lothian, Scotland. Confirmed  How many sibli
2 CONC ngs did Philip have?
2 CONT
2 CONT Arnulph de Montgomerie had an only son: Philip de Montgomerie, was born about the year 1101, ...  Maurice Fitzgerald married Alice, daughter of Arnulph de Montgomery by Lafracoth O'Brien, daughter of the King of Munster.  Sources 
2 CONC Montgomery: Pages 41-42 Philip de Montgomerie Note: Source has his father-in-law as Cospatric, second Earl of Dunbar and March. ? Historical and Topgraphical Notes: Castletown Castle (Old Castletown) page 133 Montgomery, Thomas Ha
