1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.geni.com/people/Kenneth-III-Mac-Duibh-king-of-Scots/4659985?through=6000000003219779698 KENNETH], son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Dubh-mac-M%C3%A1el-Coluim-King-of-Scots/6000000000202034309?through
2 CONC =4659985 DUFF] King of Scotland & his wife --- (-killed in battle Monzievaird [25 Mar 1005]).  The 11th century Synchronisms of Flann Mainistreach name (in order) "…Cuillen mac Illiulb, Cinaet mac Maelcolaim, Custantin mac Cuilen,
2 CONC  Cinaet mac Duib, Maelcolaim mac Cinaeta" as Scottish kings, dated to the 10th and 11th centuries[208].  The 12th century Cronica Regum Scottorum lists "…Chinet filius Duf i anno et dimidium…" as king[209].  He succeeded in 997 as
2 CONC  KENNETH III King of Scotland.  The Annals of Ulster record that "the king of the Albu Cinaed son of Dub" was killed in battle "between the men of Albu themselves" in 1005[210]. m ---.  The name of Kenneth's wife is not known. Ken
2 CONC neth III & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Giric-II-mac-Cin%C3%A1eda-King-of-Scots/6000000003615429242?through=4659985 GREG] [Giric] (-killed in battle Monzievaird [25 Mar 1005], bur Isle of Iona).  The Chronicle of the Picts and Sc
2 CONC ots dated 1251 records that "Girus mac Kinath mac Duff" reigned for 8 years, was killed "a filio Kinet in Moeghauard" and was buried at Iona[211].  The Chronicle of the Picts and Scots dated 1317 includes the same information[212]
2 CONC .  His existence is not recorded in any of the earlier chronicles and should be treated with caution.  The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that King Kenneth II decreed a change to the Scottish royal succession to enable "the n
2 CONC earest survivor in blood to the deceased king to succeed", in opposition to "Constantine the Bald, son of King Culen, and Gryme son of Kenneth son of King Duff"[213].  The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that "Gryme the son of
2 CONC  Kenneth son of Duff" succeeded in 996 after King Constantine III was killed and reigned for eight years and three months[214].  The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that Grime was killed by Malcolm, son of King Kenneth II, add
2 CONC ing that the latter arranged his burial at Iona[215].] 
