1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Órlaith married Domnall Mór, King of Munster, her parents are Sadb Ní Faeláin and Diarmaid Mac Murchadha.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Donnchad-mac-Murchada-King-of-Leinster-and-Dublin/6000000002043258537 DONCHAD], son of MURCHAD King of Leinster & his wife --- (-1115).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record
2 CONC  that “the son of Murchad, son of Diarmait, son of Máel na mbó” won a battle in 1114[689].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Donnchad son of Murchad king of Leinster” was killed in battle by “Domnall son of Murc
2 CONC hertach Húa Bríáin” in 1115[690]. m ---.  The name of Donchad´s wife is not known. Donchad & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  [https://www.geni.com/people/Enna-King-of-Leinster/6000000010646172298 ENNA] (-1126).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Toirdelbach son of Ruaidri king of Ireland” gave “the kingship of the F
2 CONC oreigners to the king of Leinster” in 1125[691].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Enna son of Donnchad son of Murchad king of Leinster” died in 1126, after which “Toirdelbach Húa Conchobair king of Ireland” was
2 CONC  made king of Leinster, unsuccessfully challenged by “Cormac Mac Carthaig king of Desmond”[692].  m ---.  The name of Enna´s wife is not known.  Enna & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/no-name/6000000079563782104 DIARMAIT] (-Fermanagh 1 May 1171).  King of Leinster.  The Annales Cambriæ record that "Diermit rex filius Murcath" was expelled from Ireland by his people and went to the E
2 CONC nglish king, recording in later passages that he returned to Ireland and built "castellum Carrec iuxta Wisefordiam" in 1170, and died in 1172[693].  "Diarmicius Rex Lageniensium" donated "terram…Balidubgaill" to All Saints Dublin 
2 CONC by undated charter witnessed by "…Enna filio meo…"[694].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that Henry II King of England arrived in Ireland in 1171, went to Dublin where he received “the kingship of Leinster and of th
2 CONC e men of Meath, Brefne, Oriel and Ulster”[695].  The Expugnatio Hibernica records the death "apud Fernas circa kal Mai" of "Dermitius Murchardi filius" [in 1171][696].  m [https://www.geni.com/people/no-name/6000000079565452902 MO
2 CONC R], daughter of ---].  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.   Mistress: (1152) DERBFORGAILL, wife of [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079565128944?from_flash=1&fsession_id=152994940
2 CONC 7223&through=6000000079565128944 TIERNAN O'Rourke] King of Breifny, daughter of [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079565326087?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529949407223&through=6000000079565326087 MURCHAD O'Malaghlin] King o
2 CONC f Meath & his wife ---.  The Expugnatio Hibernica records that "Dermitius…Murchardi filius Langeniensium princeps" eloped with "Ororicio…Medensium rege…uxor ipsius Omachlachelini filia" [in 1152][697].  The Annals of Tigernach (Co
2 CONC ntinuation) record that “Diarmait Mac Murchada king of Leinster forcibly carried off out of Meath the wife of Húa Ruairc…Derb-forgaill daughter of Murchad with her wealth” in 1152, adding in a later passage that she “came again to
2 CONC  Húa Ruairc by flight from Leinster” in 1153[698].  Diarmait & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Eva-of-Leinster-Countess-Of-Stirgoil/6000000002253465789?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529951541967&through=6000000002043192150  AOIFE] [Eva] (-after 1189).  The Annales Cambriæ record that "Ricardus comes
2 CONC  de Striguil" invaded Ireland in 1171 and married "filiam Diermit regis"[699].  The Expugnatio Hibernica records the marriage of "filia…Dermitii, Eva" and Earl Richard[700].  She was styled Countess of Ireland in 1185, but Countes
2 CONC s of Strigoil in 1186[701].  m (Waterford [26 Aug 1171]) [https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-de-Clare-2nd-Earl-of-Pembroke/6000000001446542148?through=6000000002253465789 RICHARD de Clare "Strongbow"] Earl of Pembroke, son of GIL
2 CONC BERT de Clare "Strongbow" Earl of Pembroke & his wife Isabel de Beaumont ([1130]-Dublin 20 Apr 1176, bur Dublin, Holy Trinity).  In [1168] he promised Dermot King of Leinster to help him recover his kingdom in return for the hand 
2 CONC of his daughter and eventual succession to the crown.  He landed near Waterford 23 Aug 1170, and marched to Dublin.  He acceded to the demand of King Henry II to surrender his Irish conquests to him and was granted Leinster in fee
2 CONC [702]. 
2 CONT ''[https://www.geni.com/people/Urlachan-MacMurrough/6000000023118216712?through=6000000002253465789 URLACHAN] .  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   m [https://www.geni.com/p
2 CONC eople/Domnall-M%C3%B3r-%C3%93-Briain-R%C3%AD-Tuadhmhumhain-1168-1194/6000000023173413930?through=6000000023118216712  DONOUGH] [Donald] More King of Thomond, son of TADHG King of Thomond & his wife --- (-1194).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Dermot had three illegitimate children by unknown mistresses: 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Enna-mac-Murchada/6000000079566379873?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529952139398&through=6000000079566379873 ENNA] (-1168 or after).  "Diarmicius Rex Lageniensium" donated "terram…Balidubgaill" to All Sain
2 CONC ts Dublin by undated charter witnessed by "…Enna filio meo…"[703].  The Expugnatio Hibernica records that "Ossiriæ princeps Duvenaldus" [Dounchad [Donough] Lord of Ossory] blinded "Dermitio…filium eiusdem primogenitum"[704].  The 
2 CONC Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Enna Mac Murchada crownprince of Leinster” was blinded in 1168 by “Donnchad Mac Gilla Pátraic king of Ossory”[705]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  [https://www.geni.com/people/Conchobar-Mac-Murchadha/6000000002187764124 CONNOR] (-1170).  The Expugnatio Hibernica records that "Dermitio" gave "filium suum Chuchurum" as hostage to Roderic of Connaught [in 1169][706].  The Expu
2 CONC gnatio Hibernica records that Roderic killed Dermot's son [in 1170][707]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079566357909?through=6000000079566357909&fsession_id=1529952139398&from_flash=1  DOMNALL Caemanach] (-killed 1175).  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1175 of "Domnall Caemanach so
2 CONC n of Diarmaid Mac Murchadha king of Leinster…[slain]”[708]. 
