2 CONC nglish king, recording in later passages that he returned to Ireland and built "castellum Carrec iuxta Wisefordiam" in 1170, and died in 1172[693].  "Diarmicius Rex Lageniensium" donated "terram…Balidubgaill" to All Saints Dublin 
2 CONC by undated charter witnessed by "…Enna filio meo…"[694].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that Henry II King of England arrived in Ireland in 1171, went to Dublin where he received “the kingship of Leinster and of th
