2 CONC Gwenllian, born to an unknown mistress, and married to 1) Hwfa ap Cynwrig and 2) Cadwgan of Nannau.(https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173392989825) Wolcott charts two illegitimate Gwenllians, 1) born c.1125, marrie
2 CONC d to Cadwgan, and 2) born c. 1135 and married to Hwfa. He bases this on the dating of Gruffudd ap Cadwgan to c.1155, based on his marriage to Gwenllian/Angharad ferch Dafydd ap Owain Gwynedd of c. 1170. This would preclude a Gwenl
2 CONC lian, married to Cadwgan and having son Gruffudd at c. 1155, from having a daughter with Hwfa in c. 1150 (Angharad ferch Hwfa.) However, if these dates do not hold up, there is the possibility that a Gwenllian born c,1125 could ha
2 CONC ve been married first to Cadwgan, having his children, and then marrying Hwfa and having Angharad.] (Steven Ferry, February 25, 2025.)
