2 CONT Maelgwn ab Owain Gwynedd From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maelgwn_ab_Owain_Gwynedd
2 CONT
2 CONT Maelgwn ab Owain Gwynedd was a prince of part of Gwynedd. Maelgwn was the son of Owain Gwynedd and Gwladus ferch Llywarch ap Trahaearn, and therefore full brother to Iorwerth Drwyndwn, the father of Llywelyn the Great. On the deat
2 CONC h of Owain Gwynedd in 1170 Maelgwn received Anglesey as his share of the kingdom, but in 1173 his brother Dafydd ab Owain Gwynedd attacked him and forced him to flee to Ireland. He returned later that same year, but was taken pris
2 CONC oner by Dafydd. There is no further record of his fate.
