1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Translated Extract from Grettir's Saga: Chapter 14 - Asmund's children. Grettir's childhood=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Asmund  Longhair''' now set up a large and sumptuous household in Bjarg, where he maintained a numerous retinue and became very popular. His children were as follows: The eldest was Atli, an able and accomplished man, tactful a
2 CONC nd easy to deal with; he was much liked by all. His second son was called Grettir. He was very hard to manage in his bringing up. He spoke little and was rough in his manners and quarrelsome, both in words and deeds. He got little
2 CONC  affection from his father Asmund, but his mother loved him dearly. Grettir was a handsome man in appearance, with a face rather broad and short, red-haired and somewhat freckled; not very precocious in his youth. There was a daug
2 CONC hter named Thordis, who afterwards married Glum the son of Ospak, Kjallak's son from Skridinsenni. Another daughter was named Rannveig; she married Gamli the son of Thorhall of Vineland, and they dwelt at Melar in Hrutafjord and h
2 CONC ad a son named Grim. Glum and Thordis had a son named Ospak who fell into a dispute with Odd the son of Ofeig, which is told of in the "Saga of the Banded Men."
2 CONT ://sagadb.org/grettis_saga.en2
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The saga of Hoard ch: 13 and 14 - page 659
2 CONT
