2 CONT William "Long Sword," was also known as Guillaume "Longue-Épée," Princeps Nortmannorum. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born say 892, "overseas" (not on the European mainland, and therefore possibly in Britain, Ireland, Scandinavia, or one of the islands held by Vikings, such as the Orkneys, Hebrides, Man, etc.--all plausible places for the 
2 CONC son of a Viking to be born.
2 CONT
2 CONT He subdued a rebellion by the Bretons, which gained him Brittany, the Channel Islands, the Contentin, and the Averanchin, in 930. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He is often given the anachronistic title of "duke of Normandy" though no contemporary source gives him even the title of count.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was killed on 17 December 942 in France in a treacherous ambush by Theodore of Blois and Arnulf of Flanders.
2 CONT
