2 CONT William the Longsword - Americans of Royal Descent, Charles H. Browning, p. 25
2 CONT William Longue-epee - p. 30; Longespada - COMYN4.TAF (Compuserve Roots), p. 5;
2 CONT COMYNI.GED shows mother as Gisela de France. NORM.TAF shows Poppa.  I suspect
2 CONT these are the same people and one of the parents is incorrect - NLP; Guillaume
2 CONT "Longaspada" de Normandie - COMYNI.GED (Compuserve);The Norman Conquest also
2 CONT gives his mother as Poppa - NLP;GWALTNEY.ANC (Compuserve) gives Gisela - NLP
2 CONT WILLIAM I, son of ROLLO the DANE and POPPA DE BAYEUX: Before he added the Cotentin or Cherbourg, peninsula to his domain, he may have had to suppress a Breton rising there, and then a revolt of
2 CONT  recalcitrant Danes.  It is possible that he invited new 
2 CONT Danish settlers to the Cotentin. He is said to have been a just and vigorous man, and in 942 he was murdered, at Picquigny on the Somme, by order of Arnulf of Flanders, who had forced a quarrel on
2 CONT  him in consequence of personal insult or some dispute 
2 CONT about an
2 CONT intervening property - The Conquest of England, Eric Linklater, p. 28
2 CONT Aceded 932 - http://gendex.com/users/daver/rigney/D0002/G0000093.html#I1245
