2 CONT QUAY 2
2 CONT
2 CONT William Longsword was killed in a rebellion of Rioulf of St. Savour in 933. He was supported by Anslech Turstain one of three barons who alone remained faithful and rendered military assistance to
2 CONT  the Duke, both descendants of Eisten Glumru by different wives. When William was assassinated the guardianship  of his new-born son, Duke Robert,was given to three men, one of whom was Anslech
2 CONT  Turstain. See notes under Anslech.
2 CONT
