2 CONT Guillaume I "Long Sword" Duke of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: A. Roots 121E; RC 166; Norr, p60; Coe; Guizot; Pfafman; AF; Kraentzler 1156, 1194, 1443, 1453; Davis; Ashley.
2 CONT William Longsword (Longaspatha), second Duke of Normandy, 917-943, andDuke of Aquitaine. He captured Britanny, Cotentin, the Channel Islands and the Avranchin, annexing them to his kingdom. He was slain by Arnulf ofFlanders.
2 CONT RC: William I "Longsword," Duke of Normandy; murdered 17 Dec. 943 in France.
2 CONT K: Guilaume I Longue Epee, Duke of Normandy.
2 CONT Roots: William I, "Longsword," born ca. 930, probably Rouen. Succeededto Duchy of Normandy about 927. In about 930 the Bretons rebelled. Hesubdued them, taking Brittany, the Channel Islands, Contentin and the Averanchin. Killed in
2 CONC  a treacherous ambush 17 Dec. 942 by servants of Theobald ofBlois and Arnulf of Flanders.
2 CONT Norr: William Longsword (Guillaume Longue-espee); son of Poppa; 2ndduke, 927-942; murdered.
2 CONT Ashley: William "Longsword", Count of Normandy.
2 CONT Davis: William I Longsword, ruled Normandy 931-942
2 CONT
