2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerloc (or Geirlaug), baptised in Rouen as Adela (or Adèle) in 912, was the daughter of Rollo, first duke of Normandy, and his wife, Poppa of Bayeux. She was the sister of Duke William Longsword.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 935, she married William Towhead, the future count of Poitou and duke of Aquitaine, then only ten years old. She gave him two children before dying on 14 October 962:
2 CONT
2 CONT William IV of Aquitaine
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaide of Aquitaine, wife of Hugh Capet
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerloc (or Geirlaug), baptised in Rouen as Adela (or Adèle) in 912, was the daughter of Rollo, first duke of Normandy, and his wife, Poppa of Bayeux. She was the sister of Duke William Longsword.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 935, she married William Towhead, the future count of Poitou and duke of Aquitaine. She gave him two children before dying on 14 October 962:
2 CONT
2 CONT William IV of Aquitaine 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaide of Aquitaine, wife of Hugh Capet 
2 CONT
2 CONT Retrieved from "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerloc"
