2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Aquitaine:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AQUITAINE.htm#Adelaisdied1004
2 CONT
2 CONT m (935) ADELA [Gerloc] de Normandie, daughter of ROBERT I [Rollo] Comte [de Normandie] & his [second] wife Popa [de Bayeux] (-after 969).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume de Jumièges names "Guillaume et…Gerloc" as children of Rollo and Poppa, in a later passage recording her marriage to "Guillaume comte de Poitou"[318].  Robert of Torigny also names "Willermum Longum Spatam et Gerloch" as
2 CONC  children of "Rollo dux Northmannorum" and Poppa[319].  The Chronicle of Adémar de Chabannes records the marriage of "filius Ranulfi Eblus" and "Adelam filiam Rosi Rotomagensis"[320].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronico Richardi Pictavensis also records that "Heblus…Pictavorum Comes et Dux Aquitaniæ duxit Adelam filiam Rolli Rothomagensis"[321].  This information is contradicted by other sources, is difficult to sustain from a chrono
2 CONC logical point of view, and is presumably in error.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She adopted the name ADELA when baptised.  "Guillelmi comitis, Adeleidis comitisse" subscribed a charter recording a donation to Cluny dated [963][322].  
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 Oct 962, Lothaire King of France granted her the right to dispose of extensive property in Poitiers, la Cour de Faye, effectively putting an end to the long dispute between her husband and the family of Hugues "Capet".  
2 CONT
2 CONT She used the property to found the Monastery of Sainte-Trinité[323].  "Vuillelmus dux Aquitanorum" donated property to Saint-Jean d'Angély for the soul of "…matre mea Addela…" by charter dated [971][324].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Guillaume III & his wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. GUILLAUME de Poitou ([937]-Saint-Maixent [end 995/early 996], bur Abbaye de Saint-Maixent[325], succeeded as Guillaume IV "Fier-a-Braz" Duke of Aquitaine, Guillaume II Comte de Poitou, m. Emma de Blois in 968)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. ADELAIS de Poitou ([950/55]-[1004], parentage not completely certain, m. Hugues des Francs, first King of France, OUR ANCESTOR - presumably.)
2 CONT
2 CONT From the French Wikipedia page on Adela de Normandie (morte en 962):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ad%C3%A8le_de_Normandie_(morte_en_962)
2 CONT
2 CONT Adèle de Normandie est la fille de Rollon le Marcheur et de Poppa de Bayeux, et la sœur du duc normand Guillaume Longue-Épée. Née sous le nom scandinave de Gerloc (Vieux Norrois : Geirlaug), elle est baptisée à Rouen sous le nom d
2 CONC ’Adèle en 912 ; en 935 elle est donnée pour épouse à Guillaume, futur comte de Poitiers et futur duc d'Aquitaine, alors âgé de dix ans. Elle meurt le 14 octobre 962.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle a deux enfants :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. le duc Guillaume Fierabrace (vers 935 - 993) ;
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. la princesse Adélaïde d'Aquitaine, épouse du premier roi capétien Hugues Capet.
2 CONT
2 CONT In English:
2 CONT
2 CONT Adela of Normandy was the daughter of Rollon "le Marcheur" ("the Walker") and Poppa of Bayeux, sister of the Duke of Normandy Guillaume "Long-Epee" ("Longsword"). Born under the Scandinavian name Gerloc (Old Norse: Geirlaug), she 
2 CONC was baptized in Rouen using the name Adele in 912. In 935, she was given in marriage to Guillaume, the future Comte de Poitou and Duke of Aquitaine, then at age 10 (obviously incorrect, probably a betrothal age). She died on 14 Oc
2 CONC tober 962.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Duke William "Fierabrace" (c. 935-993)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Princess Adelaide of Aquitaine, wife of the first Capetian King Hugh Capet.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
