1 NOTE {geni:about_me} #According to The Royal Genealogies Website (ROYAL92.GED), online (http://www.daml.org/2001/01/gedcom/royal92.ged. Hereinafter cited as Royal Genealogies Website). Kathlin is indeed the daughter of Poppa. There she
2 CONC  is named as Kaithlin de Normandi [Anna Pétursdottir].
2 CONT
2 CONT The unknown mother of Kaðlin (Kathline), perhaps from Scotland or maybe Iceland. Kaðlín (Kathline) was abducted when Vikings raided Scotland and her birthplace/country is unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Landnamabok (Thee Book of Settlements in Iceland) Gangu-Hrólfr had a daughter from his time in Scotland who was abducted in a raid by the Vikings.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to "The Book of Settlerments/Landnamabok" and "Laxdaela" Kaðlín was a daughter of Rollo, both books were written in the 12th and 13th centuries. 
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landn%C3%A1mab%C3%B3k
