1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Halvdan Svarte (Haraldsson) (Hálfdan svarti) ca ?-934, PAM
2 CONT
2 CONT (In English: Halfdan the Black (Haraldsson))
2 CONT
2 CONT King in part of Norway: Trondheimen
2 CONT
2 CONT http://lind.no/nor/index.asp?lang=gb&emne=nor&person=Halvdan%20Svarte%20%28Haraldsson%29&list=&vis=
2 CONT
2 CONT Merge warning: Do not merge with his grandfather with the same name or his brother Halftan Haraldsson «the White» Kvite!
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan Haraldsson or Halfdan the Black (not to be confused with his grandfather and namesake) was a son of Harald I of Norway by his first wife, Åsa, the daughter of Jarl Håkon Grjotgardsson of Lade. He was made sub-king of the T
2 CONC rondelag by his father, along with his brother Halfdan the White. According to Heimskringla, Halfdan the Black was poisoned, possibly at the behest of his sister in law Gunnhild, Mother of Kings.
