1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT http://home.sol.no/~nermo/slekt/d0007/g0000084.html#7070 +
1 NOTE Living about 870.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Harald Hårfagre's Saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "3. OF GYDA, DAUGHTER OF EIRIK.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Harald sent his men to a girl called Gyda, daughter of King Eirik of Hordaland, who was brought up as foster-child in the house of a great bonde in Valdres. The king wanted her for his concubine; for she was a remarkably hand
2 CONC some girl, but of high spirit withal. Now when the messengers came there, and delivered their errand to the girl, she answered, that she would not throw herself away even to take a king for her husband, who had no greater kingdom 
2 CONC to rule over than a few districts. "And methinks," said she, "it is wonderful that no king here in Norway will make the whole country subject to him, in the same way as Gorm the Old did in Denmark, or Eirik at Upsala." The messeng
2 CONC ers thought her answer was dreadfully haughty, and asked what she thought would come of such an answer; for Harald was so mighty a man, that his invitation was good enough for her. But although she had replied to their errand diff
2 CONC erently from what they wished, they saw no chance, on this occasion, of taking her with them against her will; so they prepared to return. When they were ready, and the people followed them out, Gyda said to the messengers, "Now t
2 CONC ell to King Harald these my words. I will only agree to be his lawful wife upon the condition that he shall first, for my sake, subject to himself the whole of Norway, so that he may rule over that kingdom as freely and fully as K
2 CONC ing Eirik over the Swedish dominions, or King Gorm over Denmark; for only then, methinks, can he be called the king of a people." "
2 CONT
2 CONT "4. KING HARALD'S VOW.
2 CONT
2 CONT Now came the messengers back to King Harald, bringing him the words of the girl, and saying she was so bold and foolish that she well deserved that the king should send a greater troop of people for her, and inflict on her some di
2 CONC sgrace. Then answered the king, "This girl has not spoken or done so much amiss that she should be punished, but rather she should be thanked for her words. She has reminded me," said he, "of something which it appears to me wonde
2 CONC rful I did not think of before. And now," added he, "I make the solemn vow, and take God to witness, who made me and rules over all things, that never shall I clip or comb my hair until I have subdued the whole of Norway, with sca
2 CONC t (1), and duties, and domains; or if not, have died in the attempt." Guthorm thanked the king warmly for his vow; adding, that it was royal work to fulfil royal words."
2 CONT
2 CONT ENDNOTES:
2 CONT (1) Scat was a land-tax, paid to the king in money, malt, meal, or flesh-meat, from all lands, and was adjudged by the Thing to each king upon his accession, and being proposed and accepted as king.
2 CONT
2 CONT "21. HARALD'S MARRIAGE AND HIS CHILDREN.
2 CONT
2 CONT When King Harald had now become sole king over all Norway, he remembered what that proud girl had said to him; so he sent men to her, and had her brought to him, and took her to his bed. And these were their children: Alof -- she 
2 CONC was the eldest; then was their son Hrorek; then Sigtryg, Frode, and Thorgils."
1 NOTE Gyda Eiriksdotter (Gyða Eiríksdóttir) var en av Harald Hårfagres hustruer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hun var datter av Kong Eirik fra Hordaland. Sammen med Harald Hårfagre fikk hun barna Ålov Årbot, Rørek, Sigtrygg, Frode og Torgils.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gyda har fått æren for Harald Hårfagres tilnavn, ?Hårfagre?. Harald hadde forelsket seg i denne kongsdatteren (datter til Kong Eirik av Hordaland), som ble fostret opp av en rik bonde i Valdres. Han sendte sine sendemenn for å
2 CONC  hente henne, men hun ville ikke ha Harald, fordi han ikke var mektig nok. Hun lurte på hvorfor han ikke hadde lagt hele Norge under seg. Han ble slett ikke fornærmet av det hun sa, men tok utfordringen, og lovte å ikke klippe s
2 CONC eg før han hadde samlet hele landet under seg. Da han hadde greid denne oppgave, giftet de seg.
