1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Sigtrygg Haraldsson''' (Sigtryggur Haraldsson)
2 CONT
2 CONT SIGGTRYGG.  Snorre names "Alof…the eldest…their son Hrorek, then Sigtryg, Frode and Thorgils" as the children of King Harald and his wife Gyda[78].  The Historia Norwegie names "Sigtrygr" as twelfth son of "Haraldus Comatus"[79]. 
2 CONC  Under his father's division of territories, Vingulmark, Raumarike, Vestfold and Thelamark were granted to Olav, Björn, Sigtryg, Frode and Thorgils[80].  
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWAY.htm#AlofAarbodMThoreRagnvaldssonA
2 CONT
2 CONT 20. Kong Harald var nu bleven enevældig over hele Norge. Da mindedes han det, som den storsindede mø havde talt til ham[42]; han sendte da mænd til hende, lod hende føre til sig og giftede sig med hende. Disse var deres børn: Aalo
2 CONC v var ældst, saa kom Rørek, saa Sigtryg Frode og Torgils
2 CONT
2 CONT The  Norwegian historian [http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Andreas_Munch P.A.Munch] claims that [http://www.geni.com/people/Svanhild-Svanhildi-Eysteinsdotter/6000000004286962211 Svanhild Eysteinsdotter] is the mother, but [http:
2 CONC //lind.no/nor/index.asp?lang=gb&emne=asatru&person=&list=&vis=s_b_harald_harfagre Snorre Sturluson: Heimskringla] states that Gyda is the mother and that Sigtrygg is their third child.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no known spouses and descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p4273.htm#i42730
2 CONT * http://lind.no/nor/index.asp?lang=&emne=nor&person=Sigtrygg%20Haraldsson
