2 NOTE The selected region shows an anachronistic portrait of King Duncan I of Scotland (Donnchad mac Crínáin). He ruled from 1034 until his death in 1040.Key Historical FactsThe Real Figure: Unlike the elderly, wise king depicted in Wil
3 CONC liam Shakespeare’s tragedy Macbeth, the real-life King Duncan was relatively young when he died. He was defeated and killed in battle near Elgin by his cousin and rival, Macbeth.Artwork Origin: This likeness is a colorized version
3 CONC  of a line engraving created by artist Isaac Taylor. It depicts the king in profile wearing classical plate armor and a Renaissance-style cap.Legacy: He was the first monarch of the House of Dunkeld line. His son later took back t
3 CONC he throne as King Malcolm III Canmore.If you are interested in researching this era further, let me know if you would like to look into:The differences between historical facts and Shakespeare's theatrical adaptationThe genealogy 
