2 CONT We know of Maldred from the book "Records of the Heath Family", 1913 by George Heath.  The entry reads as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred, son of "Crinan the Thane," was born about 1004, and married, about 1030, Aldgitha, daughter of Uchtred, Earl of Northumberland and granddaughter of AEthelred, King of England, who was the great-great- grandson of Alfred, 
2 CONC King of England. Maldred's successors were, therefore, directly descended from Alfred the Great. Maldred was brother, as well as neighbour, of "the gracious Duncan," who was King of Cumbria for about sixteen years before he succee
2 CONC ded his maternal grandfather, Malcolm II as King of Scotland on the 25th November, 1034.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had three sons: (1) Gospatric, who succeeded him; (2) Robert, Prior of Hexham; and (3) Uchtred, also Prior of Hexham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred died about 1066.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.jjhc.info/maldred1066.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Crínán of Dunkeld (died 1045) was the lay abbot of the diocese of Dunkeld, and perhaps the Mormaer of Atholl. Crínán was progenitor of the House of Dunkeld, the dynasty who would rule Scotland until the later 13th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Crinán was married to Bethoc, daughter of King Malcolm II of Scotland (reigned 1005-1034). As Malcolm II had no son, the strongest hereditary claim to the Scottish throne descended through Bethóc, and Crinán's eldest son Donnchad 
2 CONC I (reigned 1034-1040), became King of Scots. Some sources indicate that Malcolm II designated Duncan as his successor under the rules of tanistry because there were other possible claimants to the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Crinán's second son, Maldred of Allerdale, held the title of Lord of Cumbria. It is said that from him, the Earls of Dunbar, for example Patrick Dunbar, 9th Earl of Dunbar, descend in unbroken male line. - [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT [1] - http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cr’n‡n_of_Dunkeld
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Died in rebellion against Macbeth at Dunkeld.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
