2 CONT We know of Maldred from the book "Records of the Heath Family", 1913 by George Heath. The entry reads as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred, son of "Crinan the Thane," was born about 1004, and married, about 1030, Aldgitha, daughter of Uchtred, Earl of Northumberland and granddaughter of AEthelred, King of England, who was the great-great- grandson of Alfred, 
2 CONC King of England. Maldred's successors were, therefore, directly descended from Alfred the Great. Maldred was brother, as well as neighbour, of "the gracious Duncan," who was King of Cumbria for about sixteen years before he succee
2 CONC ded his maternal grandfather, Malcolm II as King of Scotland on the 25th November, 1034.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had three sons: (1) Gospatric, who succeeded him; (2) Robert, Prior of Hexham; and (3) Uchtred, also Prior of Hexham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred died about 1066.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. The book "Records of the Heath Family", 1913 by George Heath.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. jj@jjhc.info
2 CONT
2 CONT Crínán of Dunkeld
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Crinán's second son, Maldred of Allerdale, held the title of Lord of Cumbria. It is said that from him, the Earls of Dunbar, for example Patrick Dunbar, 9th Earl of Dunbar, descend in unbroken male line.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10665.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred, Lord of Allerdale1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #106641, b. circa 1015, d. 1045
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=21 Aug 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred, Lord of Allerdale was born circa 1015 at Dunbar, Scotland.3 He was the son of Crinan of Atholl, Mormaer of Atholl and Bethoc of Scotland.2 He married Ealdgyth of Northumberland, daughter of Uhtred, Earl of Northumberland 
2 CONC and Ælfgifu (?), circa 1036.3 He died in 1045, killed in action, while attempting to avenge the murder of his brother by Macbeth.2 Maldred, Lord of Allerdale gained the title of Lord of Allerdale [Feudal].4 He held the office of R
2 CONC egent of the Kingdom of Strathclyde between 1034 and 1045.2 Children of Maldred, Lord of Allerdale and Ealdgyth of Northumberland
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred (?)+ 5
2 CONT
2 CONT unknown of Scotland+ 5
2 CONT
2 CONT Gospatric, Earl of Northumberland+ b. c 1040, d. c 10752
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 23. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family, page 178.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S125] Richard Glanville-Brown, online <e-mail address>, Richard Glanville-Brown (RR 2, Milton, Ontario, Canada), downloaded 17 August 2005.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 13. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 10
2 CONC 6th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family, page 179.
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.rpi.edu/~holmes/Hobbies/Genealogy/ps06/ps06_058.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred is the younger son; his illigitimate male line still exists in the family of Dunbar. He was Lord of Carlisle and Allendale. He and Ealdgith are given as parents of Gospatrick by "The Prescott Family of America," Doris Clin
2 CONC e Ward (2nd Ed., 1977). See "The Scots Peerage," James Balfour Paul (Edinburg: David Douglas, 1906), pp. 240-41. He was Regent of Strathclyde in 1034.
2 CONT
2 CONT References: [PRES.GED],[AR7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred mac Crínán was brother of Duncan I, King of Scots, also our ancestor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred married Ealdgyth of Northumberland, daughter of Uhtred "the Bold", Earl of Northumbria and Ælfgifu of Wessex, before 1040.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred was present when Duncan was slain by his cousin Macbeth on 14 August 1040 near Elgin, Moray, Scotland. Macbeth had joined forces with the invading Northmen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred was placed on the throne of Scotland by Siward, Earl of Northumbria, in 1045, but he was slain in battle during that year at the age of 40; he was attempting to avenge the murder of his brother by Macbeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p341.htm#i7942 )
2 CONT
2 CONT from Compiler: R. B. Stewart, Evans, GA
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/index.htm )
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Maldred FitzCrinan: Occupation 1: Bet. 1034 - 1040, King of Scots. Occupation 2: Feudal Lord Allerdale. Residence: Atterdale Died in battle, slain attempting to avenge murder by MacBeth Maldred, Lord of Allerdale was bo
2 CONC rn circa 1015 at Dunbar, East Lothian, Scotland.2 He was the son of Crínáin of Dunkeld, Mormaer of Atholl and Bethoc of Alba.3 He married Ealdgyth (?), daughter of Uhtred, Earl of Northumberland and Ælfgifu (?), circa 1036.2 He di
2 CONC ed in 1045, killed in action, while attempting to avenge the murder of his brother by Macbeth.3 He gained the title of Lord of Allerdale [feudal barony].4 He held the office of Regent of the Kingdom of Strathclyde between 1034 and
2 CONC  1045.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Maldred, Lord of Allerdale and Ealdgyth (?)
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred (?)+5 unknown of Scotland+5 Gospatric, Earl of Northumberland+3 b. bt 1040 - 1048, d. c 1075 Citations
2 CONT
