2 CONC rsson”[221].  m [https://www.geni.com/people/Paul-av-Orkn%C3%B8yene/6000000000424848932?through=6000000003645825356  PAUL Thorfinsson] Joint Jarl of Orkney, son of THORFINN "the Black" Jarl of Orkney & his wife Ingibjörg Finnsdatt
2 CONC er (-in prison Bergen 1098).''' [https://www.geni.com/discussions/248662?msg=1558827 see birthdate discussion, IF her mother is Ragnhidr Magnusdottir] 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#DauHaakonMPaulThorfinssonOrkneydied1098
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT Daughter of Hákon Ivarsson av Norge, married Paul Thorfinnsson Orkneyjarl. First name unknown, but could be Ragnhild like her mother. [The Norse were not given to repeating names from one generation to the next, so this is not as 
2 CONC likely as it might have been in, say, England. Maven.]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT NN daughter.  Orkneyinga Saga records that “Earl Paul Thorfinnson” married “a daughter of Earl Hakon Ivarsson”[221].  m PAUL Thorfinsson Joint Jarl of Orkney, son of THORFINN "the Black" Jarl of Orkney & his wife Ingibjörg Finnsda
2 CONC tter (-in prison Bergen 1098). 
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#PaulIdied1098B
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#DauHaakonMPaulThorfinssonOrkneydied1098
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT PAUL Thorfinnsson, son of THORFINN II "the Black" Jarl of Orkney & his wife Ingibjörg Finnsdatter (-in prison Bergen 1098, bur Bergen).
2 CONT
2 CONT Orkneyinga Saga names “Paul and…Erlend” as the two sons of Jarl Thorfinn and his wife who survived childhood[309]. He succeeded his father [1065] as Joint Jarl of Orkney, jointly with his brother. Morkinskinna records that Harald 
2 CONC III King of Norway sailed to Orkney en route for his invasion of England in 1066 and “recruited the aid of Jarl Thorfinn´s sons Páll and Erlendr”[310]. He may have fought with his father at Stamford Bridge 1066[311]. Orkneyinga Sa
2 CONC ga records that Magnus "Barelegs" King of Norway “seized the Earls, Paul and Erlend” on his arrival in Orkney, “sent them east to Norway, and made his own son Sigurd overlord of the islands with regents to govern the earldom”, add
2 CONC ing in a later passage that Paul “was buried at Bergen”[312]. He was deposed and imprisoned in 1098 by Magnus "Barelegs" King of Norway, and died in Bergen according to Snorre[313].
2 CONT
2 CONT m --- '''Haakonsdatter, daughter of HAAKON Ivarsson & his wife Ragnhild Magnusdatter of Norway. Orkneyinga Saga records that “Earl Paul Thorfinnson” married “a daughter of Earl Hakon Ivarsson”'''[314].
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul & his wife had children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. HAKON Paulsson (before [1070]-Orkney [1126]). Orkneyinga Saga names “Hakon” as son of “Earl Paul Thorfinnson” and his wife[315]. It is extremely unlikely that Hakon was born before [1070], given the estimated birth date of his 
2 CONC granddaughter Margaret (see below). Snorre names "Hakon, a son of Earl Paul" when recording that "a year or two after King Magnus's fall…[he] came from Orkney" and was given the earldom of Orkney by Kings Eystein, Sigurd and Olav,
2 CONC  before sailing back to Orkney[316]. Orkneyinga Saga records that Hakon left Orkney for Norway where he visited “King Olaf the Peaceful…towards the end of Olaf´s reign” (King Olaf´s death is dated to 1093) before sailing east to S
2 CONC weden and “King Ingi Steinkelsson”[317]. He was appointed Joint Lieutenant for Sigurd Magnusson King of Orkney and the Isles, when the latter returned to Norway in 1103 on his accession as king. He was installed in [Spring 1105] a
2 CONC s Jarl of Orkney by King Sigurd. He ruled as Joint Jarl from Spring 1108, when his cousin Magnus Erlendsson was installed as Jarl of ½ Orkney. He later quarrelled with his cousin, took him prisoner on Egilsay and had him killed. O
2 CONC rkneyinga Saga records that “Earl Hakon Paulsson died in his bed in Orkney”[318].
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---. The name of Hakon´s wife is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (1): HELGA, daughter of MODDAN of Dalr in Caithness & his wife ---. Orkneyinga Saga names “Helga” daughter of “a farmer…Moddan…living in the Dales of Caithness” as “Earl Hakon´s mistress”[319]. Her stepson banished her an
2 CONC d her sister Frakok to the latter's estates in Helmsdale, Sutherland after the death of her son [1131].
2 CONT
2 CONT Hakon & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT a) PAUL [II] Hakonsson "the Silent" (-after 1137). Orkneyinga Saga records that earl Hakon “had another son Paul…the Silent”[320]. He succeeded his father in [1126] as Joint Jarl of Orkney and Caithness, jointly with his half-brot
2 CONC her, sole Jarl after the latter's death in [1131]. His second cousin, Kali-Ragnvald, rebelled in 1135 and demanded a half share of Orkney. In revenge for being refused, the latter seized Shetland in 1136, but Paul [II] defeated hi
2 CONC m in Yell Sound 27 Jun 1136. The following year he again seized the Shetlands, and captured and deposed Paul [II] in 1137.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hakon had three illegitimate children by Mistress (1):
2 CONT
2 CONT b) HARALD [I] "Slettmali/Smooth-spoken" (before [1090]-[1131]). Orkneyinga Saga names “Harald…Smooth-Tongue and two daughters…Ingibjorg…Margaret” as the children of Earl Hakon and his mistress Helga[321]. It is unlikely that Haral
2 CONC d was born later than [1090] if the estimated birth date of his daughter Margaret is correct. He succeeded his father in [1126] as Joint Jarl of Orkney and Caithness, jointly with his half-brother. Orkneyinga Saga records that he 
2 CONC died after trying on a poisoned garment prepared by his mother and intended for his half-brother Paul[322].
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---. The name of Harald´s wife is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT i) ERLEND Haraldsson (-murdered Damsay Dec 1156). Orkneyinga Saga names “Erlend” as son of “Harald Smooth-Tongue” when recording that he was reared by Frakokk, sister of his paternal grandmother[323]. Eystein II King of Norway gav
2 CONC e him permission in Autumn 1151 to administer ½ Orkney during the absence of Jarl Kali-Ragnvald, but he was unable to impose his claim. He was recognised as Earl of ½ Caithness by Malcolm IV King of Scotland 24 May 1153, in opposi
2 CONC tion to his first cousin Harald Maddadsson, during the absence of Jarl Kali-Ragnvald. He was invested as Jarl of Orkney in 1153 by King Eystein II, invaded Orkney and defeated Jarl Harald [II] at Kiarrek-Stadir 28/29 Sep 1154, for
2 CONC cing him to surrender his share of Orkney. He was dispossessed of Orkney by Jarl Kali-Ragnvald in Sep 1156 after the latter's return. After a brief revival as Jarl following his defeat of Jarl Harald [III] 24 Oct 1156, he was once
2 CONC  more defeated by Kali-Ragnvald and killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT c) INGIBJÖRG . Orkneyinga Saga names “Harald…Smooth-Tongue and two daughters…Ingibjorg…Margaret” as the children of Earl Hakon and his mistress Helga, adding that Ingibjörg married “Olaf Tit-Bit King of the Hebrides”[324].
2 CONT
2 CONT m [as his second wife], OLAV Bitling King of Sodor and Man 1097-1098 and 1103-1153, son of ---. Olav & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT i) GODROD . His parentage is deduced from the Orkneyinga Saga which records that the mother of “Rognvald Godrodarson, King of the Hebrides” was “Ingibjorg, Earl Hakon Paulsson´s daughter”[325].
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---. The name of Godrod´s wife is not known. Godrod & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT (a) RAGNVALD Godradarson . King of Man and the Isles. Orkneyinga Saga records that the mother of “Rognvald Godrodarson, King of the Hebrides” was “Ingibjorg, Earl Hakon Paulsson´s daughter”[326]. William "the Lion" King of Scotlan
2 CONC d sold Caithness to him after the battle of Wick in 1198. He lost Caithness to Harald [II] Maddadsson Jarl of Orkney in 1200.
2 CONT
2 CONT d) MARGARET (before [1115]-). Orkneyinga Saga names “Harald…Smooth-Tongue and two daughters…Ingibjorg…Margaret” as the children of Earl Hakon and his mistress Helga[327]. It is unlikely that Margaret was born after [1115] if it is
2 CONC  correct that her son was born in 1134. Orkneyinga Saga records that “Margaret Hakon´s-Daughter” married “Earl Maddad of Atholl”[328]. Orkneyinga Saga records that “Erlend the Young” abducted Margaret from Orkney and took her to S
2 CONC hetland, and that her son eventually granted permission for their marriage[329].
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([1133]) as his second wife, MADDAD [Madach] Earl of Atholl, son of MAELMUIRE [brother of MALCOLM III Caennmor King of Scotland] (-[1142/52]).
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly ERLAND "Ungi/the Young" (-killed 1156).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. THORA Paulsdatter . Orkneyinga Saga names (in order) “Thora…Ingirid…Herbjorg…Ragnhild” as the daughters of “Earl Paul Thorfinnson” and his wife, adding that Thora married “in Norway…Halldor, the son of Brynjolf Camel” and that 
2 CONC their son was “Brynjolf, the father of Halldor who married Gudrid Dag´s-Daughter”[330].
2 CONT
2 CONT m HALLDOR, son of BRYNIOLF Camel & his wife ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. INGRID Paulsdatter . Orkneyinga Saga names (in order) “Thora…Ingirid…Herbjorg…Ragnhild” as the daughters of “Earl Paul Thorfinnson” and his wife, adding that Ingrid married “Einar Vorse-Raven”[331].
2 CONT
2 CONT m EINAR Vorsa-Krakr.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. HERBJÖRG Paulsdatter . Orkneyinga Saga names (in order) “Thora…Ingirid…Herbjorg…Ragnhild” as the daughters of “Earl Paul Thorfinnson” and his wife, adding that Herbjörg was the mother of “Ingibjorg the High-born, who married Si
2 CONC gurd of Westness, their sons were Hakon Pike-Staff and Brynjolf” and of “Hakon the Child and of Herborg whom Kolbein Heap married”[332].
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. RAGNHILD Paulsdatter . Orkneyinga Saga names (in order) “Thora…Ingirid…Herbjorg…Ragnhild” as the daughters of “Earl Paul Thorfinnson” and his wife, adding that Ragnhild was mother of “Benedikt, father of Ingibjorg, mother of Er
2 CONC ling the archdeacon” and “a daughter…Bergljot, who married Havard Gunnason, and their sons were Magnus, Hakon Claw, Dufniall and Thorstein”[333].
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
