2 CONT # Note: One source says father of Gudrod "The Magnificent". The other source has White Leg as gr grandfather. The latter is my genealogy, with Halfdan "The Old" being father of Gudrod.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Note: Title: Royal Families of Medieval Scandinavia, Flanders, and Kiev, by Rupert Alen & Anna Dahlquist, 1997, King's River Publ., Page: 7 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 48. HALFDAN HVITBEIN MADE KING.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those of the Swedes who had more understanding found that the
2 CONT
2 CONT dear times proceeded from there being a greater number of people
2 CONT
2 CONT on the land than it could support, and that the king could not be
2 CONT
2 CONT blamed for this. They took the resolution, therefore, to cross
2 CONT
2 CONT the Eida forest with all their men, and came quite unexpectedly
2 CONT
2 CONT into Soleyar, where they put to death King Solve, and took
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan Hvitbein prisoner, and made him their chief, and gave him
2 CONT
2 CONT the title of king. Thereupon he subdued Soleyar, and proceeding
2 CONT
2 CONT with his army into Raumarike, plundered there, and laid that
2 CONT
2 CONT district also in subjection by force of arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT 49. OF HALFDAN HVITBEIN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan Hvitbein became a great king. He was married to Aasa, a
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of Eystein the Severe, who was king of the Upland
2 CONT
2 CONT people, and ruled over Hedemark. Halfdan and Aasa had two sons,
2 CONT
2 CONT Eystein and Gudrod. Halfdan subdued a great part of Hedemark,
2 CONT
2 CONT Toten, Hadeland, and much of Westfold. He lived to be an old
2 CONT
2 CONT man, and died in his bed at Toten, from whence his body was
2 CONT
2 CONT transported to Westfold, and was buried under a mound at a place
2 CONT
2 CONT called Skaereid, at Skiringsale. So says Thjodolf: --
2 CONT
2 CONT "Halfdan, esteemed by friends and foes,
2 CONT
2 CONT Receives at last life's deep repose:
2 CONT
2 CONT The aged man at last, though late,
2 CONT
2 CONT Yielded in Toten to stern fate.
2 CONT
2 CONT At Skiringsale hangs o'er his grave
2 CONT
2 CONT A rock, that seems to mourn the brave Halfdan,
2 CONT
2 CONT to chiefs and people dear,
2 CONT
2 CONT Received from all a silent tear."
2 CONT
2 CONT ***********************
2 CONT
