2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT King of Raumerike Hálfdan Hvítbeinn Óláfsson was King of Raumerike between 710 and 750. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was brought up in Soleyar, in the house of his mother's brother Solve. He subdued Soleyar (his foster father's homeland), and then proceeded with his army into Raumarike, plundered there, and laid that district also in subjecti
2 CONC on by force of arms. He subdued a great part of Hedemark, Toten, Hadeland, and much of Westfold. He took possession of Värmland after his brothers death, raised scatt (tax) from it, and placed earls over it as long as he lived.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was captured by the Swedes who had killed his uncle, and made their Chief (in deference to his Yngling blood?). 
2 CONT
2 CONT He also went by the name of Halfdan "White Leg."
2 CONT
2 CONT He founded a pagan temple at Skaereid, Skiringsale. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Ása Eysteinsdóttir, daughter of Eysteinn Hardrádi of Uppland and Sólveig Hálfdanardóttir 
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived to be an old man (an unusual accomplishment in those days), and died in his bed at Toten. His body was transported to Westfold, and was buried under a mound at a place called Skaereid, at Skiringsale.
2 CONT
2 CONT So says Thjodolf:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Halfdan, esteemed by friends and foes,
2 CONT
2 CONT Receives at last life's deep repose:
2 CONT
2 CONT The aged man at last, though late,
2 CONT
2 CONT Yielded in Toten to stern fate.
2 CONT
2 CONT At Skiringsale hangs o'er his grave
2 CONT
2 CONT A rock, that seems to mourn the brave Halfdan,
2 CONT
2 CONT to chiefs and people dear,
2 CONT
2 CONT Received from all a silent tear."
2 CONT
