1 CONT AFN: 9G9P-C0
0 @N6000000002187891797@ NOTE Caustantín of the Picts
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Caustantín (Scottish Gaelic: Caustantín mac Fergusa) was king of Dál Riata and king of the Picts or Fortriu, in modern Scotland, from 789 until 820. He is credited with having founded the church at Dunkeld which later received rel
1 CONC ics of St Columba from Iona.
1 CONT
1 CONT He is thought to be the king commemorated on Dupplin Cross. He may have been a grandson of Onuist son of Urguist. He was a brother of Óengus mac Fergusa, and uncle of Uen. He was the father of Drust.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Eochaid IV King of Dál Riada
1 CONT 789-820 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Óengus (II) 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Conall King of Pictavia
1 CONT 789-820 
