0 @N6000000002176675512@ NOTE Scottish history is said to have started with the mission of St. Columba in
1 CONT 563. Columba was an Irishman of Noble birth who became a priest and a monk
1 CONT and settled in Iona to undertake conversions of heathen North Britain.
1 CONT Iona was a small kingdom of Dalriada founded by the race to which Columba
1 CONT belonged. The Scots came from Ireland, a Christian land from Roman times.
1 CONT Columba died in 597 leaving his most important work: the re-conversion of the
1 CONT North of England to Christianity. His feast day is June 9th.
