0 @N6000000001353843038@ NOTE Donald II (889 - 900)
1 CONT King of the Scots (from 889), son of Constantine I and successor to Eochaid and Giric (reigned 878-889). His reign coincided with renewed invasions by the Danes, who came less to plunder and more to occupy thelands bordering Scotl
1 CONC and and the Anglo-Saxon kingdoms. He was also embroiled in efforts to reduce the highland robber tribes. By one account he was slain at Dunnottar, meeting a Danish invasion; by another hedied of infirmity brought on by his campaig
1 CONC ns against the highlanders. He was succeeded by his cousin Constantine II.
0 @N6000000001354412033@ NOTE Donald II (889 - 900)
1 CONT King of the Scots (from 889), son of Constantine I and successor to Eochaid and Giric (reigned 878-889). His reign coincided with renewed invasions by the Danes, who came less to plunder and more to occupy thelands bordering Scotl
1 CONC and and the Anglo-Saxon kingdoms. He was also embroiled in efforts to reduce the highland robber tribes. By one account he was slain at Dunnottar, meeting a Danish invasion; by another hedied of infirmity brought on by his campaig
1 CONC ns against the highlanders. He was succeeded by his cousin Constantine II.
