0 @N6000000003232674923@ NOTE Alias:<ALIA> Malcolm I of Alba/, Milcolumbus
1 CONT Cause of Death:<CAUS>
1 CONT Some sources list his death in 958.
1 CONT
1 CONT [Sargent.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Malcolm I (ruled 943-954). Malcolm I succeeded his second cousin Constantine II, who abdicated to enter a monastery. In 954 Malcolm captured Moray, a kingdom to the north, and killed its king. He also made a pact to assist England
1 CONC  against the Scandinavians, but he later turned against his allies and captured territory in northern England. Malcolm was killed while trying to put down a rebellion in Moray. Constantine II named his second cousin Malcolm as suc
1 CONC cessor. In those days, in order to stamp your authority as a King, you were expected to wage war and claim your prizes as any strong, worthwhile King would--and Malcolm was good at this part of the job. Cleverly allied with the En
1 CONC glish now, Malcolm and his new found friends marched on to stamp out the Scandinavian threat from Ireland. But in 950, with a little pushing from Monk Constantine, Malcolm moved into England and started taking the northern territo
1 CONC ries there.
1 CONT
1 CONT However, on his return from his crusade in 954, Malcolm had now found that his own northerly regions had revolted and in a brief conflict with them they killed him at Fordoun in the Mearns.
1 CONT
1 CONT http://www.highlanderweb.co.uk/monarch2.htm
1 CONT
1 CONT King of Scots 943. Killed by the men of Moray 954.
