0 @N6000000003796223591@ NOTE [Geoffrey De Normandie, Gedcom BSJTK Smith Family Tree.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT Note:
1 CONT Name Suffix: Earl of Orkney
1 CONT
1 CONT The data in this section of royal Norwegian genealogy was compiled by
1 CONT historians, Anders Stilloff, and Ola Robøle Hegge of Norway and presented
1 CONT in chart format by Carl M. Ringen Gunderson. The lineage presented here
1 CONT was given to meas part of my ancestry by genealogist Betty Rockswold,
1 CONT associated with the Valdres Samband Lag organization. When asked about 
1 CONT the research done on the lineage, she said: "It would take a 'volume' to
1 CONT describe the connections to royalty of the Kvåle line." She goes on to 
1 CONT saythat she sent a copy of the material to her skeptic cousin, Herman
1 CONT Nettum, in East Toten who is a noted genealogist. After examination of 
1 CONT the chart, which Betty says she is sure he went over with a 'fine tooth
1 CONT comb' hunting for errors, his only criticism was that,while the lineage
1 CONT was correct, no one knowsthe first name of Earl Thorfinn Sigurdson's
1 CONT wife which was listed as being Ingeborg. It appears that the lineage in
1 CONT this database links to Scandinavian royalty insofar as the genealogy
1 CONT accounts written by the medieval writers is correct. The vice consul of
1 CONT Norway, Lars Løberg, says that the medieval writers, most notably Snorri
1 CONT Sturluson, may have had a political motive for presenting the royal line
1 CONT as an old Norwegian dynasty. Since the lineage in this database ties to
1 CONT the traditionallyaccepted royalty line, it is presented here.)
0 @N6000000003796259385@ NOTE [Geoffrey De Normandie, Gedcom BSJTK Smith Family Tree.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT Dead
0 @N6000000003174381344@ NOTE
1 CONT Called “Turf Eynor” because he taught the islanders how to cut and burn turf. He was one-eyed and famed for his cunning.
0 @N6000000003232675259@ NOTE [Sargent.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [Direct Linage1.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Note:
1 CONT bk&q chart 27, NB5, pp 425, 441, 444, 446
1 CONT
1 CONT Earl of Orkney c894-?920.
1 CONT He was known as Torf-Einar because he introduced turf as a fuel to the islanders. He was the brother of the disgraced Hallad who had been unable to control the Danish pirates in the western seas. Einar pleaded with his father to l
1 CONC et him have the responsibility. He was given one longship and crew. He sailed first to the Shetlands to recruit more men and then advanced on the leaders of the Danish Vikings, Þori Treebeard and Kalf Skurfa, whom he killed, regai
1 CONC ning control of the Orkneys. Soon after the Orkneys were invaded by Halfdan Háleg, the son of the Norwegian king. Halfdan had already killed Einar's father, Ragnald, and seemed intent on wiping out Ragnald's family. Einar escaped 
1 CONC but conducted a surprise raid and captured Halfdan, whom he killed by carving an eagle shape out of his body in revenge for the death of his father. He sacrificed the remains to Odin. Harald Finehair brought his fleet to the Orkne
1 CONC ys and exacted compensation from Einar for the death of his son, but he allowed him to retain his title as Earl of Orkney. Although Einar is described as ugly, with one blind eye, he was remembered as a strong leader who protected
1 CONC  his islanders, though in return confiscated their independent tenure and treated them as tenants. He apparently ruled much of the territory conquered by Sigurd and Þorstein, which included Caithness and Sutherland and parts of Ro
1 CONC ss. The date of his death is not recorded, though the sagas note that he ruled for a long time and died of a sickness. Allowing for the ages of his sons to succeed him he must have ruled to at least the year 920 or even later.
0 @N6000000003232733071@ NOTE Alias:<ALIA> Einar Truf Rognvaldson/
1 CONT
1 CONT Per Nermo, Norwegian genealogist lists his mother as Ragnhild Rolvsdohter. Brian Tompsett, UK genealogist lists his mother as Groa. I' ll have to check the HEIMSKRINGLA to see if he is listed there and whether his mother is named.
1 CONC  Many genealogists list his mother as Hiltrude/Raginhilde Hrolfsdottir.
1 CONT Some sources list his death in 910.
