0 @N6000000000269742753@ NOTE Kenneth II (died 995), king of Scotland (971-95), the son o f Malcolm I MacDonald. From the beginning of his reign, Kenneth waged war against the Saxons, particularly the earls of Northumbria, who occupied southern Scotland, and t
1 CONC he Scandinavian Vikings, who controlled Scotland north of the Spey River. Although his wars were not successful, Kenneth consolidated central Scotland into a strong kingdom.
