0 @N6000000003635716577@ NOTE [2992] COLVER31.TXT file
1 CONT
1 CONT "Bloodline ...", p 274, king of Scotland 971-95
1 CONT
1 CONT Microsoft Encarta. Copyright 1993
1 CONT Kenneth II (died 995), king of Scotland (971-95), the son of Malcolm I MacDonald (reigned 943-54). From the beginning of his reign, Kenneth waged war against the Saxons, particularly the earls of Northumbria, who occupied southern
1 CONC  Scotland, and the Scandinavian Vikings, who controlled Scotland north of the Spey River. Although his wars were not successful, Kenneth consolidated central Scotland into a strong kingdom.
0 @N6000000003949883494@ NOTE In 973 he acknowledged Edgar, King of England as his lord in return for recognition that he held Lothian, which he had seized from the Angles. In about 994, he broke his promise and invaded England. He was defeated and lost Lothia
1 CONC n again. He killed Culen (the prior king's brother in 977 and was himself killed in a blood feud by Culen's son, Constantine, who became the next king of Scotland
