0 @N6000000002187965540@ NOTE Glick/Foster Ancestry
1 CONT Entries: 121850    Updated: Mon Dec 29 21:49:25 2003    Contact: cherylvarner34c cherylvarner34c
1 CONT Index | Descendancy | Register | Pedigree | Ahnentafel | Download GEDCOM | Add Post-em
1 CONT # ID: I20096
1 CONT # Name: Sigtryg SIGTRYGSSON
1 CONT # Surname: Sigtrygsson
1 CONT # Given Name: Sigtryg
1 CONT # Sex: M
1 CONT # Birth: 0880 in Northumbria
1 CONT # Death: 0927
1 CONT # Reference Number: Minor,Newl
1 CONT # _UID: 168FDBA8520F7F45A742FCA6AED3199C0E4E
1 CONT # Note:
1 CONT
1 CONT     !Married King Athelstan's sister as part of a treaty between the two. In 926 he renounced his wife and gave up Christianity. Athelstan had vowed revenge when Sihtric was murdered or died. His sons Guthfric and Anlaf fled when 
1 CONC Athelstan led an army into Northumbria. Guthfric returned the next year in arms to claim the Northumbrian kingdom; but he was subdued by Athelstan, and, making his submission, was received in kindness. [Knight's Popular History of
1 CONC  England, Vol. 1, p. 146]
1 CONT
1 CONT     BURR, MINOR, NEWLIN LINES
1 CONT
1 CONT     !Son of Ivar; brother of Reginald, King of the Dhu-galls. In 917/18 he re-established the chieftainship of his family in Ireland, and became "King of the Danes" in Dublin. On the death of Reginald, his brother Godfrey became K
1 CONC ing of the Danes in Dublin, Sitric ceding to him their Irish possessions, and taking Northumbria as his portion. Sitric died, having a few months before married the sister of Athelstane; and the Saxon king at once seized the oppor
1 CONC tunity of annexing the province to the English kingdom. [The Bruces and the Cumyns, p. 495]
1 CONT
1 CONT     !Danish king of York. Married Princess Edith. [Chronicle of the Royal Family, p. 17]
1 CONT
1 CONT     Immersed for a while in Irish affairs, as the recoverer of Dublin and slayer of the high-king Njall. King of the Liffey Norsemen. Of the stirring progeny of Ragnar, so regarded himself as having claims on the Danish kingdom of
1 CONC  Northumbria (i.e. the Old English Deira). [A History of the Vikings, p. 235]
1 CONT
1 CONT     Grandson of Ivar; father of:
1 CONT     1. Olaf Cuaran, king of Dublin and York
1 CONT     2. Harald, king of Limerick
1 CONT     [Stewart Baldwin
1 CONT
1 CONT     Son of Sigtryg Halfdansson; m. Edgyth, Princess of England; father of:
1 CONT     1. Harald Sigtrygsson who m. Edgyth
1 CONT     2. Olaf Sigtrygsson, King of Dublin
1 CONT     [
1 CONT
1 CONT 1 2 3 4
1 CONT # Change Date: 19 Mar 2003 at 17:13:02
1 CONT
1 CONT Father: Sigtryg HALFDANSSON b: 0849 in Denmark
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage 1 Eadgyth, Princess of the ANGLO-SAXONS b: 0896 in Wessex,England
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Divorced: Y
1 CONT     * Married: BEF 0926
1 CONT
1 CONT Children
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Has Children Olaf or Amlaib Kvaran or Cuaran SITRICSON King of Dublin b: ABT 0900 in of Dublin,Ireland
1 CONT    2. Has No Children Anlaf the Dane b: ABT 0910 in ,,of Northumbria,England
1 CONT    3. Has Children Harald Aralt SITRICSON King of Limerick b: 0925 in Northumbria
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Sources:
