0 @N6000000000437077952@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> King Name Suffix:<NSFX> Ii, Of Scotland King of Scotland (1005–34). He acquired the throne after killing Kenneth III and defeating a Northumbrian army at Carham (c. 1016). He became the first king to reign over 
1 CONC territory roughly equivalent to modern Scotland . He tried to eliminate rivals to his grandson Duncan I , but Macbeth survived to challenge the succession.
