0 @N6000000001351708738@ NOTE Fought in battle in 1008 at Corham with Uchtred, son of Waltheof, Earl of Northumberland; overcame the Danes in 1017; published a code of laws.   In 1016 made his grandson Duncan King of Strathclyde and named him his successor.  D
1 CONC efeated Northumbrians at Carham on Tweed & conquered Lothian in 1005.  Controlled beyond old Alba of the Angles in the South East, and Britions in South West. Said to have married an Irishwoman from Ossory.  Killed by his kinsman.
