1 CONT There
1 CONT  was still no established boundary between Scotland and England.
0 @N6000000002244423334@ NOTE See message under Duncan I, his successor and grandson.
0 @N6000000002244367041@ NOTE conquered Lothian 1018. King of Alba, King of Strathclyde.
1 CONT      said to have married an Irishwoman from Ossory.
1 CONT      Killed by his kinsman.
1 CONT
1 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1 CONT  In 1018, under MacAlpin's descendant Malcolm II, the Angles were
1 CONT finally
1 CONT  defeated in this northerly part of Britain and Lothian came under
1 CONT Scottish rule.
1 CONT  In the same year, the British (Celtic) King of Strathclyde died
1 CONT leaving no heir;
1 CONT  his throne went to Malcolm's grandson Duncan. In 1034, Duncan became
1 CONT King
1 CONT  of a much-expanded Scotland that included Pict-land, Scotland, Lothian,
1 CONT  Cumbria and Strathclyde. It excluded large tracts in the north, the
1 CONT Shetlands,
1 CONT  Orkneys and the Western Isles, which were held by the Scandinavians.
1 CONT There
1 CONT  was still no established boundary between Scotland and England.
