1 CONT A Grandchild's Heritage URL:  http://www.reach.net/~roanne/macmurrough.html
1 CONT
1 CONT Generation No. 36-44
1 CONT
1 CONT 36 Crimthann Coscrach: his son; the 85th Monarch for 7 years. He was distinguished by that name because he behaved with such bravery at the head of his army, that he was victorious in every battle he fought; "Cosgrach" signifies "
1 CONC slaughter" and "bloodshed" He was slain by Rogerus, the son of Sithrig. 
1 CONT
1 CONT 37 Mogh-Art: his son. 
1 CONT
1 CONT 38 Art: his son. 
1 CONT
1 CONT 39 Allod (Olioll): his son. 
1 CONT
1 CONT 40 Nuadh Falaid: his son. 
1 CONT
1 CONT 41 Fearach Foghlas: his son. 
1 CONT
1 CONT 42 Olioll Glas: his son. 
1 CONT
1 CONT 43 Fiacha Fobrug: his son. 
1 CONT
1 CONT 44 Breassal Breac: his son. Had following sons between whom he divided his country: 
1 CONT
1 CONT      Lughaidh, who is described below. He was the ancestor of the Kings, nobility, and gentry of Leinster. He inherited all the territories on the north side of the river Barrow, from      Wicklow to Droghe
1 CONT
1 CONT      Conla. He was the ancestor of the Kings, nobility, and gentry of Ossory. He inherited the south part, from the Barrow to the sea 
1 CONT
1 CONT ===================================================================
