0 @N6000000001353915912@ NOTE Harald II EIRIKSSON, byname HARALD GRAYCLOAK, Norwegian HARALD GRÅFELL, Old Norse HARALD GRÁFELDR (b. c. 935--d. c. 970), Norwegian king who, along with his brothers, overthrew Haakon I about 961 and ruled oppressively until about
1 CONC  970. He is credited with establishing the first Christian missions in Norway.
1 CONT The son of Erik Bloodax, who was the half brother of Haakon I, Haraldtook refuge in Denmark following his father's death. Aided by his uncle, the Danish king Harald Bluetooth (Blåtand), Harald and his brothers launched raids again
1 CONC st Haakon I in Norway and killed him about 961.Harald ruled harshly, killing two of the kings in the Oslo region andHaakon, earl of Lade, and he aroused opposition with his prohibition of the public worship of pagan gods. He was k
1 CONC illed in battle about 970by the forces of Haakon (later Haakon the Great), son of the earl of Lade, with the connivance of Harald Bluetooth, some of whose Norwegianholdings had been appropriated by Harald. [Encyclopaedia Britannic
1 CONC a CD '97, HARALD II EIRIKSSON]
