0 @N6000000003949893056@ NOTE One summer a ship from Iceland carrying skins for sail arrived at Hardanger. There were a great number of people, but none would buy the skins. The steersman implored King Harold to help. Harold visited the ship and asked if the s
1 CONC teersman would make a gift of a gray pelt. The man agreed and soon all of Harald's men bought gray skins just like the one wore by Harald. In a few days so many people had come to buy skins that not half could be served. After tha
1 CONC t incident Harold was known as Harold Grafeld (Graypelt).
