1 CONT     murdered-The Survival of Scotland, Eric Linklater, p. 19
1 CONT     MALCOLM II, son of KENNETH II, was King of Strathclyde, 990-995; King of Scotland, 1005-1034; fought in battle in 1008 at Corham with Uchtred, son of Waltheof, Earl of Northumberland; overcame the
1 CONT     danes in 1017; published a code of laws - Royalty for
1 CONT     Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 121
1 CONT     King of Scots 25 March 1005 to 25 NOV 1034. Fought in battle in 1008 at Corham with Uchtred son of Waltheof,Earl of Northumberland. Overcame the Danes in 1017. Published a set of Laws. Murdered
1 CONT     1034.
1 CONT     - HAWKINS.GED
