0 @N6000000003796205448@ NOTE ==================================================================
1 CONT
1 CONT A Grandchild's Heritage URL:  http://www.reach.net/~roanne/macmurrough2.html
1 CONT
1 CONT Generation No. 2
1 CONT
1 CONT Cellach macCinaeda O'Cheinnselaig, King Ui Cheinnselaig died 947.
1 CONT 2nd son of Ceneth; was slain by the Ossorians in 945, at Athcliath (Dublin). 
1 CONT He had following sons: 
1 CONT Doncadh, King of Leinster for 6 years 
1 CONT Donal, who is described below[KFH] 
1 CONT
1 CONT ===================================================================
0 @N6000000003796205237@ NOTE ==================================================================
1 CONT
1 CONT A Grandchild's Heritage URL:  http://www.reach.net/~roanne/macmurrough2.html
1 CONT
1 CONT Generation No. 5
1 CONT
1 CONT Donnchad Máel na mBó, King Ui Cheinnselaig died 1006[1].
1 CONT Donoch Maol-na-mBo: was King of Leinster for 9 years.[KFH]
1 CONT
1 CONT He married (1) Aife ingen Gilla Patraic, daughter of Gilla Patraic and Echrad Carlusa. He married (2) Mael Maidne ingen Domnaill, daughter of Domnall macFaelain.
1 CONT
1 CONT Notes
1 CONT King of Munster
1 CONT
1 CONT Child of Donnchad na mBó and Aife Patraic is:
1 CONT Diarmait MacMáil na mBó, King of Ireland, died 7 February 1071/72.
1 CONT
1 CONT Child of Donnchad mBó and Mael Domnaill is:
1 CONT + 7 i. Domnall6 Remar macMáel na mBó, died 1041.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT ===================================================================
0 @N6000000001783295554@ NOTE Arnulph, younger son of Roger de Montgomery, did his homage for Dyved, and is said, by our author, to have erected a slender fortress with stakes and turf at Pembroke, in the reign of king Henry I., which, however, appears to have
1 CONC  been so strong as to have resisted the hostile attack of Cadwgan ap Bleddyn in 1092, and of several lords of North Wales, in 1094.
0 @N6000000002275761851@ NOTE see http://www.geneajourney.com/talvas.html
