0 @N6000000003796193625@ NOTE ==================================================================
1 CONT
1 CONT A Grandchild's Heritage URL:  http://www.reach.net/~roanne/macmurrough2.html
1 CONT
1 CONT Generation No. 9
1 CONT
1 CONT Diarmait macDonnchada MacMurchada, King of Leinster KFH LINK
1 CONT born 1110[8]
1 CONT died 1 May 1171 in Ferns[9]. 
1 CONT Dermod naNGhall: 2nd son of Donoch MacMorough; died 1171; was the 58th Christian King of Leinster.[KFH]
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Mor ingen Muirchertaig Ua Tauthail, daughter of Mouirchertach O'Toole and Cacht O'Morda.
1 CONT
1 CONT Notes
1 CONT It has often been suggested that Diarmait Mac Murchada (Dermot MacMurrough) earned the sobriquet "Diarmait na nGall" (Dermot of the Foreigners) from the fact that he entered a military alliance with, and gave his daughter Aífe in 
1 CONC marriage to, Richard de Clare (Strongbow), but it is more probable that the cognomen refers to the fact that he asserted control over the Hiberno-Norse kingdom of Dublin. Despite his negative posthumous reputation as the catalyst 
1 CONC for Norman rule in Ireland, Diarmait was roundly praised by contemporary accounts as a great patron of church reform, having endowed the Cistercian abbey of Baltinglass. This act moved St. Bernard of Clairvaux to write a letter of
1 CONC  commendation to Diarmait. 
1 CONT
1 CONT quote from Leinster History
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Children of Diarmait MacMurchada and Mor Ua Tauthail are:
1 CONT Aoife MacMurrough, Princess of Leinster, born Abt 1145 in Leinster, Ireland; died Aft 1186.
1 CONT 15 ii. Urlachan.
1 CONT 16 iii. Donall Kavanagh MacMurchada.
1 CONT 17 iv. Lawrence O'Toole (St.), Archbishop of Dublin.
1 CONT
1 CONT 13. Sadb ingen Mael Morda9 O'Domnail. She married Donncuan O'Toole, son of Gilla O'Toole.
1 CONT
1 CONT Child of Sadb O'Domnail and Donncuan O'Toole is:
1 CONT + 18 i. Gilla Comgaill10 O'Toole, died 1127.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT ===================================================================
0 @N6000000001783580646@ NOTE Mór Uí Thuathail
0 @N6000000003949830251@ NOTE The marriage of Diarmait Mac Murchada (Dermot MacMurrough) to Mor, daughter of Muircheartach Ua Tuathail (O'Toole)  Is well documented in the "Ban Shenchus", a contemporary twelfth century source which also verifies that she (and 
1 CONC not some other wife of Diarmait) was the mother of Eve of Leinster.  The "Ban Shenchus"   has been discussed on other occasions in this newsgroup, and is an indispensible source for anyone who wishes to study the marriages of the 
1 CONC early Irish royalty.  It was edited by Margaret Dobbs in Revue Celtique volumes 47 (1930) 282-339, 48 (1931) 163-234, and 49 (1932) 437-489, of which the last is an every-name index to the names in the other two parts.
0 @N6000000000337405516@ NOTE Source #1: Frederick Lewis Weis, "Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700), Seventh Edition, with additions and corrections by Walter Lee Sheppard, Jr., assisted by Davis Faris (Baltimore, MD:
1 CONC   Genealogical Publishing Co, 1995)
1 CONT
1 CONT daughter of Muirchertach Ua Tuathail (O'Toole) and sister of St. Laurence O'Toole
