0 @N6000000002187763508@ NOTE Iorwerth Drwyndwn
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Iorwerth ab Owain Gwynedd or Iorwerth Drwyndwn (1145-1174), meaning "the broken-nosed", was a legitimate son of Owain Gwynedd (the king of Gwynedd) and his first wife Gwladys ferch Llywarch. He married Marared ferch Madog. His son
1 CONC  Llywelyn ab Iorwerth eventually united the realm and became known as Llywelyn Fawr and is one of Wales's most famous monarchs. Iorwerth was killed in battle at a place called Pennant Mehangell during the wars deciding the success
1 CONC ion following the death of his father.
