1 CONT Sources: A. Roots 121E;RC 166; Norr, p60; Coe; Guizot; Pfafman; AF;
1 CONT Kraentzler 1156, 1194, 1443, 1453; Davis; Ashley.
1 CONT William Longsword (Longaspatha), second Duke of Normandy, 917-943, and Duke
1 CONT of Aquitaine. He captured Britanny, Cotentin, the Channel Islands and the
1 CONT Avranchin, annexing them to his kingdom. He was slain by Arnulf ofFlanders.
1 CONT RC: William I "Longsword," Duke of Normandy; murdered 17 Dec. 943
1 CONT in France.
1 CONT K: Guilaume I Longue Epee, Duke of Normandy.
1 CONT Roots: William I, "Longsword," born ca. 930, probably Rouen. Succeeded to
1 CONT Duchy of Normandy about 927. In about 930 the Bretons rebelled. He subdued
1 CONT them, taking Brittany, the Channel Islands, Contentin and the Averanchin.
1 CONT Killed in a treacherous ambush 17 Dec. 942 by servants of Theobald of Blois and
1 CONT Arnulf of Flanders.
1 CONT Norr: William Longsword (Guillaume Longue-espee); son of Poppa; 2nd duke,
1 CONT 927-942; murdered.
1 CONT Ashley: William "Longsword", Count of Normandy.
1 CONT Davis: William I Longsword, ruled Normandy 931-942 [Chancellor.FTW]
1 CONT
