1 CONC nd duke of Normandy, even if this title did not exist at the time.
1 CONT
1 CONT Little is known about his early years. He was born in Bayeux or Rouen. His parents were Rollo and Poppa. All that is known of Poppa is that she was a Christian, and the daughter to Berengar of Rennes, the previous lord of what (Br
1 CONC ittania Nova) became Normandy. According to the Planctus, he was baptized a Christian.
1 CONT
1 CONT William succeeded Rollo sometime around 928. It appears that he faced a rebellion early in his reign, from Normans who felt he had become too Frankified. The following years are obscure. In 939 William became involved in a war wit
1 CONC h Arnulf I of Flanders, which soon became intertwined with the other conflicts of the reign of Louis IV of France. He was killed by followers of Arnulf while at a meeting to settle their conflict. His son Richard I of Normandy suc
1 CONC ceeded him.
