0 @N6000000004303398309@ NOTE Guillaume (William) "Longsword" Duke NORMANDY (876-942)
0 @N6000000005076794061@ NOTE Guillaume I 'Longsword', 2nd Duc de Normandie was born circa 900 at Normandy, France.3 He was the son of Rollo Ragnvaldsson, 1st Duc de Normandie and Poppa of Normandy de Valois.2 He married Sprota (?) circa 932 in a Normandy marr
1 CONC iage.3 He married Luitgarda de Vermandois, daughter of Heribert II, Comte de Vermandois and Liégarde de France, in 935.2 He died on 17 December 942 at Normandy, France, murdered.3
1 CONT      Guillaume I 'Longsword', 2nd Duc de Normandie succeeded to the title of 2nd Duc de Normandie in 925.1
1 CONT Children of Guillaume I 'Longsword', 2nd Duc de Normandie and Sprota (?)
1 CONT Raoul d'Ivry+ 2
1 CONT Richard I, 3rd Duc de Normandie+ b. 28 Aug 933, d. 20 Nov 9961
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 86. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World.
1 CONT [S106] Royal Genealogies Website (ROYAL92.GED), online ftp://ftp.cac.psu.edu/genealogy/public_html/royal/index.html. Hereinafter cited as Royal Genealogies Website.
1 CONT [S125] Richard Glanville-Brown, online <e-mail address>, Richard Glanville-Brown (RR 2, Milton, Ontario, Canada), downloaded 17 August 2005.
