1 CONT !Per "My Boone Family":  Ivar, Jarl of the Uplands, with a band of his followers crossed into Sweden where he set up a base for Viking raids and established his own clan under the insignia of "the bear" (bjorn).  Norse "Vik" (to g
1 CONC o sailing) hence Vikings: sailors.  Norse o is pronounced "oo" as in Boone.
1 CONT Norse "Jarl": the "j" is pronounced "y"; the Norse "Yarl" is the root of the English title "Earl".
