0 @N6000000003615380921@ NOTE Killed by MacBeth, Who Succeeded him.
1 CONT
1 CONT Macbeth killed his wife's cousin Duncan I and seized the throne of Scotland, remaining as King of Scotland for several years. Duncan's son Malcolm killed Macbeth and became King of Scotland the following year. Macbeth's step-son, 
1 CONC his wife's child by a first marriage, was king from 1057 to 1058, when Malcolm took the throne back, becoming Malcolm III. 
1 CONT
1 CONT ALIA: Duncan 'the Gracious' // I 
1 CONT Title: King 
1 CONT Birth: 1007 in of Atholl, Perthshire, Scotland 1 
1 CONT Death: 14 AUG 1040 in Iona, near Elgin, Scotland (killed By Macbeth) 2 
1 CONT Event: Note 1 25 NOV 1034 Ascended to the throne 
1 CONT Event: Note 2 BET. 1034 - 1040 King of Scotland 
1 CONT Event: Note 3 14 AUG 1040 Slain by Macbeth 3 
1 CONT Event: AKA (Facts Page) Duncan 'the Gracious', King of Scotland Reference Number: IND1397 
1 CONT Note: Duncan I. (Maldred), King of Scotland, was slain by his cousin, Macbeth, local chief of Moray in 1041. One source puts his death on August 14, 1040.
1 CONT
