1 CONT Accor ding to the med ieval historian , Snor ri Sturlu son, Fin n lived
1 CONT for
1 CONT a
1 CONT time at Austrat t in the district of Yr jar i nwestern Norway. He had
1 CONT b een
1 CONT on several v iking expedition s . He was a well-liked stew a rd of King
1 CONT H arald Sigurtharson i n Norway. The k ing had F innintercede for hi m
1 CONT and
1 CONT m ake reco nciliation wit h his enemies who were ang er ed about some s la
1 CONT yings . In on e reconciliatio n att empt, an enemy by the n a m e of Hkon
1 CONT agre ed t o be reconci led to the king if he was giv en Ragnhi ld , a
1 CONT relative
1 CONT of t he king , in marri age. The kin g agree d, but said, "Neith er you
1 CONT nor
1 CONT any else will fin d i t adv isabl e to obtain Ragn hild in marriag e unle
1 CONT ss
1 CONT it
1 CONT be wi t h her own con sent." R agnhild did not wan t tomarry a ma n wh o
1 CONT wa
1 CONT s
1 CONT no t of p rincely rank. The ki ng would have grantedth e title of e arl
1 CONT to
1 CONT Hk on , but th ere was a long-st a nding prac tice of havin g just one e
1 CONT arl
1 CONT at
1 CONT a time , and he did not wan t to t ake the titleaway from the cur rent
1 CONT Earl
1 CONT Or m. (Lat e r after Earl Orm d ied , Hk on was given the titl e and Ragn
1 CONT hil
1 CONT d
1 CONT married him.) Some other eve nts a nd the death of Finn's b roth e r caus
1 CONT ed
1 CONT Finn to be so ange r ed at t he king tha t he lef t Norway. He joined w
1 CONT ith
1 CONT King Svein in Denmark, and was giv en the t itle of earl and ruled the
1 CONT pro vi nce of Halland, whe re he was i n charge of de fense ag ainst the
1 CONT Norwe gians .[geddown.ged]
