0 @N6000000001353915961@ NOTE Called "Mikillati" (the magnificent), King of Vestfold and Roumarike;ruled in Norway and in Denmark; probably the "Godfrey the Proud" (andso identified by Moncreiffe, I. 1982) of the Franks who opposed the Emperor Charlemagne. [Ro
1 CONC derick W. Stuart, Royalty for Commoners, 3rd ed., Genealogical Publishing Company, Baltimore MD, 1998]
1 CONT Sources: A. Roots 243A; RC 166, 204; Kraentzler 1609; AF.
1 CONT Roots: Gudrod, "the Magnificent," also called "the Hunting-King," sonof
1 CONT Halfdan "White-Leg" and Asa, according to Moriarty, but Sturleson says
1 CONT great-grandson of Halfdan "White-Leg. Gudrod was King of Vermaland, Vestfold
1 CONT and Vingulmark and was murdered 810-827 at the instigation of (2) wife Asa in
1 CONT revenge for forcibly abducting her and killing, about 800, her fatherand
1 CONT brother. Married (1) Alfhilde, daughter of Alfrim, rulter of Vingulmark;
1 CONT married (2) Asa, daughter of Harald, "Redbeard," King of Agdir.
1 CONT RC: "Mikillati" (the magnificent). King of Vestfold and Roumarike. Ruled in
1 CONT Norway and in Denmark. Probably the "Godfrey the Proud" of the Frankswho
1 CONT opposed Charlemagne. Killed 810.
1 CONT K: Gudrod Halfdansson.
1 CONT RC Note: Moncreiffe adds two generations between Gudrod and Halfdan
1 CONT Olafsson. He says Gudrod's father was Halfdan "the Stingy," King of Vestfold.
1 CONT And he calls Gudrod Godfrey and Proud. Halfdan's father, he says, wasEystein
1 CONT "the Fart," King of Roumarike. "Though the work carries no bibliography,
1 CONT Moncreiffe was an outstanding authority, and pending proof otherwise,may well
1 CONT be considered correct."
