0 @N6000000002319315198@ NOTE Gudrod  (King of Vestfold)
1 CONT
1 CONT      BIRTH: ABT. 738, Vestfold, Norway
1 CONT      DEATH: 810
0 @N6000000004287328342@ NOTE Sources: A. Roots 243A; RC 166, 204; Kraentzler 1609; AF. Roots: Gudrod, "the Magnificent," also called "the Hunting-King," son of Halfdan and Asa, according to Moriarty, but Sturleson says great-grandson of Halfdan "White-Leg. Gu
1 CONC drod was King of Vermaland, Vestfold and Vingulmark and was murdered 810-827 at the instigation of (2) wife Asa in revenge for forcibly abducting her and killing, about 800, her father and brother. Married (1) Alfhilde, daughter o
1 CONC f Alfrim, rulter of Vingulmark; married (2) Asa, daughter of Harald, "Redbeard," King of Agdir. RC: "Mikillati" (the magnificent). King of Vestfold and Roumarike. Ruled in Norway and in Denmark. Probably the "Godfrey the Proud" of
1 CONC  the Franks who  opposed Charlemagne. Killed 810. K: Gudrod Halfdansson.  RC Note: Moncreiffe adds two generations between Gudrod and Halfdan  Olafsson. He says Gudrod's father was Halfdan "the Stingy," King of Vestfold. And he ca
1 CONC lls Gudrod Godfrey and Proud. Halfdan's father, he says, was Eystein "the Fart," King of Roumarike. "Though the work carries no bibliography,  Moncreiffe was an outstanding authority, and pending proof otherwise, may well be consi
1 CONC dered correct." Gudrod Halfdansson "Mikillati" (the magnificent), King of Vestfold & Roumarike ; ruled in Norway and in Denmark; probably the "Godfrey the Proud" (and so identified by Moncreiffe) of the Franks who opposed the Empe
1 CONC ror Charlemagne;
0 @N6000000005758036718@ NOTE REF RFC. King of Vestfold and Roumarike. Ruled in Norway and Denmark.         Probably "Godfrey the Proud" of the Franks who opposed the         Emperor Charlemagne.      b. ABT 738, Vestfold, Norway      d. 810    Married Asa (74
1 CONC 3-)     Children:     Olaf II Gudrodsson (770-)   Halfdan "the Black" King of Vestfold (-860) m. Ragnhild
